61,"login":"freben","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTc0NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nttdevopscc/backstage/commits/71da72d1a695042be1572c40112fab9abeee7d16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-09T13:11:25Z","email":"freben@spotify.com","name":"Fredrik Adelöw"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-09T14:35:06Z","email":"freben@spotify.com","name":"Fredrik Adelöw"},"message":"Fix flaky createBarrier test by using fake timers\n\nThe ''abandons a wait after the timeout expires'' test relied on real\nsetTimeout calls with tight margins (~50ms) between barrier timeouts\nand tick delays. On loaded CI machines, timer coalescing could cause\nboth to fire in the same event loop turn, making the test flaky.\n\nSwitched all createBarrier tests to jest.useFakeTimers() with\nadvanceTimersByTime() for deterministic timer control, removing\nthe real-timer tick helper entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Fredrik Adelöw <freben@spotify.com>\nMade-with: Cursor","tree":{"sha":"a9747793b0192b8b09eb5f35a6d04053b7fcf650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nttdevopscc/backstage/git/trees/a9747793b0192b8b09eb5f35a6d04053b7fcf650"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nttdevopscc/backstage/git/commits/71da72d1a695042be1572c40112fab9abeee7d16","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3097461?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freben/e