3.5 carries a critical remote code execution in\nnext/og ImageResponse, and the gate''s npm audit (--audit-level=high) now\nfails every pull request on it. The pin moves to 16.3.8, the first release\npast the advisory''s range on this line, and `npm audit fix` takes\nbaseline-browser-mapping past GHSA-w5vr-8v7q-w6rv (moderate). Lock-only\nchange; npm audit reports no vulnerabilities.","tree":{"sha":"3c31f210423792f484be7323808fbf57b2837e44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/3c31f210423792f484be7323808fbf57b2837e44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/afbc8097ae747e3749a760a5c09dab947fa5bf54","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/afbc8097ae747e3749a760a5c09dab947fa5bf54","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKGFmYmM4MDk3YWU3NDdlMzc0OWE3NjBhNWMwOWRhYjk0N2ZhNWJmNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/05ab2c0bd5a317d06e153ead1248ed00eea64866","sha":"05ab2c0bd5a317d06e153ead1248ed00eea64866","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/05ab2c0bd5a317d06e153ead1248ed00eea64866"}],"sha":"afbc8097ae747e3749a760a5c09dab947fa5bf54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/afbc8097ae747e3749a760a5c09dab947fa5bf54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/05ab2c0bd5a317d06e153ead1248ed00eea64866/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:41:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:53:55Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump hex-service-kit to v0.0.11: trace only through the collector\n\nDecision D1: build_tracer refuses an unset OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT instead of\nexporting straight to Cloud Trace around the collector''s GenAI-content redaction, and\ntakes no project argument any more.\n\n- pyproject.toml and the locks: hex-service-kit v0.0.11 (ec2d724). The only other lock\n  movement is opentelemetry-exporter-gcp-trace and its dependencies leaving with the\n  kit''s otel extra, where this repo resolved it.\n- adapters/gcp/tracer.py: build_tracer(service=...) only.\n- tests/contract: the managed tracer''s documented refusal is now\n  CollectorEndpointRequiredError; on-prem keys off a new onprem_refuses field; a new\n  test keeps the old guarantee that with a collector configured and no SDK a span\n  degrades to a no-op.\n- settings, config, Terraform variable and adoption notes stop describing a direct\n  Cloud Trace path that no longer exists.\n\nRelocked without --upgrade: fleet-deps bump-commons'' --upgrade relock moved 0\nunrelated pins here, and those were reverted.","tree":{"sha":"3c5b590dae3dfabc12cdd47119219db2a6ef05ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/3c5b590dae3dfabc12cdd47119219db2a6ef05ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/05ab2c0bd5a317d06e153ead1248ed00eea64866","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/05ab2c0bd5a317d06e153ead1248ed00eea64866","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKDA1YWIyYzBiZDVhMzE3ZDA2ZTE1M2VhZDEyNDhlZDAwZWVhNjQ4NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/0635f7926817178939ea12d7c96e0a207c583b96","sha":"0635f7926817178939ea12d7c96e0a207c583b96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/0635f7926817178939ea12d7c96e0a207c583b96"}],"sha":"05ab2c0bd5a317d06e153ead1248ed00eea64866","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/05ab2c0bd5a317d06e153ead1248ed00eea64866"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/0635f7926817178939ea12d7c96e0a207c583b96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:37:19Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:39:55Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Screen every generation call through a fail-closed guardrail port (rule R1)\n\nPhase P3 of the guardrail/registry/observability plan, adopting the fixed\ndesign from hex-service-template (ab3284e).\n\n- ports/guardrail.py, adapters/{local,gcp,onprem}/guardrail.py: the\n  GuardrailPort with the template''s adapters. The Model Armor adapter\n  allows ONLY on filter_match_state NO_MATCH_FOUND with invocation_result\n  SUCCESS, read by enum .name (str() of the proto-plus IntEnum is its\n  number, so the old substring test never blocked), carries a per-call\n  deadline (model_armor.timeout_seconds) and takes an injectable client.\n  The local heuristic is word-bounded and matches DAN case-sensitively.\n- domain/response_pack_service.py: all three generation calls\n  (classification, item and cover-note narration, fact normalisation) go\n  through _generate_screened: INPUT on the prompt as sent (it carries\n  every caller-controlled field), OUTPUT on the answer before it is\n  parsed; each sanitized_text is used exactly as given. A refusal, or a\n  guardrail that raises, is now audited Decision.BLOCKED (no severity,\n  never the refused text) before the call site degrades; the refusal was\n  previously swallowed with no record. Narration is optional by design\n  here, so a refused call drops the model''s contribution whole (fixed\n  fallback paragraph with an ungrounded_draft blocker, no suggestion, no\n  facts). An audit sink that refuses the BLOCKED record fails the request\n  instead of degrading. propose_topic takes the actor.\n- domain/kernel.py: Decision.BLOCKED, GuardrailVerdict refuses\n  allowed-without-text and blocked-with-text, AuditEvent.severity is\n  optional for BLOCKED records.\n- config.py, adapters/controls.py, settings.yaml: EXAMRFI_GUARDRAIL\n  (three-state), ModelArmorSettings with a validated timeout_seconds, a\n  boot refusal when on under gcp with no template named.\n- pyproject.toml, requirements-gcp.lock: google-cloud-modelarmor in the\n  gcp extra (0.7.1), so the image carries it and lint-gcp checks it.\n- infra/terraform: model_armor.tf gated on model_armor_full_capabilities\n  with template_metadata and ignore_partial_invocation_failures = false,\n  roles/modelarmor.user, the API, the VPC-SC entry, the guardrail_enabled\n  switch on the edge, the reserved env name, and a guardrail_blocks\n  alert on BLOCKED audit records. The google-beta provider, its lock\n  entry and its tftest mock were already in place.\n- eval/run_eval.py: the grounding score screens its direct generation\n  call the same way; scripts/demo.py: a guardrail row in EXIT_CALLS.\n- tests: guardrail screening (switch states, boot refusal, heuristic\n  tables, every call screened in order on the text sent, BLOCKED audits,\n  fail-closed and unauditable-refusal cases), the SDK-free verdict mirror,\n  and the real-enum mapping test (skips without the SDK unless\n  EXAMRFI_REQUIRE_MODEL_ARMOR_SDK=1).\n- Docs: COMPLIANCE R1, SPEC, ARCHITECTURE, runbook, model card,\n  onprem-migration, ADOPTING, practices-audit and the FAQs no longer say\n  the guardrail is unbound.","tree":{"sha":"87708eab97354539ab5c7f761c05b0e7a16b8d84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/87708eab97354539ab5c7f761c05b0e7a16b8d84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/0635f7926817178939ea12d7c96e0a207c583b96","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https