/git/commits/8fd68f2cbb63c7ea5ce82ddaaafd0ac0423fc5c4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/8fd68f2cbb63c7ea5ce82ddaaafd0ac0423fc5c4","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKDhmZDY4ZjJjYmI2M2M3ZWE1Y2U4MmRkYWFhZmQwYWMwNDIzZmM1YzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/f4b97553ecaa128966a8f6b89f53db026577a376","sha":"f4b97553ecaa128966a8f6b89f53db026577a376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/f4b97553ecaa128966a8f6b89f53db026577a376"}],"sha":"8fd68f2cbb63c7ea5ce82ddaaafd0ac0423fc5c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/8fd68f2cbb63c7ea5ce82ddaaafd0ac0423fc5c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/f4b97553ecaa128966a8f6b89f53db026577a376/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T08:44:26Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:11:50Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Make customer-managed encryption optional, and off by default\n\nEvery binding to the stack''s Cloud KMS key now sits behind cmek_enabled,\ndefault false: the key ring, the key, every grant to a service agent, and\nevery store, log bucket, registry and revision that took the key. Block\nbindings became dynamic blocks; scalar bindings read the key through one(),\nwhich is null when the key does not exist and omits the attribute rather\nthan pointing it at nothing. The Terraform tests that assert on key material\nturn the gate on to keep meaning what they meant.\n\nWhy the default is off: a key ring can never be deleted, a log bucket that\nhas CMEK can never drop it, and registries and document stores take their\nkey at creation. None of that changes an answer or a screen, and everything\nis encrypted at rest with Google-managed keys regardless. A deployment with\na customer whose data it must shred, whose key access must be audited or\nwhose keys must live in an HSM sets it true in its own tfvars BEFORE the\nfirst apply. Where a stack already applied it, the key''s prevent_destroy\nrefuses a plan that omits the line, which is the right answer: the stores it\nbound stay bound.\n\nThe vendored deploy-and-residency-hardening skill says the same.","tree":{"sha":"671b6526a4e9473134571905035881dd5519a527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/671b6526a4e9473134571905035881dd5519a527"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/f4b97553ecaa128966a8f6b89f53db026577a376","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/f4b97553ecaa128966a8f6b89f53db026577a376","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKGY0Yjk3NTUzZWNhYTEyODk2NmE4ZjZiODlmNTNkYjAyNjU3N2EzNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/9fcf06410854564f2b446475396e0e7606b85f68","sha":"9fcf06410854564f2b446475396e0e7606b85f68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/9fcf06410854564f2b446475396e0e7606b85f68"}],"sha":"f4b97553ecaa128966a8f6b89f53db026577a376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/f4b97553ecaa128966a8f6b89f53db026577a376"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/9fcf06410854564f2b446475396e0e7606b85f68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:17:41Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:30:33Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Resync the embeddable-UI skill: both assertion header names\n\nThe canonical skill told the next repository to verify \"the injected\n`x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion`\" and nothing else, which is the instruction that\nproduced the defect this branch fixes. Fixed at the source in org-metadata and\nvendored here.\n\nOnly this one skill is resynced rather than the whole set, because\ndeploy-and-residency-hardening is in flight on another branch and a blanket\n`sync-skills.sh` would pull that unmerged work in with it.","tree":{"sha":"43eabcfdfd51beea67095ebf3cb707d152884c39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/43eabcfdfd51beea67095ebf3cb707d152884c39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/9fcf06410854564f2b446475396e0e7606b85f68","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/9fcf06410854564f2b446475396e0e7606b85f68","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKDlmY2YwNjQxMDg1NDU2NGYyYjQ0NjQ3NTM5NmUwZTc2MDZiODVmNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/b4b201309bfaefbdcf8b38a3030ce05ccf1163bd","sha":"b4b201309bfaefbdcf8b38a3030ce05ccf1163bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/b4b201309bfaefbdcf8b38a3030ce05ccf1163bd"}],"sha":"9fcf06410854564f2b446475396e0e7606b85f68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/9fcf06410854564f2b446475396e0e7606b85f68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/b4b201309bfaefbdcf8b38a3030ce05ccf1163bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:03:16Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:30:33Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Read the IAP assertion under both names a request can carry it\n\n`x-goog-*` is Google''s reserved namespace and the serverless frontend strips\nthat whole namespace from a request entering a service, so an embedding host\nbehind IAP cannot forward the assertion its own edge was handed under the\nstandard name. It sends the same value as `x-portal-iap-assertion` as well,\nand this adapter read only the reserved one.\n\nSo this service would have answered 401 to EVERY authenticated caller the day\nit was embedded, and said \"request did not pass through IAP\" about a request\nthat passed through IAP one hop earlier. Nothing would have reported it: the\ngate is green, a console''s first calls need no identity at all, and the unit\nsuite builds its own request, so it could only ever choose the header the\nauthor had in mind.\n\nThe read is now the commons selection function, which examines both names,\nprefers the edge-injected one for diagnosis rather than for trust, strips so a\nheader a proxy rendered blank is absent rather than malformed, and names both\nheaders in its refusal so an operator reads which hop dropped one.\n\ntests/unit/test_embedded_assertion_transport.py is the standing proof, and it\nwas falsified first: with only the header read reverted, five of its cases\nfail, including the one that resolves the contradiction between a passing\nclaim suite and a live 401.","tree":{"sha":"fe3aaca53ff9f47283e3096e27596f52f66f3e71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/fe3aaca53ff9f47283e3096e27596f52f66f3e71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/b4b201309bfaefbdcf8b38a3030ce05ccf1163bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/b4b201309bfaefbdcf8b38a3030ce05ccf1163bd","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKGI0YjIwMTMwOWJmYWVmYmRjZjhiMzhhMzAzMGNlMDVjY2YxMTYzYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/4b1975a9a7337ee5eb5645a7c238b47c7accd81e","sha":"4b1975a9a7337ee5eb5645a7c238b47c7accd81e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/4b1975a9a7337ee5eb5645a7c238b47c7accd81e"}],"sha":"b4b201309bfaefbdcf8b38a3030ce05ccf1163bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/b4b201309bfaefbdcf8b38a3030ce05ccf1163bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/4b1975a9a7337ee5eb5645a7c238b47c7accd81e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:40:43Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:49:12Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Gate the posture alerts, and stop copying every audit log into this bucket\n\nTwo changes the deployed stacks already carry, brought to the rest of the\nfleet so a fork does not inherit either on its first apply.\n\nThe posture alert policies and the log-based metrics behind them now sit\nbehind posture_alerts_enabled, default false. Cloud Monitoring bills every\nmetric-based alert condition, and a deployment with nobody on call buys\nnothing with them; the signals still land in Cloud Logging, where an operator\ncan read them.\n\nThe audit sink routes only this application''s own ledger into its bucket. It\nused to copy every Cloud Audit Log entry as well, which is a second\nCMEK-encrypted ingestion of what _Default already keeps for thirty days.\n\nNothing here is applied anywhere, so neither change moves a live resource.\nWhat they remove is the trap a fork inherits the day it applies.","tree":{"sha":"7268006be6a799d93baabbfd8e98fdd9063ac0e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/7268006be6a799d93baabbfd8e98fdd9063ac0e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/4b1975a9a7337ee5eb5645a7c238b47c7accd81e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/4b1975a9a7337ee5eb5645a7c238b47c7accd81e","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKDRiMTk3NWE5YTczMzdlZTVlYjU2NDVhN2MyMzhiNDdjN2FjY2Q4MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/cc93d84fc33d15b6b7d5d1b81935e1c6a10395e9","sha":"cc93d84fc33d15b6b7d5d1b81935e1c6a10395e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/cc93d84fc33d15b6b7d5d1b81935e1c6a10395e9"}],"sha":"4b1975a9a7337ee5eb5645a7c238b47c7accd81e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/4b1975a9a7337ee5eb5645a7c238b47c7accd81e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/cc93d84fc33d15b6b7d5d1b81935e1c6a10395e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:05:06Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:13:30Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Vendor the reduced required-artifact set\n\nThe portfolio gate stopped requiring `docs/practices-audit.md`,\n`docs/onprem-migration.md` and a fleet-wide `COMPLIANCE.md` on 2026-09-13, and the\ncanonical skills README was updated to match. This is the vendored copy following, so\nthe convention this repository carries is the one actually in force.\n\nThe scorecard shipped PRE-FILLED from a template render, so requiring it fleet-wide\nmeant every repository asserting a per-check verdict nobody had reached. The exit guide\ndocumented a migration for a profile that is a deliberate fail-fast placeholder. The\nprinciple-to-control mapping is now a launch-set expectation, because it is what a\nbuyer is shown.\n\nRetiring a requirement does not delete a file this repository already has. Nothing is\nremoved here; only the statement of what is required changes.\n\nVendored by `sync-skills.sh` from the canonical copy in org-metadata, never edited in\nplace, so the drift check stays green.","tree":{"sha":"e280e5a24cc7b7734c5f110c45068d88957cadcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/e280e5a24cc7b7734c5f110c45068d88957cadcd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/cc93d84fc33d15b6b7d5d1b81935e1c6a10395e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/cc93d84fc33d15b6b7d5d1b81935e1c6a10395e9","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKGNjOTNkODRmYzMzZDE1YjZiN2Q1ZDFiODE5MzVlMWM2YTEwMzk1ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/4bddec938be7be216f9df0275f4563b2a3ff0b1e","sha":"4bddec938be7be216f9df0275f4563b2a3ff0b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/4bddec938be7be216f9df0275f4563b2a3ff0b1e"}],"sha":"cc93d84fc33d15b6b7d5d1b81935e1c6a10395e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/cc93d84fc33d15b6b7d5d1b81935e1c6a10395e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/4bddec938be7be216f9df0275f4563b2a3ff0b1e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:27:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:48:22Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Gate the project audit config, and default it off\n\n`google_project_iam_audit_config` is AUTHORITATIVE for the service it names, so a\nstack declaring `allServices` does not add to the project''s audit configuration,\nit REPLACES it. Forty-eight stacks in this fleet declared it unconditionally and\nfour gated it, which is the collision the posture record already documents as the\nreason those four decline: a stack asking for DATA_READ and DATA_WRITE removes an\nADMIN_READ a sibling enabled, and Terraform reports it as a create rather than a\nchange, because the stack holds no prior state for a resource that is already live.\n\nThis stack now carries `manage_audit_config`, defaulted false. A deployment that\nwants data-access logging names it in its own tfvars, in exactly one stack per\nproject. Data-access logs are also the highest-volume class Cloud Logging ingests,\nand nothing in the reference deployment reads them.\n\nVerified: terraform fmt is clean and terraform validate passes on every touched\ntree; the three Terraform test suites asserting plan-level refusals pass.","tree":{"sha":"7dc14d22727d54fb750231121cb65899eb5b5ef0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/7dc14d22727d54fb750231121cb65899eb5b5ef0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/4bddec938be7be216f9df0275f4563b2a3ff0b1e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/4bddec938be7be216f9df0275f4563b2a3ff0b1e","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKDRiZGRlYzkzOGJlN2JlMjE2ZjlkZjAyNzVmNDU2M2IyYTNmZjBiMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/a93d17d4ce5acb268ba2eb44ea1c7ca083618494","sha":"a93d17d4ce5acb268ba2eb44ea1c7ca083618494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/a93d17d4ce5acb268ba2eb44ea1c7ca083618494"}],"sha":"4bddec938be7be216f9df0275f4563b2a3ff0b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/4bddec938be7be216f9df0275f4563b2a3ff0b1e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/a93d17d4ce5acb268ba2eb44ea1c7ca083618494/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:07:40Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:17:34Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.8","tree":{"sha":"6121ff7c92920241848c111e867b65183978d0c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/6121ff7c92920241848c111e867b65183978d0c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/a93d17d4ce5acb268ba2eb44ea1c7ca083618494","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/a93d17d4ce5acb268ba2eb44ea1c7ca083618494","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKGE5M2QxN2Q0Y2U1YWNiMjY4YmEyZWI0NGVhMWM3Y2EwODM2MTg0OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/55c52c22873ee130c741127d1aa7ca201a91ebd2","sha":"55c52c22873ee130c741127d1aa7ca201a91ebd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/55c52c22873ee130c741127d1aa7ca201a91ebd2"}],"sha":"a93d17d4ce5acb268ba2eb44ea1c7ca083618494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/a93d17d4ce5acb268ba2eb44ea1c7ca083618494"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/55c52c22873ee130c741127d1aa7ca201a91ebd2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:31:09Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:38:00Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Every bar this corpus cannot express is 1.0 now, and says so\n\nA threshold t tolerates a single failure only over at least 1/(1-t) scored\ndecisions. Every bar raised here is scored 0/1 once per case over a corpus far\nshort of that, so each one already required a perfect run while reading as though\nit priced one failure in. 0.99 was not a looser bar than 1.00 over these corpora.\nIt was the same bar with a friendlier face, which is worse than either: a\nreviewer reads it as headroom that does not exist.\n\nEach rubric now carries the arithmetic beside the number: how many decisions the\nmetric scores, what a single failure would give, and how many cases it would take\nbefore a bar below 1.0 meant anything. The last line is the useful one, because\nit says the number to move first is the corpus and not the bar.\n\nFor the safety family it is also what the property means. A leak gate that is\nright 99% of the time is a gate with a hole in it, and there is no acceptable\nlevel of one unredacted identifier reaching an audit record.\n\nFound by org-metadata''s new eval-governance check, which reads every launch-set\nrepository''s rubrics against the promotion authority and could see what no single\nrepository can see about itself.","tree":{"sha":"b6b041480e979522cfd89cee595bedcc5f2880e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/b6b041480e979522cfd89cee595bedcc5f2880e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/55c52c22873ee130c741127d1aa7ca201a91ebd2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/55c52c22873ee130c741127d1aa7ca201a91ebd2","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKDU1YzUyYzIyODczZWUxMzBjNzQxMTI3ZDFhYTdjYTIwMWE5MWViZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/39881106e5c56ea2304f526ee68e905784d76b37","sha":"39881106e5c56ea2304f526ee68e905784d76b37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/39881106e5c56ea2304f526ee68e905784d76b37"}],"sha":"55c52c22873ee130c741127d1aa7ca201a91ebd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/55c52c22873ee130c741127d1aa7ca201a91ebd2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/39881106e5c56ea2304f526ee68e905784d76b37/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:42:21Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:18:41Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Judge the paragraph, not only whether it cited what it was given\n\nEight metrics here and every one is deterministic. The closest thing to a\nquality measure is `citation_grounding`, and it is a PREDICATE: a paragraph\npasses by citing only exhibits it was given and writing only numbers it was\nhanded. That is a floor on honesty. It is not a floor on usefulness, and the two\nare not the same thing.\n\nA regulator reads this paragraph, with the firm''s name on it, inside a statutory\nclock. It can be perfectly grounded and still fail to say which item it answers,\nhedge the completeness figure until it means nothing, omit the deadline the\nexaminer is counting, or promise a document the firm never agreed to produce.\n\n`eval/run_narrative_eval.py` judges six paragraphs drawn from the golden cases,\neach written once per profile, banded against `config/quality-floors.toml`. The\nfloor is 0.70 and the target 0.90, higher than a marketing vertical''s because\nthe audience is a regulator and the cost of a hedged answer is a follow-up\nrequest against a shorter deadline, not a weaker click-through. It is not 1.0\nbecause a paragraph missing one secondary exhibit reference is worse than one\nthat names it and is not a paragraph that must never be sent.\n\nThe four defects in the `regressed` column are the argument for the whole thing,\nand they are specific rather than generic badness. Each is a sentence somebody\nwould write to be helpful, each would pass a grounding predicate reading it in\nisolation, and each is worse than saying nothing:\n\n  a breach reported as a deadline, \"produced within the agreed timetable, due 10\n  March 2027\", on the one item whose deadline passed on 10 March;\n\n  an access gap reported as an absence, \"we are unable to locate one further\n  record and no such record is held\", where the firm holds it and the preparer is\n  not entitled to it;\n\n  withheld material reported as nothing withheld, with the withheld legal\n  analysis then summarised anyway in the next sentence;\n\n  stale evidence reported as current, on the one item held precisely because its\n  evidence predates the period it is offered for.\n\nSubjects, item references, completeness figures and deadlines all come from\n`golden_cases.jsonl`, so the criteria are about paragraphs this service actually\nproduces rather than paragraphs invented for a judge. The `reduced` column is a\nthinner paragraph rather than a wrong one and is expected DEGRADED, so a profile\nthat quietly got better fails too: a band nobody predicted is a change nobody\nreviewed.\n\n`make gate` gains `eval-narrative`.","tree":{"sha":"cf7bb78afb93021836a610100ea33a7c9645ecb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/cf7bb78afb93021836a610100ea33a7c9645ecb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/39881106e5c56ea2304f526ee68e905784d76b37","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/39881106e5c56ea2304f526ee68e905784d76b37","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKDM5ODgxMTA2ZTVjNTZlYTIzMDRmNTI2ZWU2OGU5MDU3ODRkNzZiMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/a094211afcd5fe1ab0ab28704231b407a4c9e862","sha":"a094211afcd5fe1ab0ab28704231b407a4c9e862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/a094211afcd5fe1ab0ab28704231b407a4c9e862"}],"sha":"39881106e5c56ea2304f526ee68e905784d76b37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/39881106e5c56ea2304f526ee68e905784d76b37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/a094211afcd5fe1ab0ab28704231b407a4c9e862/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:29:07Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:35:49Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: agent-eval-kit v0.0.3","tree":{"sha":"954667195f64b6d6bcca0080d46848dbfec135af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/trees/954667195f64b6d6bcca0080d46848dbfec135af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/git/commits/a094211afcd5fe1ab0ab28704231b407a4c9e862","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/a094211afcd5fe1ab0ab28704231b407a4c9e862","node_id":"C_kwDOUKLkONoAKGEwOTQyMTFhZmNkNWZlMWFiMGFiMjg3MDQyMzFiNDA3YTRjOWU4NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commit/e8e7f6196b0289b2502197075c37680e73aa3397","sha":"e8e7f6196b0289b2502197075c37680e73aa3397","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/e8e7f6196b0289b2502197075c37680e73aa3397"}],"sha":"a094211afcd5fe1ab0ab28704231b407a4c9e862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/a094211afcd5fe1ab0ab28704231b407a4c9e862"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/exam-rfi-orchestrator/commits/e8e7f6196b0289b2502197075c37680e73aa3397/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:54:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:59:36Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Give eight bars a rubric each, and stop one of them overstating its tolerance\n\nThis repository had no rubric directory at all: every bar was an unlabelled\nmodule constant, which is exactly what practice E1 asks a repository not to do.\nEight rubric files now carry each number beside the argument for it, the runner\nreads them, and assert_covers fails the build in both directions.\n\nWriting the arguments down surfaced one bar that said less than it meant.\ncitation_grounding at 0.99 is a PER-CASE grounding verdict over eleven golden\nrequests, not a rate over individual citations, so a 0.99 bar passed only at\neleven out of eleven: ten of eleven is 0.909. It was a 1.0 wearing a 0.99 label,\nand it now says 1.0, which is also what the property means, since an assertion in\na response pack that resolves to no document the orchestrator holds is a\nstatement made to a supervisor with nothing behind it.\n\nThe other seven bars were already 1.0 and the rubrics now say why: each is a\npolicy decision about what a regulator is told, with no sampling process for a\nrate to describe.\n\nTwo design details this repository already had are now written down where a\nreader will find them, because both are worth copying: blocker_recall is\nmicro-averaged over blockers rather than over cases (a per-case mean gave the\ncases expecting none a free 1.0 each, so a large share of the score was awarded\nfor checking nothing), and the corpus preconditions RAISE rather than score (a\ngolden set that plants no identifier, and a fixture corpus with no hard-withhold\ntag, are both refused rather than scored a vacuous 1.0).\n\ndocs/evals.md is generated from the rubrics and the corpus, with --check in\n`make gate`. Pin: agent-eval-kit v0.0.2. practices-audit gains E4 and E5. The\npromotion bundle this repository names is now registered by the authority, which\nit was not: --mode gate would have failed closed on UnknownMetricError.\n\nVerified: `make gate` green end to end (563 passed, eval PASS over 11 cases and\n8 metrics).","tree":{"sha":"7c93017190974c7f4cbf28b686d0d3001e579531","url":"https://api