4b1d9923298e84dde25eba85930"}],"sha":"56b292b67b04ae4999ffa0ba48a64cb5e42fc103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/56b292b67b04ae4999ffa0ba48a64cb5e42fc103"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4d5c3cead274d4b1d9923298e84dde25eba85930/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:16:28Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:16:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: close the .markdown endpoint to callers outside this node (#57)\n\nGHSA-q67w-prc3-ch5h #3. Opting a page into revision history was enough to\nserve every text-bearing string property beneath it -- including properties no\ntemplate displays -- to an anonymous visitor. An independent review re-measured\nthis on the released 1.4.12 jar and found the response byte-identical to\n1.4.10''s: the per-site exclusion list added in 1.4.11 ships EMPTY, so the\nfinding was made configurable rather than fixed.\n\nFixed at the reader instead of the source. The .markdown URL is not a\nvisitor-facing feature; it is how a snapshot is made -- the module asks this\nnode, over its own loopback connector, for the markdown render of a page and\nstores the answer, and the backfill script does the same for historical\ninstants. Nothing else reads it, and the public feature (the revision list and\nthe comparison) is rendered by HTML views that never touch it. So it now\nanswers 404 unless the caller is capture itself, presenting CaptureToken, or a\nuser holding siteAdminContentRevisionHistory on the site.\n\nWhy not narrow what is emitted. The breadth is load-bearing: a per-type list of\n\"which properties hold prose\" can never be complete, because modules ship their\nown types, and a snapshot that emits nothing for an unrecognised type is silent\ncontent loss -- which textProperties documents as the worst failure this module\nhas. Closing the endpoint fixes the whole class instead of the measured\ninstance, covers types nobody has written yet, needs no per-site configuration\nto be safe, and leaves every stored snapshot byte-identical, so no\ngeneratorVersion bump and no diff churn across the upgrade.\n\nWhy a token and not the caller''s address: Jahia is routinely fronted by Apache\nor HAProxy on the same host, so a public request reaches Tomcat from 127.0.0.1\nand would pass. Why not a credential: the capture render must stay ANONYMOUS,\nbecause rendering as guest is how the module establishes what the public can\nsee. The token authenticates the CALLER without touching the identity the\nrender runs AS, which no credential-based gate can do.\n\nThe gate sits in MarkdownContentTypeFilter.prepare at priority 5, beside the\nexisting opted-in gate and for the same reason: it is the only point before the\nfragment cache. A gate above CacheFilter (16.5) would refuse the miss and serve\nevery hit, which is exactly how 1.4.7''s content-type fix held for one request\nper cache lifetime. The two gates are independent and a test pins that.\n\ncapture.excludedProperties stays, and is now documented in the shipped .cfg,\nfor keeping a value out of the stored record at all -- a different question\nfrom who may read it.\n\nSpec 12 changed rather than being extended, because its premise no longer\nholds: it asserted that the ANONYMOUS .markdown response must be typed\ntext/plain, and there is no longer an anonymous response to type. It now\nasserts the stronger property -- nothing comes back at all, three times over so\na warm cache cannot serve it -- and the content-type and nosniff assertions\nmoved to an entitled caller, where they still bite and where the 1.4.7\nwarm-cache regression is still reachable.\n\nAlso verifies #4, which the advisory could not confirm in either direction\nbecause the case needs two entries with divergent per-entry ACLs and none exist\non a default install. Spec 14 builds that state. Its control is the distinction\nthe fix turns on: with no snapshots, an entitled caller reaches the snapshot\nlookup (noSnapshot) while a caller who may not read one entry is answered as\nabsent (notFound), and the per-entry check runs before the snapshot lookup. So\nthe test fails if that check is removed, rather than passing for both.\n\nGate: 389 unit tests (was 383), full Cypress suite 116/116 (was 111/13 specs),\nESLint and tsc clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e18142001bcc044f99d76537ec873fcddbe9a122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/e18142001bcc044f99d76537ec873fcddbe9a122"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/4d5c3cead274d4b1d9923298e84dde25eba85930","verification":{"payload":"tree e18142001bcc044f99d76537ec873fcddbe9a122\nparent e6a9acebd5e3c8e6d17caf149f3ca95ed8998d67\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788956188 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788956188 +0200\n\nfix: close the .markdown endpoint to callers outside this node (#57)\n\nGHSA-q67w-prc3-ch5h #3. Opting a page into revision history was enough to\nserve every text-bearing string property beneath it -- including properties no\ntemplate displays -- to an anonymous visitor. An independent review re-measured\nthis on the released 1.4.12 jar and found the response byte-identical to\n1.4.10''s: the per-site exclusion list added in 1.4.11 ships EMPTY, so the\nfinding was made configurable rather than fixed.\n\nFixed at the reader instead of the source. The .markdown URL is not a\nvisitor-facing feature; it is how a snapshot is made -- the module asks this\nnode, over its own loopback connector, for the markdown render of a page and\nstores the answer, and the backfill script does the same for historical\ninstants. Nothing else reads it, and the public feature (the revision list and\nthe comparison) is rendered by HTML views that never touch it. So it now\nanswers 404 unless the caller is capture itself, presenting CaptureToken, or a\nuser holding siteAdminContentRevisionHistory on the site.\n\nWhy not narrow what is emitted. The breadth is load-bearing: a per-type list of\n\"which properties hold prose\" can never be complete, because modules ship their\nown types, and a snapshot that emits nothing for an unrecognised type is silent\ncontent loss -- which textProperties documents as the worst failure this module\nhas. Closing the endpoint fixes the whole class instead of the measured\ninstance, covers types nobody has written yet, needs no per-site configuration\nto be safe, and leaves every stored snapshot byte-identical, so no\ngeneratorVersion bump and no diff churn across the upgrade.\n\nWhy a token and not the caller''s address: Jahia is routinely fronted by Apache\nor HAProxy on the same host, so a public request reaches Tomcat from 127.0.0.1\nand would pass. Why not a credential: the capture render must stay ANONYMOUS,\nbecause rendering as guest is how the module establishes what the public can\nsee. The token authenticates the CALLER without touching the identity the\nrender runs AS, which no credential-based gate can do.\n\nThe gate sits in MarkdownContentTypeFilter.prepare at priority 5, beside the\nexisting opted-in gate and for the same reason: it is the only point before the\nfragment cache. A gate above CacheFilter (16.5) would refuse the miss and serve\nevery hit, which is exactly how 1.4.7''s content-type fix held for one request\nper cache lifetime. The two gates are independent and a test pins that.\n\ncapture.excludedProperties stays, and is now documented in the shipped .cfg,\nfor keeping a value out of the stored record at all -- a different question\nfrom who may read it.\n\nSpec 12 changed rather than being extended, because its premise no longer\nholds: it asserted that the ANONYMOUS .markdown response must be typed\ntext/plain, and there is no longer an anonymous response to type. It now\nasserts the stronger property -- nothing comes back at all, three times over so\na warm cache cannot serve it -- and the content-type and nosniff assertions\nmoved to an entitled caller, where they still bite and where the 1.4.7\nwarm-cache regression is still reachable.\n\nAlso verifies #4, which the advisory could not confirm in either direction\nbecause the case needs two entries with divergent per-entry ACLs and none exist\non a default install. Spec 14 builds that state. Its control is the distinction\nthe fix turns on: with no snapshots, an entitled caller reaches the snapshot\nlookup (noSnapshot) while a caller who may not read one entry is answered as\nabsent (notFound), and the per-entry check runs before the snapshot lookup. So\nthe test fails if that check is removed, rather than passing for both.\n\nGate: 389 unit tests (was 383), full Cypress suite 116/116 (was 111/13 specs),\nESLint and tsc clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoU4cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8bQQAGMmRNXsPI29yhofXpSZK009\nebTir0z/6s9GxncIcfy2FVNjZahVv8dzv6XM28SnT15WS0lPTM+s6fjNCGIal1DR\ngu64OZx2yx2vsgIEKc+He+UiN9ma7TlYD7QmhT9nXYRAx5JrVu6y4WaY6mSMTQnH\n7ZA+9uJ+OlpaZhosdkdOmWaWiiGddAMGeF7o5VxecVDpdXRIUscy/oV7YrPNmImj\ndx2BkDYkDxsz25r8sTZpfIGSO+eyD1KF5N4AEkUR2BgnxCt9Sr3yLvg4FxPv3LIG\nKTFJNlTG054m/UFvyjUI+Jg8oK07Ni8DXeOabfAWyoOy3M+4/3mh9/FQopPcEXdW\nz6/mTq4BXJKFASrp0qP5Xm3VmxQaKYwaPQVp52qPBqNgKg79AOCHHJw1GBe3OtH9\nv+E6GXq3GR3jMJ4J5HBRU8uVdBx1safGVVfwIij5kamup9zig1U2Pzeq0NhsZD7e\nYemyDrWgILH2ZZnAVIsc7S/3SkpA8Wh0xvo6cqvZrTEsAVv7Vl0slr7y3Ky/nsxt\nouOM4H/jodjCNccglabE9kiTJ+GEB+yrMx5I8K/jS5YtkqoV4PtzYLpZtgwh/ip6\n35xAqhQOUe4K6Nqkcem0EdjiU7L6V76O8pRWng7hif+O+PDKVOaSsU39Gbj6Tx0Z\niDRhftWLescpCNGw6n0V\n=w+KP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T12:16:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/4d5c3cead274d4b1d9923298e84dde25eba85930","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDRkNWMzY2VhZDI3NGQ0YjFkOTkyMzI5OGU4NGRkZTI1ZWJhODU5MzA","parents":