24Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"release: 1.4.12\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e741bb19e7d7e1075c1f6e43b43cb5b07536478","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/9e741bb19e7d7e1075c1f6e43b43cb5b07536478"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/5edbe62c8fb55d190d0a2fbfddb0eaeac5b9fb18","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e741bb19e7d7e1075c1f6e43b43cb5b07536478\nparent dabf9ba183a1d296e75db941f8c04f1cc7ce1968\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788868224 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788868224 +0200\n\nrelease: 1.4.12\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqf9oAACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nhOAgAoKerFwR7JFqMVCNppkfOCFodW4dd02z+Mh9d/J+cQqimOY+3LkVlJHQZ\nT0sr97ipPHZTlfCe0v7DKk/DaxpPbeBAywHFGDGT6onCm7D63jxzwkihIHJEC5Pa\nJSwCq5LqTeMO4/9C+uz7D8HXLQfXtsyaRQZ1K1tmhZr5zk3W3d1bKwzYs5Lw6LJ6\nLvMkeVggmr3DUp6Wcu1DVwthjYTGYz62krL2U/nnAx3Mvkr5XWFCV8qLF5t6ZKeK\nFUycWE46yM+aU6aHiH5ZX/MULyQ5xHHQ4kAHsZyA2ZMwS+5MtMlYY2Wa5O5JT5IB\nc7EavqiupweyaSVd0wELILX46zRF/g==\n=QDf6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T11:50:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/5edbe62c8fb55d190d0a2fbfddb0eaeac5b9fb18","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDVlZGJlNjJjOGZiNTVkMTkwZDBhMmZiZmRkYjBlYWVhYzViOWZiMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/dabf9ba183a1d296e75db941f8c04f1cc7ce1968","sha":"dabf9ba183a1d296e75db941f8c04f1cc7ce1968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/dabf9ba183a1d296e75db941f8c04f1cc7ce1968"}],"sha":"5edbe62c8fb55d190d0a2fbfddb0eaeac5b9fb18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/5edbe62c8fb55d190d0a2fbfddb0eaeac5b9fb18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/dabf9ba183a1d296e75db941f8c04f1cc7ce1968/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T11:49:30Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T11:49:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: hide \"What changed\" on an Initial version revision (#53)\n\nThe first recorded revision of a page has no predecessor, so \"What changed\"\nhas no answer. Rendering the row anyway invited an editor to invent one\n(\"initial publication\") or left a visitor reading a description of a change\nthat never happened.\n\nThe whole dt/dd pair is dropped rather than the value alone: a <dt> with no\n<dd> is invalid inside a <dl>, and an empty <dd> would still spend a grid row\non an unanswered label. Compared with `ne` so every other value keeps the row,\nincluding an unset one -- matching the changeType fallback directly above it,\nwhich reads an empty value as substantive.\n\n`summary` stays mandatory and stays stored. What an editor wrote remains on\nthe node and in the export; it is simply not part of the PUBLIC record for\nthis one change type, which the new field description tells them. Relaxing\n`mandatory` would have applied to every change type, letting a substantive\nrevision publish with no explanation at all.\n\nThe e2e test asserts per <article>, not page-wide: \"What changed\" is a shared\nresource-bundle string, so a page-wide absence check would pass just as well\nif the row vanished for every change type -- the regression worth catching. It\nrenders an initial entry and a substantive sibling in one container and checks\nthe label and summary text are absent from the first and present in the second.\n\nAlso documents the \"Initial version\" change type in the README, which listed\nonly Editorial, Substantive and Correction -- drift predating this change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"b35b36e080487bee9968d089de51bd6a5a6e7a5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/b35b36e080487bee9968d089de51bd6a5a6e7a5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/dabf9ba183a1d296e75db941f8c04f1cc7ce1968","verification":{"payload":"tree b35b36e080487bee9968d089de51bd6a5a6e7a5f\nparent 5ccd88cbf6617a5545d51c75973425b8b45152f1\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788868170 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788868170 +0200\n\nfeat: hide \"What changed\" on an Initial version revision (#53)\n\nThe first recorded revision of a page has no predecessor, so \"What changed\"\nhas no answer. Rendering the row anyway invited an editor to invent one\n(\"initial publication\") or left a visitor reading a description of a change\nthat never happened.\n\nThe whole dt/dd pair is dropped rather than the value alone: a <dt> with no\n<dd> is invalid inside a <dl>, and an empty <dd> would still spend a grid row\non an unanswered label. Compared with `ne` so every other value keeps the row,\nincluding an unset one -- matching the changeType fallback directly above it,\nwhich reads an empty value as substantive.\n\n`summary` stays mandatory and stays stored. What an editor wrote remains on\nthe node and in the export; it is simply not part of the PUBLIC record for\nthis one change type, which the new field description tells them. Relaxing\n`mandatory` would have applied to every change type, letting a substantive\nrevision publish with no explanation at all.\n\nThe e2e test asserts per <article>, not page-wide: \"What changed\" is a shared\nresource-bundle string, so a page-wide absence check would pass just as well\nif the row vanished for every change type -- the regression worth catching. It\nrenders an initial entry and a substantive sibling in one container and checks\nthe label and summary text are absent from the first and present in the second.\n\nAlso documents the \"Initial version\" change type in the README, which listed\nonly Editorial, Substantive and Correction -- drift predating this change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn/ZKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/o0QAE/1IHNE9jqmf7Tfa6Ru98D+\nKGkwrQqL2V+0Vxp9td8An9cPM3ZgyUaliqM5M8pdfjEpA9TU45FTIZU1mCmQ+GME\nuqp6OuB1kVWtOk+p82KHgvRza55thufRg8tmHg/1OoZTiSFdcP16atkiLOAp3Szv\nt6CvYg4i/ccQHchzwX5G/GAAJRB4JmlR7ZgzVX10+habW+UFihCz2/JG4+fqdNA7\nr1l+RKYCZ8CnhoUgO5Q41aGg7t5V5zZSrjCwpP7Vr7qr4kZbO0bjJAALfrVjCEXu\nkmf1EjaRV4N07ajrzTTFz50/q51KFCCj21Ki6quFcPCfsa4KrgQ1o1+CSL+8JLiV\nMWMOUzELFBl7s2VBPsH9kcs0Lx9yqKEF1qab+BbrKxIsHbQ44ja6et0sQYMdAC9F\nVOTGacwrOTGY9/pgS3LSKvE7XDpxv8wUv81GrfoINqbnvV40wyoCzxwvevMxMftw\n59sdKPbQS+HDOyUXrOWqKHJCHb4sTIStwvgu/q8jwhQz/o4dlerZkqXl1yMyzRmx\nnxaF2HwTTMcELPKuvVKKaj7DK+1A8x+VVkEvDVvxD+vtfHBUpNhlnmuhJnHTJQnL\nc3pg0KNqN3ZuvozcTbepuhxcwjUGZ3wsGd0y1L3zF0UZ0v3NMUjOOqmyCMS085wG\nsix5BtcrW9tf8mP2ku+O\n=aJFE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T11:49:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https