F3aW4o\nq+ZCv3SAu4QZAIm9MODTmnUJiYMyEe/TtQ6oP4QPbVDp9p7KUeiLlM5gkN+cTF87\nsPuZ/D32U6Aeg2mgNJTUjiX0aHZDASVdiuiCt/gYJHJYA78deXU1jI8+NdlYRHA2\nyHSX197nuL1lbnqVFazQLvTKCy6pcg==\n=UQ3S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T05:57:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/4fdb3c44e3339ad46216d0ac6f14258233f1779a","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDRmZGIzYzQ0ZTMzMzlhZDQ2MjE2ZDBhYzZmMTQyNTgyMzNmMTc3OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/f7f466305556ec0b132d797a575dbc2227147f1a","sha":"f7f466305556ec0b132d797a575dbc2227147f1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/f7f466305556ec0b132d797a575dbc2227147f1a"}],"sha":"4fdb3c44e3339ad46216d0ac6f14258233f1779a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4fdb3c44e3339ad46216d0ac6f14258233f1779a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/f7f466305556ec0b132d797a575dbc2227147f1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T05:51:29Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T05:51:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: render blockquotes, rules, tables and links in the revision diff (#51)\n\n* feat: read blockquote depth and horizontal rule in InlineMarkdown\n\nParse the ''> '' quote prefix (counted per level, nesting-aware) and a bare\n''---'' rule out of a generated-Markdown line, so the diff panel can render\nthem formatted instead of as literal syntax. A table separator row keeps\nits pipes and is left to the table path; a heading or list inside a quote\nstill reports its own shape after the prefix is stripped.\n\nModel only; the view wiring follows. Word-level highlight crossing is\npreserved past the ''> '' prefix.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: render Markdown links as safe anchors in the diff, preserving change visibility\n\nA link now reads back as its text plus an allow-listed href (http, https,\nmailto, or site-relative) instead of staying literal ''[text](href)''. The\ndocumented invariant is kept a different way: the whole span carries one\nchanged flag, set when any character -- text OR href -- changed, so a\ndestination-only edit still highlights. Disallowed schemes (javascript:)\nnever become an href; the span falls back to literal. Images stay literal:\nthe ''!'' guards the ''['' so the link parser never fires on one.\n\nReplaces the linksStayLiteral test, whose assertion encoded the old literal\ncontract, with tests for the new one incl. the href-change-highlights case.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: render Markdown tables as cells in the diff instead of pipe rows\n\nTable membership is a block property, so MarkdownDiff detects it over the\nwhole line sequence -- a ''--- | ---'' separator anchors the block, the row\nabove is the header, the pipe rows below are the body -- and hands each Line\nan inTableBlock flag. InlineMarkdown then splits a row at '' | '' into cells,\ninline-parsing each over its own slice so bold, italic, links and the\nword-level highlight all work per cell; the separator is marked structure\nand carries no text. run()/link/emphasis scanning is now end-bounded so a\nbracket or delimiter in one cell cannot reach into the next.\n\nInherited limitations, documented: a single-column separator is just ''---''\n(indistinguishable from a rule) and a literal '' | '' inside a cell reads as a\nboundary -- both are ambiguities in how the normalizer stores tables.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: render blockquote, rule, tables and links in the diff view\n\nExtract the diff cell''s formatted-content rendering into two static-include\nfragments (md-line.jspf, md-piece.jspf) so the four cells of a row share one\nimplementation, then teach it the new shapes: a blockquote bar, a horizontal\nrule, table cells with dividers instead of pipes, and safe <a> links\n(rel=nofollow noopener, href allow-listed in Java and fn:escapeXml''d here).\nLine-level shape stays appearance-only -- classes, never real <blockquote>/\n<table> -- so the snapshot''s structure is never spliced into the host page.\nCSS inherits the row colour throughout, so every new shape still reads as\nadded or removed with the stylesheet absent (SC 1.4.1: never colour alone).\n\nTable columns are not aligned across rows (each diff row is an independent\ngrid element); the pipe soup is gone, which was the point.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: changelog entry for rendered blockquote, rule, tables and links\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: strip control chars before the link scheme check (defense in depth)\n\nhrefAllowed matched the scheme regex against the raw href, so a control char\ninside the scheme -- ''java\\tscript:'' -- broke the match and fell through as a\nsafe relative URL. Browsers strip tab/CR/LF from a URL before parsing its\nscheme, resolving it to javascript:, so this is the one case the read-side\nbackstop exists for. Now mirrors MarkdownNormalizer.sanitizeUrl exactly:\nstrip [\\x00-\\x1F\\x7F], then check, and emit the cleaned href so the check\nand the attribute agree on which characters count. Not reachable through the\ncurrent capture path (the normalizer already strips at capture); this closes\nthe backstop for snapshots from an older or foreign generator.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: three correctness gaps found in review (parens href, quoted tables, unchanged table rows)\n\n- matchLink balanced the parentheses in an href instead of taking the first\n  '')'', so a URL like https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foo_(bar) is no longer\n  truncated with a stray '')'' left over. The normalizer stores these unescaped.\n- MarkdownDiff strips the ''> '' quote prefix before its separator/boundary\n  checks, so a table nested in a blockquote is detected (it was rendered as\n  quoted text with literal pipes). Aligns the diff-side detector with the\n  strip InlineMarkdown already does.\n- An unchanged line''s table formatting now comes from either revision, not\n  only the old side: a header row whose text did not change is still shown\n  as cells when a separator was added beneath it in the other revision. The\n  OR only renders a table where one genuinely exists, never from shared prose.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: e2e coverage for rendered blockquote, rule, tables and links\n\nPublishes a revision carrying a quote, a rule, a link and a table, compares\nit against the plain-text rev-c, and asserts the panel renders crh-md-quote,\ncrh-md-rule, crh-md-cell, crh-md-tsep and an <a class=\"crh-md-link\"> with the\nsanitised href -- and that the raw Markdown syntax and real structural\nelements never reach a diff row. Closes the gap where the model was unit-\ntested but the end-to-end rendering was not.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address blind PR review (emphasis parity, link-parse DoS, a11y contrast/focus/cells)\n\nCorrectness:\n- closesLater/italicClosesLater now test backslash-run PARITY, not just the\n  single preceding char, so a bold/italic span whose text ends in a literal\n  backslash (e.g. **C:\\temp\\**) keeps its emphasis instead of silently\n  rendering as literal asterisks. Pre-existing; surfaced by the review.\n- matchLink caps its paren-balance scan at MAX_HREF_SCAN so a line of anchors\n  with an unbalanced ''('' cannot make link parsing O(n^2) on the public path.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2):\n- .crh-md-rule / .crh-md-tsep use var(--crh-rule) instead of a faded\n  currentColor, clearing the 3:1 non-text-contrast floor (SC 1.4.11); tsep is\n  dashed to stay distinct from a rule.\n- .crh-md-link gets the module''s focus ring (SC 2.4.13).\n- Table cells carry a visually-hidden separator so a screen reader does not\n  run adjacent cells together.\n\nDocs: record the stored-format ambiguities (authored ''---'' -> rule; literal\n'' | '' in a cell) and the a11y gaps (no semantic table for AT; link name lacks\nolder/newer side) as known limitations, plus tighten the link-highlight\nguarantee wording. New unit tests for parity, the scan bound, protocol-relative\nrejection, control-char-cleaned href, single-column fallback, and the old-side\nof the unchanged-table OR.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: assert rel=nofollow noopener on the rendered diff link\n\nCloses the last coverage gap from the review: the E2E rich-formatting case now\npins the anchor''s rel attribute alongside its class and href.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc072d0645cdcc83d64cdaa58fc10f42409ab51f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/bc072d0645cdcc83d64cdaa58fc10f42409ab51f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/f7f466305556ec0b132d797a575dbc2227147f1a","verification":{"payload":"tree bc072d0645cdcc83d64cdaa58fc10f42409ab51f\nparent 965fbd729c5f7acf2baad81b3f192ac37499ee3c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788587489 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788587489 +0200\n\nfeat: render blockquotes, rules, tables and links in the revision diff (#51)\n\n* feat: read blockquote depth and horizontal rule in InlineMarkdown\n\nParse the ''> '' quote prefix (counted per level, nesting-aware) and a bare\n''---'' rule out of a generated-Markdown line, so the diff panel can render\nthem formatted instead of as literal syntax. A table separator row keeps\nits pipes and is left to the table path; a heading or list inside a quote\nstill reports its own shape after the prefix is stripped.\n\nModel only; the view wiring follows. Word-level highlight crossing is\npreserved past the ''> '' prefix.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: render Markdown links as safe anchors in the diff, preserving change visibility\n\nA link now reads back as its text plus an allow-listed href (http, https,\nmailto, or site-relative) instead of staying literal ''[text](href)''. The\ndocumented invariant is kept a different way: the whole span carries one\nchanged flag, set when any character -- text OR href -- changed, so a\ndestination-only edit still highlights. Disallowed schemes (javascript:)\nnever become an href; the span falls back to literal. Images stay literal:\nthe ''!'' guards the ''['' so the link parser never fires on one.\n\nReplaces the linksStayLiteral test, whose assertion encoded the old literal\ncontract, with tests for the new one incl. the href-change-highlights case.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: render Markdown tables as cells in the diff instead of pipe rows\n\nTable membership is a block property, so MarkdownDiff detects it over the\nwhole line sequence -- a ''--- | ---'' separator anchors the block, the row\nabove is the header, the pipe rows below are the body -- and hands each Line\nan inTableBlock flag. InlineMarkdown then splits a row at '' | '' into cells,\ninline-parsing each over its own slice so bold, italic, links and the\nword-level highlight all work per cell; the separator is marked structure\nand carries no text. run()/link/emphasis scanning is now end-bounded so a\nbracket or delimiter in one cell cannot reach into the next.\n\nInherited limitations, documented: a single-column separator is just ''---''\n(indistinguishable from a rule) and a literal '' | '' inside a cell reads as a\nboundary -- both are ambiguities in how the normalizer stores tables.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: render blockquote, rule, tables and links in the diff view\n\nExtract the diff cell''s formatted-content rendering into two static-include\nfragments (md-line.jspf, md-piece.jspf) so the four cells of a row share one\nimplementation, then teach it the new shapes: a blockquote bar, a horizontal\nrule, table cells with dividers instead of pipes, and safe <a> links\n(rel=nofollow noopener, href allow-listed in Java and fn:escapeXml''d here).\nLine-level shape stays appearance-only -- classes, never real <blockquote>/\n<table> -- so the snapshot''s structure is never spliced into the host page.\nCSS inherits the row colour throughout, so every new shape still reads as\nadded or removed with the stylesheet absent (SC 1.4.1: never colour alone).\n\nTable columns are not aligned across rows (each diff row is an independent\ngrid element); the pipe soup is gone, which was the point.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: changelog entry for rendered blockquote, rule, tables and links\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: strip control chars before the link scheme check (defense in depth)\n\nhrefAllowed matched the scheme regex against the raw href, so a control char\ninside the scheme -- ''java\\tscript:'' -- broke the match and fell through as a\nsafe relative URL. Browsers strip tab/CR/LF from a URL before parsing its\nscheme, resolving it to javascript:, so this is the one case the read-side\nbackstop exists for. Now mirrors MarkdownNormalizer.sanitizeUrl exactly:\nstrip [\\x00-\\x1F\\x7F], then check, and emit the cleaned href so the check\nand the attribute agree on which characters count. Not reachable through the\ncurrent capture path (the normalizer already strips at capture); this closes\nthe backstop for snapshots from an older or foreign generator.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: three correctness gaps found in review (parens href, quoted tables, unchanged table rows)\n\n- matchLink balanced the parentheses in an href instead of taking the first\n  '')'', so a URL like https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foo_(bar) is no longer\n  truncated with a stray '')'' left over. The normalizer stores these unescaped.\n- MarkdownDiff strips the ''> '' quote prefix before its separator/boundary\n  checks, so a table nested in a blockquote is detected (it was rendered as\n  quoted text with literal pipes). Aligns the diff-side detector with the\n  strip InlineMarkdown already does.\n- An unchanged line''s table formatting now comes from either revision, not\n  only the old side: a header row whose text did not change is still shown\n  as cells when a separator was added beneath it in the other revision. The\n  OR only renders a table where one genuinely exists, never from shared prose.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: e2e coverage for rendered blockquote, rule, tables and links\n\nPublishes a revision carrying a quote, a rule, a link and a table, compares\nit against the plain-text rev-c, and asserts the panel renders crh-md-quote,\ncrh-md-rule, crh-md-cell, crh-md-tsep and an <a class=\"crh-md-link\"> with the\nsanitised href -- and that the raw Markdown syntax and real structural\nelements never reach a diff row. Closes the gap where the model was unit-\ntested but the end-to-end rendering was not.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address blind PR review (emphasis parity, link-parse DoS, a11y contrast/focus/cells)\n\nCorrectness:\n- closesLater/italicClosesLater now test backslash-run PARITY, not just the\n  single preceding char, so a bold/italic span whose text ends in a literal\n  backslash (e.g. **C:\\temp\\**) keeps its emphasis instead of silently\n  rendering as literal asterisks. Pre-existing; surfaced by the review.\n- matchLink caps its paren-balance scan at MAX_HREF_SCAN so a line of anchors\n  with an unbalanced ''('' cannot make link parsing O(n^2) on the public path.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2):\n- .crh-md-rule / .crh-md-tsep use var(--crh-rule) instead of a faded\n  currentColor, clearing the 3:1 non-text-contrast floor (SC 1.4.11); tsep is\n  dashed to stay distinct from a rule.\n- .crh-md-link gets the module''s focus ring (SC 2.4.13).\n- Table cells carry a visually-hidden separator so a screen reader does not\n  run adjacent cells together.\n\nDocs: record the stored-format ambiguities (authored ''---'' -> rule; literal\n'' | '' in a cell) and the a11y gaps (no semantic table for AT; link name lacks\nolder/newer side) as known limitations, plus tighten the link-highlight\nguarantee wording. New unit tests for parity, the scan bound, protocol-relative\nrejection, control-char-cleaned href, single-column fallback, and the old-side\nof the unchanged-table OR.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: assert rel=nofollow noopener on the rendered diff link\n\nCloses the last coverage gap from the review: the E2E rich-formatting case now\npins the anchor''s rel attribute alongside its class and href.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqm63hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANasQAIfotCrXt/H5yEAguvRO1gkH\nB10sfiC4ZjecaS6Z9thKJIty8GXJFEaLRewz6xP/9SBwGnzrGIHsBaLrNfEQ0xfW\nYcr1wBnHRc9iNZSL30Dy3OUlgNBtL7i6WEvp3lM98+l3Jzt6O9vhZvcKHYQDfSWu\n+4GSaRAQnV1Tykktcu8av74XF8FZrv9bY/U1Xjj28QATkXzFzlSTHbdnFphAeY35\nHrL96Uzej+NQGzQS3eAbZe45WuX+3D/6iAoGq3ltec9DJe5DXdx2epNEsnLIW8Lo\nQvG1kal67xoM/qBgHEfKTFsGPgrm0jLQ2Z51KhZ1jfbv6dyymIcJPRmoNDqjrSzF\ns5UT7lkNFCkSynzSSqL4rNmWskY6856hExc37ouSCnZVj5aFEZVxZMlqxWGscTxi\n/Bo/h56BAEkOuIV7yUAy3+O9V8XqYpvEXc6HezYi/X05KW/s/V50hJtdEW/chkmz\nQvBNtaoJ14jr7LY67d+F9KTtnf8aODWMhhbTY9lZIJ/pG5x+ry3VFFkIdQtHw39Y\nfxINV750NysAA+Df2s3rX0dJHApU6L6/dZVOYQ/nvzPmqGWMRKPRJuUf74oMG+lV\nop8ZAH5l+ddF4L+lVbA92hDcKPW6AQ8E64Qx1IY8Wuvi/+1JzzHoKO2BN1+k7bo4\nB67+OCH5NmH/FnZ3exF1\n=ifqH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T05:51:30Z"}},"committer":{"avata