se/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/a3fec7c8ed4f6f42a0940b7ffce9ef611106c344/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:20:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:20:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: gate .markdown to opted-in pages; mask emphasis spans; record status for any captured language (#49)\n\n* fix(security): gate the .markdown endpoint to pages that opted into revision history\n\nCloses #46.\n\nThe markdown views are registered on the core jnt:page/jnt:content types,\nso installing the module opened an anonymous .markdown URL on every page of\nevery site, and crh:textProperties handed a visitor every text-bearing\nproperty of every guest-readable node -- including properties the page''s\nHTML view never displays. Verified live: about.markdown (not revisioned)\nreturned 200 text/plain with layout-config properties (predefinedColumns,\n8_4, full-width) that never appear as visible text on about.html.\n\nNot an ACL bypass -- a guest-unreadable node still 404s -- but it crosses\n\"not shown by the template\" into \"not exposed\" and breaks the module''s\npromise to change nothing until a page opts in.\n\nMarkdownContentTypeFilter now refuses (404, empty body) any .markdown\nrender whose main resource is not within a jmix:publiclyRevisioned node,\nvia RevisionedAncestor.of. The check is on the MAIN resource, so one check\nsettles a page and all its nested component renders; fail-closed on error.\nCapture is unaffected: it only fetches .markdown for revisioned pages and\ncontent nodes, which is exactly what passes the gate. The Cypress specs\nthat fetched a non-opted-in page (10 sub-page, 12 plain page) now assert\n404 and no property leak.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: mask emphasis spans from the sentence splitter, like links\n\nCloses #47.\n\nAn <em>/<strong> covering more than one sentence was shredded: maskLinks\nprotected [...](...) from BreakIterator but nothing protected *...* /\n**...**, so <em>First. Second.</em> normalised to \"*First.\\nSecond\\n.\\n*\"\nand the viewer, finding no closing delimiter on a line, showed literal\nasterisks and an orphan \".\". Same \"display disagrees with the archive\"\nclass as #27/#44, introduced when #27 taught the viewer to render emphasis.\n\nEmphasis spans are masked alongside links now (bold before italic so **\nnever reaches the single-* pass; a negative lookbehind keeps an escaped \\*\nfrom being read as a delimiter). Restoration is outermost-first, so a bold\nspan containing a link is put back intact. Both patterns are non-greedy and\nsingle-line, hence linear-time -- a ReDoS test pins that.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: record a capture status for any language the module actually tried to capture\n\nCloses #48.\n\nrecordStatus reaches ensureFolder -> requireKnownLanguage, which validated\nthe language against the site''s configured languages (getLanguages()) while\ncapture is triggered for its active-live languages\n(fillInMissingLanguages -> getActiveLiveLanguages()). When the two sets\ndiffer -- a language dropped between publish and the async capture -- the\ndurable FAILED write threw IllegalArgumentException and recordStatus\nswallowed it, so the record this module relies on was lost and the gap\nshowed only in the log. The guard now accepts the union of both sets, via\nthe package-private isKnownLanguage, which is unit-tested directly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"53bf8f6c17fc5fd7e93eef39c1638b4ce3f7d503","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/53bf8f6c17fc5fd7e93eef39c1638b4ce3f7d503"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/a3fec7c8ed4f6f42a0940b7ffce9ef611106c344","verification":{"payload":"tree 53bf8f6c17fc5fd7e93eef39c1638b4ce3f7d503\nparent d238cda988ee9a22ed4823280ab3621fc1c6899c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788510034 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788510034 +0200\n\nfix: gate .markdown to opted-in pages; mask emphasis spans; record status for any captured language (#49)\n\n* fix(security): gate the .markdown endpoint to pages that opted into revision history\n\nCloses #46.\n\nThe markdown views are registered on the core jnt:page/jnt:content types,\nso installing the module opened an anonymous .markdown URL on every page of\nevery site, and crh:textProperties handed a visitor every text-bearing\nproperty of every guest-readable node -- including properties the page''s\nHTML view never displays. Verified live: about.markdown (not revisioned)\nreturned 200 text/plain with layout-config properties (predefinedColumns,\n8_4, full-width) that never appear as visible text on about.html.\n\nNot an ACL bypass -- a guest-unreadable node still 404s -- but it crosses\n\"not shown by the template\" into \"not exposed\" and breaks the module''s\npromise to change nothing until a page opts in.\n\nMarkdownContentTypeFilter now refuses (404, empty body) any .markdown\nrender whose main resource is not within a jmix:publiclyRevisioned node,\nvia RevisionedAncestor.of. The check is on the MAIN resource, so one check\nsettles a page and all its nested component renders; fail-closed on error.\nCapture is unaffected: it only fetches .markdown for revisioned pages and\ncontent nodes, which is exactly what passes the gate. The Cypress specs\nthat fetched a non-opted-in page (10 sub-page, 12 plain page) now assert\n404 and no property leak.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: mask emphasis spans from the sentence splitter, like links\n\nCloses #47.\n\nAn <em>/<strong> covering more than one sentence was shredded: maskLinks\nprotected [...](...) from BreakIterator but nothing protected *...* /\n**...**, so <em>First. Second.</em> normalised to \"*First.\\nSecond\\n.\\n*\"\nand the viewer, finding no closing delimiter on a line, showed literal\nasterisks and an orphan \".\". Same \"display disagrees with the archive\"\nclass as #27/#44, introduced when #27 taught the viewer to render emphasis.\n\nEmphasis spans are masked alongside links now (bold before italic so **\nnever reaches the single-* pass; a negative lookbehind keeps an escaped \\*\nfrom being read as a delimiter). Restoration is outermost-first, so a bold\nspan containing a link is put back intact. Both patterns are non-greedy and\nsingle-line, hence linear-time -- a ReDoS test pins that.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: record a capture status for any language the module actually tried to capture\n\nCloses #48.\n\nrecordStatus reaches ensureFolder -> requireKnownLanguage, which validated\nthe language against the site''s configured languages (getLanguages()) while\ncapture is triggered for its active-live languages\n(fillInMissingLanguages -> getActiveLiveLanguages()). When the two sets\ndiffer -- a language dropped between publish and the async capture -- the\ndurable FAILED write threw IllegalArgumentException and recordStatus\nswallowed it, so the record this module relies on was lost and the gap\nshowed only in the log. The guard now accepts the union of both sets, via\nthe package-private isKnownLanguage, which is unit-tested directly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmn9SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbugQAGUFL3Qk6wb8G6wqtNVEEeTG\nkHq50ccf7oMcTi6kULE/tyQt+Em9zzRwioKZMF2x5yVdDF