38cda988ee9a22ed4823280ab3621fc1c6899c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/d238cda988ee9a22ed4823280ab3621fc1c6899c"}],"sha":"a3fec7c8ed4f6f42a0940b7ffce9ef611106c344","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/a3fec7c8ed4f6f42a0940b7ffce9ef611106c344"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/d238cda988ee9a22ed4823280ab3621fc1c6899c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:01:55Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:01:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: escape line-start syntax in content so the viewer does not show it as structure (#45)\n\nCloses #44.\n\nA rich-text paragraph -- or a plain-string property -- beginning a line\nwith \"#\", \"- \" or \"N. \" was read by InlineMarkdown as a heading, a bullet\nor an ordered item. The archive was right; the panel misrepresented it,\nthe same defect as the inline asterisks of #27 at the other position.\n\nThe renderer now marks the lines it makes structural (headings, list\nitems, fences and fenced code, and the \"# title\" headings the views emit\nas text) with a private-use character, and the sentence splitter -- the\nonly stage that knows where lines actually start -- escapes those three\nshapes on every unmarked line and strips the marker from the rest. The\nmarker never reaches the output; a test asserts that.\n\nNo generator bump: 6 is unreleased.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"0089ad0fff9223deb68e28aa30ab835bd723a8e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/0089ad0fff9223deb68e28aa30ab835bd723a8e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/d238cda988ee9a22ed4823280ab3621fc1c6899c","verification":{"payload":"tree 0089ad0fff9223deb68e28aa30ab835bd723a8e4\nparent 0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788505315 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788505315 +0200\n\nfix: escape line-start syntax in content so the viewer does not show it as structure (#45)\n\nCloses #44.\n\nA rich-text paragraph -- or a plain-string property -- beginning a line\nwith \"#\", \"- \" or \"N. \" was read by InlineMarkdown as a heading, a bullet\nor an ordered item. The archive was right; the panel misrepresented it,\nthe same defect as the inline asterisks of #27 at the other position.\n\nThe renderer now marks the lines it makes structural (headings, list\nitems, fences and fenced code, and the \"# title\" headings the views emit\nas text) with a private-use character, and the sentence splitter -- the\nonly stage that knows where lines actually start -- escapes those three\nshapes on every unmarked line and strips the marker from the rest. The\nmarker never reaches the output; a test asserts that.\n\nNo generator bump: 6 is unreleased.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmmzkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9gwQAIj+z4AVhCwGwolWEWsexZb2\nivQ0hLsTMmW6HPoC9CsaTesF5ifDN3pRJhyQJX7WQs5OAL3/l+OKpffv232COHbT\nRkcC336DULisP56UPABTu7ETScG4hEZIzsKWNYWw7b6TyFDTtQ/rB82Ec5XJZVKJ\nOAtzsD3WoNi908PJDUniDGcg4kF25afPXOljJ1N97n6Ws8/3w6y/Crg37NOLKpCT\nFgnSCn//S0QWwS2IT3YY2EPri8M6810AtZQ32mAyeYlaSp0p9yMPGtcypa2ld87m\n2x4jfttM92nux3tTC/AUC+evyeD1Kd9Qh7bHWOeYSAJbFpdBWaWmlwiybelspu3c\nmjs61jNcf+WWBigZMBxduqgpi03a+DfxWjDXeO4wDMGxa5OhmuOSDLQpfqOyuzrb\nMUH9b32T+U0cWucQ9TRP99VtbP1ol24rxZLfjBtsNCt4Ls9iGD5DR0FbqOypbjbt\n2C0YuadgsQ9saA5BlAftdkD0SApAJrElTHUuIL8lP4kODrFjTsubeXSIiKKf6PjC\nDM1qqyjvT56wcSBuPlmcGlgQfMRDrj/ajPy4j4cvFRKP0o30wc0zPqRt+N1MSCvy\nWi1YH7kJqvYpcyoH+nlEVxg22s77WTRlJ/fmmGlzA1bzeHOHutfvdshbwfzlBrrD\n5lflTYIF5jKaogcWnGuf\n=/koO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T07:01:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/d238cda988ee9a22ed4823280ab3621fc1c6899c","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGQyMzhjZGE5ODhlZTlhMjJlZDQ4MjMyODBhYjM2MjFmYzFjNjg5OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3","sha":"0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3"}],"sha":"d238cda988ee9a22ed4823280ab3621fc1c6899c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/d238cda988ee9a22ed4823280ab3621fc1c6899c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:44:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:44:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: a page''s markdown snapshot no longer includes its sub-pages (#43)\n\n* fix: a page''s markdown snapshot no longer includes its sub-pages\n\nCloses #23.\n\nSub-pages are children of the page node, and template:module on one\nresolves the same page view and recurses, so a page''s snapshot contained\nevery page beneath it rather than what a visitor sees on it. Revisioning\n/home snapshotted the whole site -- a permanent OVERSIZE -- and under the\ncap, republishing after an unrelated sub-page changed made the comparison\nshow text that never appeared on the page. RevisionEntryBinder already\nskipped PAGE_TYPE; the view now does too. A sub-page owns its own history\nwhen it opts in, and still renders on its own .markdown URL.\n\nCypress: 10-fallbackViewContent gains a sub-page under the probe page and\nasserts its title is absent from the parent render and present on its own.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: per-site file naming, the retention floor and reference protection\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d8b84b13b433bf626a5dd6fc17f589d53ada48ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/d8b84b13b433bf626a5dd6fc17f589d53ada48ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3","verification":{"payload":"tree d8b84b13b433bf626a5dd6fc17f589d53ada48ba\nparent ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788504285 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788504285 +0200\n\nfix: a page''s markdown snapshot no longer includes its sub-pages (#43)\n\n* fix: a page''s markdown snapshot no longer includes its sub-pages\n\nCloses #23.\n\nSub-pages are children of the page node, and template:module on one\nresolves the same page view and recurses, so a page''s snapshot contained\nevery page beneath it rather than what a visitor sees on it. Revisioning\n/home snapshotted the whole site -- a permanent OVERSIZE -- and under the\ncap, republishing after an unrelated sub-page changed made the comparison\nshow text that never appeared on the page. RevisionEntryBinder already\nskipped PAGE_TYPE; the view now does too. A sub-page owns its own history\nwhen it opts in, and still renders on its own .markdown URL.\n\nCypress: 10-fallbackViewContent gains a sub-page under the probe page and\nasserts its title is absent from the parent render and present on its own.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: per-site file naming, the retention floor and reference protection\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmmjdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6RoQAI1tlsLMKo66dYOTG/EyMhkS\n2soMDoJmmKj+644Ru47bH9inI65Ps3ku31tTa4G6BOxJbIph4ve4ucL4DwFUIuFP\nkI2YzwvCrdHbnz+Ui3pIPvYTE6pjyk/f9dEndTxA6KJXnLVvdZ7lizL1WOxV/rHc\nL7/aHx/9f/tfyFbsAm/rxgih2cc4Jbm/70iHXhvs39JabuqObh1Rj2vHuFjC8W9j\n1xZG7dcNxBRgbCSIwIpaazPLtnVb/IthF93m1Ymwsvnmsz0jCz7U56H4crkAr8hZ\nj1AnE9yYmpQlEYlvlG5KPIVlbgzh+CQ4KX6ye+AouuiZIjptkDEjTmAb3GXoFFwo\npJtadacmeMiG0NM8QXE1+MN6pn+ho0Rc+BtedaVJTnjMJPzthLOgl2guQdvVPoGo\nwqMriVUQ4c9jSBRmyP6TKkLFDTz5oOzMs0vqOROsGw5DLtICfdcZAxk7cMCC/w6y\n+s4cV6py6z9rSsTwKI5DHTfnt5L+iLw6XFSZN4PM8W+YFXOa1jB+nnao2970RBio\nEPwKhKaJs2L35sXG88nony6qJ5Fa9d5/a/B9NS/D2qliydTl0zz76hVAs/yqer0M\nXTReltCL/RT0pTXtrdQY6LGgoT+07oGsTeBlaSR5KQ0mUmcluNmD+sx+b+I1uPUH\ngz3eSAyyhBZoP302Uxal\n=mzi3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T06:44:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDBiMmZmNjc5ZDYxODNjYTEwYzQ0MGUwNjdlYzVmODI0MzE0MzU5YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810","sha":"ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810"}],"sha":"0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0b2ff679d6183ca10c440e067ec5f824314359a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:42:15Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:42:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: keep relative links in revision summaries; close the prune and capture test gaps (#42)\n\nCloses #26, #33, #36.\n\n#26  RichTextSanitizer resolved every URL against an empty base URI. jsoup\n     removes an attribute that fails to resolve whatever preserveRelativeLinks\n     says, so every site-relative and fragment href was stripped and \"see the\n     <a>policy page</a>\" rendered as dead text -- the opposite of the comment\n     beside the call. A reserved .invalid base makes the protocol check pass;\n     the attribute keeps the value the editor wrote. Unwrapped block elements\n     are separated by a space instead of running together (onetwo, alphabeta).\n#33  Every prune fixture had excess >= n - 1, so the cap never ended the loop\n     and getNodes() was stubbed in chronological order, so the sort was a\n     no-op. New fixtures: 10 snapshots at cap 5 (exactly the six oldest go),\n     3 at cap 5 (nothing goes), and newest-first iteration at cap 3.\n#36  The snapshot name was assembled twice under a comment saying the copies\n     could not drift; nothing tested that. It is built once (snapshotName),\n     storedByTheWinner and snapshotPath are package-private and tested\n     against a session mock including the unreadable case, and coordinate\n     validation is tested through the public write path instead of by\n     reflection on the patterns.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"93baec4db81c3707923d21f02f5c9d9324e7527f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/93baec4db81c3707923d21f02f5c9d9324e7527f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810","verification":{"payload":"tree 93baec4db81c3707923d21f02f5c9d9324e7527f\nparent 12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788504135 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788504135 +0200\n\nfix: keep relative links in revision summaries; close the prune and capture test gaps (#42)\n\nCloses #26, #33, #36.\n\n#26  RichTextSanitizer resolved every URL against an empty base URI. jsoup\n     removes an attribute that fails to resolve whatever preserveRelativeLinks\n     says, so every site-relative and fragment href was stripped and \"see the\n     <a>policy page</a>\" rendered as dead text -- the opposite of the comment\n     beside the call. A reserved .invalid base makes the protocol check pass;\n     the attribute keeps the value the editor wrote. Unwrapped block elements\n     are separated by a space instead of running together (onetwo, alphabeta).\n#33  Every prune fixture had excess >= n - 1, so the cap never ended the loop\n     and getNodes() was stubbed in chronological order, so the sort was a\n     no-op. New fixtures: 10 snapshots at cap 5 (exactly the six oldest go),\n     3 at cap 5 (nothing goes), and newest-first iteration at cap 3.\n#36  The snapshot name was assembled twice under a comment saying the copies\n     could not drift; nothing tested that. It is built once (snapshotName),\n     storedByTheWinner and snapshotPath are package-private and tested\n     against a session mock including the unreadable case, and coordinate\n     validation is tested through the public write path instead of by\n     reflection on the patterns.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmmhHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALxoQAKRv6ATi4X6VK/X9Oldtshn2\nHJasp4yxxYKkBONvlvNnnfHR9mg0N9ijJX6wFHp27M5L70fJOUq+qXtkqM046fYp\nRQZaQguLJHHScjfxgstZiHz31tcxm6eXN7wp3k0bxy2SZgM3cbAbr3vdWuG9IZZa\n/SeQEWLHzZZCotKuNH8wpKfL2Vlr89Ct9EQNpad9K+2JCvRmghWjbchHKV/rfhzG\nYRocdC5Tbz0jQoyyB1rSEBYbphh5WoYGmg9O1JIkhK0WKAtyMKg8V/SBj7+YXpBO\n7a8c6kHvR+P5dUHtheQtPbC3rBKZDvtDJOsKhl/bYW3IMBWuFPrU/Fd3xensUFmF\nJHIrOBnvK5GP3mnTPU5dFoEFan/1cdZJyQDYZLY/tKEYnhwYvQKsApfW6qUPaqZE\nrD1YNGAsr94u902fLeJeFYIt8xpo1AtV7W9aO8TCxlayOILBz/J6SlUWByiHtOPK\n7IkRfHy/Z5wCG5J3igqEC9EYu09Hkh3FTmE75oBd4PwrRcKbWGv0KuWy1nxRZxKv\nwnamCtKGvch0ESssKBYWcGDEam/VJhgZVfQe9qc2uQ302hpGdC2CZPOS3fywEj+Y\na4Ugpei//pley1o70ZqnX+EhE6Zvzlzwh+oqCWt6HR4EnZbHivUAdn0cuBIw2mtT\nL4OfGK056pkY8F3y4nDL\n=gT9m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T06:42:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGNlYWYyOTBiZDU3ZmNiN2NhNjNhZmRmZjcxMjZlNGFiMzVlZTQ4MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa","sha":"12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa"}],"sha":"ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/ceaf290bd57fcb7ca63afdff7126e4ab35ee4810"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:40:09Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:40:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: per-site settings -- write back to the delivering file, clear on delete, one key rule, typed errors (#41)\n\nCloses #21, #28, #29, #30, #31, #32, #34, #35.\n\n     updated() keys a site by the siteKey property inside whatever file\n     delivered it. A site configured from an operator-named file got a\n     second file on the first panel save, the hand-added capture.secret was\n     not carried into it, the two files competed across restarts, and \"Use\n     defaults\" removed only the new one. The registry now remembers the\n     file FileInstall delivered each site from (felix.fileinstall.filename)\n     and rewrites that; the conventional name is used only for a site with\n     no file yet.\n     refetch still showed the deleted settings and a publication in the\n     FileInstall window was captured under them. Cleared immediately, as\n     save() already applied its write immediately.\n     legal key such as _intranet captured normally but could not save\n     settings. One rule now: RevisionSnapshotService.isValidSiteKey.\n     exceptions, which the GraphQL error handler collapses to \"Internal\n     Server Error(s)\". They are now BaseGqlClientException with the\n     registry''s message.\n     re-emitted, growing by one line per save. Skipped on read.\n     mutation refused it and the panel said min=1. One floor (2) applied\n     on read, with a warning, and in the panel.\n     so caught the SSRF guard, not the line-break check. It now injects\n     through capture.user and asserts the message; the backslash refusal\n     is tested for the first time.\n     last test; the registry''s fallback assertion held only by run order.\n     Reset after each test, and the fallback is asserted positively.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2e8d13be1b6819a99b4fe3c7ff4cb87235c5fe34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/2e8d13be1b6819a99b4fe3c7ff4cb87235c5fe34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e8d13be1b6819a99b4fe3c7ff4cb87235c5fe34\nparent a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788504009 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788504009 +0200\n\nfix: per-site settings -- write back to the delivering file, clear on delete, one key rule, typed errors (#41)\n\nCloses #21, #28, #29, #30, #31, #32, #34, #35.\n\n     updated() keys a site by the siteKey property inside whatever file\n     delivered it. A site configured from an operator-named file got a\n     second file on the first panel save, the hand-added capture.secret was\n     not carried into it, the two files competed across restarts, and \"Use\n     defaults\" removed only the new one. The registry now remembers the\n     file FileInstall delivered each site from (felix.fileinstall.filename)\n     and rewrites that; the conventional name is used only for a site with\n     no file yet.\n     refetch still showed the deleted settings and a publication in the\n     FileInstall window was captured under them. Cleared immediately, as\n     save() already applied its write immediately.\n     legal key such as _intranet captured normally but could not save\n     settings. One rule now: RevisionSnapshotService.isValidSiteKey.\n     exceptions, which the GraphQL error handler collapses to \"Internal\n     Server Error(s)\". They are now BaseGqlClientException with the\n     registry''s message.\n     re-emitted, growing by one line per save. Skipped on read.\n     mutation refused it and the panel said min=1. One floor (2) applied\n     on read, with a warning, and in the panel.\n     so caught the SSRF guard, not the line-break check. It now injects\n     through capture.user and asserts the message; the backslash refusal\n     is tested for the first time.\n     last test; the registry''s fallback assertion held only by run order.\n     Reset after each test, and the fallback is asserted positively.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmmfJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr6sQAKtTFviQCfYyn2G6iyRGQsP/\nHwBQ0ymLm8V3+4Eq1f8udp1WOzIyTuOumAM40Q0L8RZcBy93jehJQC7GxKJ13Sku\n/B0XhS7dNwMDJhagICFUwfu8M63MSSQDVDTLiKigvXLj1+JCh7yDnNIJis4k9sSZ\nATdnGW+TGvxfxl12fHUCAnCPqCGLbGc2uMPSn76bSJff2Z58DKo1w6BYW8zcCN/O\np62OSSi0lS+pVEIPoTvV2c8cABZ7XHpS7UxE7LskYQx9QxkAczPsfI1fjxGgwhOg\n7FG28GiOV+aAcmz+2YCmcIuJ+XyTa+sADjvZjUEONR8UXPm3zu4wNdWhuo5oJsd6\n7PiIAcpnmZ8qjaPGjvNumAy0dDWZur+ArIYR98lHd7QBFPwiSHQkFX8VrANTwr/N\ng1SOTbRLRJMgR3kzPRJcXGsV08TcHgWiKvVXtyq78idPpWintOcjdnEriH9Vol7t\n8mw5QmPLQiF3A0FloAH7QPphnzD0OiSjcOB3AVQQ7mp07W1WpCkt+5xY8xgFYiQG\nVxgnlXtw76G3qbE4B0PU1W97eYgehgMkHfX3HMcebIsEOK2GoB3kAM44OYkHqLlx\nLmHDUJ065v5oK/andAAVMq4nsg5dUnlbKV9cMoxl4XqARCCbFDE7LD5u0u73Yndn\njNx2Tj/ly9pW9PfHekTE\n=zzem\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T06:40:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDEyNzQ4ZGI3ZmU3NDI4NDI5NTVhMGVjMDliNTY1ZDFjNGFkZjczZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012","sha":"a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012"}],"sha":"12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/12748db7fe742842955a0ec09b565d1c4adf73fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:37:17Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:37:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: capture a revisioned block inside a container; record a capture cancelled on stop (#40)\n\nCloses #19, #24, #37.\n\n     node. Publication infos arrive in tree order, so a container was\n     memoised first and a revisioned content node inside it matched the\n     container''s prefix and took the container''s answer -- the enclosing\n     page''s uuid, or \"none\". The block''s own history was never written,\n     with no status and no log line. A node carrying the mixin is now its\n     own owner before the memo is consulted; the memo still spares the walk\n     for everything else.\n     line, so the folder kept the previous STORED and the gap looked like\n     \"no change\". Each scheduled job now remembers what it was to capture,\n     and a cancelled job leaves a durable FAILED status on every page and\n     language, saying to republish. An orderly shutdown deactivates the\n     component first, so a restart is covered by the same path; a crash is\n     not, and cannot be.\n     path now take their collaborators (session; scheduler, status\n     recorder, site resolver) as parameters, and nine tests cover the\n     ownership table and the three cancellation outcomes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"694133411b92dcaed284994b2bd28e2621dcd579","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/694133411b92dcaed284994b2bd28e2621dcd579"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012","verification":{"payload":"tree 694133411b92dcaed284994b2bd28e2621dcd579\nparent 38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788503837 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788503837 +0200\n\nfix: capture a revisioned block inside a container; record a capture cancelled on stop (#40)\n\nCloses #19, #24, #37.\n\n     node. Publication infos arrive in tree order, so a container was\n     memoised first and a revisioned content node inside it matched the\n     container''s prefix and took the container''s answer -- the enclosing\n     page''s uuid, or \"none\". The block''s own history was never written,\n     with no status and no log line. A node carrying the mixin is now its\n     own owner before the memo is consulted; the memo still spares the walk\n     for everything else.\n     line, so the folder kept the previous STORED and the gap looked like\n     \"no change\". Each scheduled job now remembers what it was to capture,\n     and a cancelled job leaves a durable FAILED status on every page and\n     language, saying to republish. An orderly shutdown deactivates the\n     component first, so a restart is covered by the same path; a crash is\n     not, and cannot be.\n     path now take their collaborators (session; scheduler, status\n     recorder, site resolver) as parameters, and nine tests cover the\n     ownership table and the three cancellation outcomes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmmcdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAdcQAD3g9LHCb7DKGPOHBr36a58T\n6SwVhvLUz0U9PKCvSRFW5ixi4XcZ/bSnATktE6FuZb6MTqHNwu2wOFig5Jbp9e7b\nl6947xOj8IbOGRoHTJQqHihp9XkhhLidWZcCD71cKkd4NtmLv0VbJxu/xnEgcQt1\ngMa3ReEYHlDtBqOJtJGWkfNoaKA6T9Gpn/kcRRbKYeLEDOQ6H+DP3IN0SU1Mt2uX\nyf+GjWkORt7SKIrs1oOKFPVgL1ssSpjZEgxegAkYoYlINT0tKlDOpg6HqsVae9me\nh4W6diBT8/yRMlyOvUb2NN+o0qkTfOucAZZBsSCJEK2OFAi+TckDetuvPVNA2gih\nVjSAwEuxJemwuzioOL2xXLOyZ5u/i+wb+7NqCKRTkawY3mRqUdy5CVqsPwPGrEVj\n8/BZlh6xwqh8jg+/ZWrZBPlCbrInfm2IAV6O7zPxGfuRvXEXElHtwMe33NDXOsLS\nLXcqk+ipKB7WLTcptv7Cq0lWOA6896RQRoHLn1g7gTEBzbo4Ed6IZ+YdolSMy1Gk\n30ABCy29ra3Jy97kXXWwzy27q2/uaNrRriN5PHaMpT/5X8AxAJzaR9Q4qIDJsMcf\n15qB/e7ft+99ie1hO5nTFd4l7ImDmwL7QT96dbc6vcEBwTQ1MQH+70xqhDGjDNbs\nOq4NI5bUso5DR1UAW9vL\n=OEU3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T06:37:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGEyNTZkMzQ2YjRmY2M0Mzg2NjgwMDNmNGE0MDA5N2M3NzhkOGYwMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495","sha":"38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495"}],"sha":"a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/a256d346b4fcc438668003f4a40097c778d8f012"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:32:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:32:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: keep the snapshot faithful -- plain text is text, tables/lists/quotes/embeds survive (#39)\n\nCloses #18, #20, #22, #25, #27.\n\n#18  A literal <style>, <script>, <xmp>, <noscript> or <!-- in a plain\n     string property or a title swallowed the rest of the page out of the\n     snapshot: the views printed plain strings raw into a stream parsed as\n     HTML, where those are raw-text/comment elements consuming to EOF, and\n     DANGEROUS_ELEMENTS then removed the tail. Plain strings and titles are\n     now escaped (fn:escapeXml in the views, crh:textProperties for every\n     non-rich-text property); rich text stays raw so it can be converted.\n#20  table.select(\"tr\") was a descendant selector: nested rows rendered\n     once per enclosing level (~4x growth per level, OOM at depth 26,\n     duplicated rows). Rows are read from the table''s own tr/thead/tbody/\n     tfoot children only.\n#22  <li><p>..</p></li> produced a bare hyphen and unindented text. Items\n     render into their own buffer; a second paragraph continues indented.\n#25  blockquote (> per sentence line), iframe/video/audio/object/embed\n     ([embed](src)), caption, header-row separator, hr and ol start are in\n     the record; each used to normalise away, so real changes diffed as\n     identical.\n#27  The normaliser escaped backslashes inside link text only while the\n     viewer treated every backslash as an escape and any ** as a delimiter,\n     so the panel misrepresented the archive. Literal \\ and * are escaped in\n     all text, the viewer honours escapes, and *italic* is rendered.\n\nGENERATOR_VERSION 5 -> 6.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e45b8f3606c4b54db246735df7825667b5e1f7f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/e45b8f3606c4b54db246735df7825667b5e1f7f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495","verification":{"payload":"tree e45b8f3606c4b54db246735df7825667b5e1f7f0\nparent 1aacbbc53d3eedd3a49e05f9708c0b62d43ea93f\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788503527 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788503527 +0200\n\nfix: keep the snapshot faithful -- plain text is text, tables/lists/quotes/embeds survive (#39)\n\nCloses #18, #20, #22, #25, #27.\n\n#18  A literal <style>, <script>, <xmp>, <noscript> or <!-- in a plain\n     string property or a title swallowed the rest of the page out of the\n     snapshot: the views printed plain strings raw into a stream parsed as\n     HTML, where those are raw-text/comment elements consuming to EOF, and\n     DANGEROUS_ELEMENTS then removed the tail. Plain strings and titles are\n     now escaped (fn:escapeXml in the views, crh:textProperties for every\n     non-rich-text property); rich text stays raw so it can be converted.\n#20  table.select(\"tr\") was a descendant selector: nested rows rendered\n     once per enclosing level (~4x growth per level, OOM at depth 26,\n     duplicated rows). Rows are read from the table''s own tr/thead/tbody/\n     tfoot children only.\n#22  <li><p>..</p></li> produced a bare hyphen and unindented text. Items\n     render into their own buffer; a second paragraph continues indented.\n#25  blockquote (> per sentence line), iframe/video/audio/object/embed\n     ([embed](src)), caption, header-row separator, hr and ol start are in\n     the record; each used to normalise away, so real changes diffed as\n     identical.\n#27  The normaliser escaped backslashes inside link text only while the\n     viewer treated every backslash as an escape and any ** as a delimiter,\n     so the panel misrepresented the archive. Literal \\ and * are escaped in\n     all text, the viewer honours escapes, and *italic* is rendered.\n\nGENERATOR_VERSION 5 -> 6.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmmXnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUfwQAIGKb41+5bi2gZwQBUBpF0zZ\nppFho4MjbX+4FKrH0fljVA2QpecY0lFKRuQSosp6E0a8GiT+35o/3T5QwTDIfmSd\n8IQotnBsa7NWnSGnWlGW8HWc78TZvZJDFgW4L023G93H01oDtX65ju8fXKsnVXZ3\n+gPq2HOsLt4s3hcS0TZVQW34p3wgL6+9Q3Jw3UIkfyU8WgugSv0TBKRloKbTVYr2\nmw0+y1DJ8x/3elQyggpn+myox+181vRCdeD88axi/pAi0BalmCyQbxrVt98+wjVk\n11o5BOq7sqw02e4sD/bX9Vj4uVSjF7QbBVBtWxJBJsMUCJTIm4F1P0yIMgjYHF00\nLvRqOKuppz5fGAnG63CSLRipQZAXI4wDoRKVhw8E0jTxa9D22SBzoTRET2T+9E54\n08HOMrJ+jeqIpJSdQJhsTvP8+Yy7pXms03w4nIgURT7iVB8YVfJWp6t06YSXf99n\nNnhL2Q0SnjbH2Qm/YOEDwFVUMJ2Cc3XJGMw8qjg8iBIBm8+Y8h9zTRB/3bQ1g6Q5\nLw/0mpSNvZ5J3FvV2OEPLwd7d6g8WSl6oR/UzUqhR/9FmPi7vQu4PPptQPrOUGpU\nWp/XySNzxaGnRiqvyp8qx37e7uwUVp9oYCg6zIY8Vi7yjMhonLo3ndEU2K0EGUNK\nlXlu1V93pIVNUm5BEChB\n=/u3F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T06:32:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDM4ZDAxYWNjNDVlN2M5ZDY2YjBiOGRhZWZlMGM1NjZiMDk0NGI0OTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/1aacbbc53d3eedd3a49e05f9708c0b62d43ea93f","sha":"1aacbbc53d3eedd3a49e05f9708c0b62d43ea93f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1aacbbc53d3eedd3a49e05f9708c0b62d43ea93f"}],"sha":"38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/38d01acc45e7c9d66b0b8daefe0c566b0944b495"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1aacbbc53d3eedd3a49e05f9708c0b62d43ea93f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:13:59Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:13:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): run the markdown content-type filter before the fragment cache (#38)\n\nThe 1.4.7 fix for GHSA-4hvq-2x8x-49w2 held for one request per cache\nlifetime. MarkdownContentTypeFilter ran at priority 98, and the render\nchain stops at the first filter whose prepare() returns content -- on a\ncache hit that is CacheFilter at 16.5 (legacy AggregateCacheFilter at\n16.0), which applies to the markdown template type in live. So the\ntext/plain + nosniff headers were set on the cache miss only; every\nfollowing anonymous request was served as text/html with the unescaped\nbody. Measured on 8.2.3.2 with 1.4.7: request 1 text/plain, requests 2\nand 3 text/html.\n\nThe filter now runs at 5, ahead of every filter that can end the chain\nearly, MarkedForDeletionFilter (10) included.\n\nTests: the unit test pinned the wrong bound (< 99, TemplateScriptFilter);\nit now pins < 16 and < 10 with the reason. The Cypress spec made four\nsingle fetches, none positioned to see a warm-cache response, and used a\n?v= cache-buster that does not vary the anonymous fragment key; it now\nasserts the headers on a sequence of byte-identical requests after the\npublication''s asynchronous flush has settled.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9333a399bb87d71c0db4385a9428c92bab59917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/a9333a399bb87d71c0db4385a9428c92bab59917"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/1aacbbc53d3eedd3a49e05f9708c0b62d43ea93f","verification":{"payload":"tree a9333a399bb87d71c0db4385a9428c92bab59917\nparent fe8d8b4c5678270f6b1e5237f566e9963e884880\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788502439 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788502439 +0200\n\nfix(security): run the markdown content-type filter before the fragment cache (#38)\n\nThe 1.4.7 fix for GHSA-4hvq-2x8x-49w2 held for one request per cache\nlifetime. MarkdownContentTypeFilter ran at priority 98, and the render\nchain stops at the first filter whose prepare() returns content -- on a\ncache hit that is CacheFilter at 16.5 (legacy AggregateCacheFilter at\n16.0), which applies to the markdown template type in live. So the\ntext/plain + nosniff headers were set on the cache miss only; every\nfollowing anonymous request was served as text/html with the unescaped\nbody. Measured on 8.2.3.2 with 1.4.7: request 1 text/plain, requests 2\nand 3 text/html.\n\nThe filter now runs at 5, ahead of every filter that can end the chain\nearly, MarkedForDeletionFilter (10) included.\n\nTests: the unit test pinned the wrong bound (< 99, TemplateScriptFilter);\nit now pins < 16 and < 10 with the reason. The Cypress spec made four\nsingle fetches, none positioned to see a warm-cache response, and used a\n?v= cache-buster that does not vary the anonymous fragment key; it now\nasserts the headers on a sequence of byte-identical requests after the\npublication''s asynchronous flush has settled.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmmGnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc10QAH9Z6TZfjXXXZVlVoJ+Ntxfd\nJ8A8ZyCo/WQ9pPWBumKBewMiQmaOEZI2RPv3HpQWvaBeCcI1MGCzsttnv/k9xJ8E\n8/4dM8AqIH8mEftu+vgbe8f5i1PS1lkquM/0oyI6Zftk0AU5AWwXWySzWnGjFTK6\nlkKWMX8Cra3zcjHGMrt9eFBG9EC32ZzIVXscr0Ps3vNzaVMZ13JUXApqOF42TEQh\n1gZnUPB3cWkGXVnszqVz9RWwc/02Qo3T+arN7838il6DHJzS8jexh6U1nFe4Cdrm\nTkYTX3O9RfONa7dK9B/dgVg1fmir8qVMfxe6pKQMjOCTGOLBgTR14onzLEkdND5x\n6n3iSEDfe2P+WLZPfuFe0ol4U51EUOjf+Sl45ZDx0WcMHB3mzfJw/IAwDQy+XUxW\npm+ObkA26qZfZLGvaTx7923FbARSwXXF+t7Ogro38HjT/UwvcwITUE5FmKNtsZcm\nOgi4qjUSZGcL6lVi2Uo/+vx0Hosp9XwmREJpa+A5