tar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/d3411150fc3b5b05c35413cfdb753ea316ceb209","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGQzNDExMTUwZmMzYjViMDVjMzU0MTNjZmRiNzUzZWEzMTZjZWIyMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/853e66623f5b8b52a60156d53d6d57cc283b0c2b","sha":"853e66623f5b8b52a60156d53d6d57cc283b0c2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/853e66623f5b8b52a60156d53d6d57cc283b0c2b"}],"sha":"d3411150fc3b5b05c35413cfdb753ea316ceb209","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/d3411150fc3b5b05c35413cfdb753ea316ceb209"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/853e66623f5b8b52a60156d53d6d57cc283b0c2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T05:32:14Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T05:32:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(diff): authorise the viewer in the workspace being rendered (#15)\n\nComparing two revisions answered ''One of the selected revisions is not\npart of this history.'' for anyone not logged in, on entirely public content.\n\nThe permission gate asked JCRSessionFactory.getCurrentUserSession(), which\nresolves the current USER from the thread but hard-defaults the WORKSPACE to\n''default'' (verified in the 8.2.3.2 bytecode). So a visitor was asked whether\nthey could read the history in the EDIT workspace, and Jahia does not grant\njcr:read_default to guest -- the answer was always no. Editors passed the\nsame gate, which is why it survived review and testing as root. The\nworkspace now comes from the view''s own renderContext.\n\nTwo further consequences of the same root cause, also fixed:\nrenderingWorkspace() could never return ''live'' except by throwing, so a live\nvisitor''s comparison described DRAFT entries and now describes published\nones; and snapshotsFor()''s page-level gate had the identical defect, failing\nmore quietly as an empty panel.\n\nEvery Cypress spec logs in first and cy.request carries the session cookie,\nso 34 tests asserting the public surface ran as root. The two new tests\ncompare as a genuine guest and prove they are one by asserting the edit\nworkspace refuses them first.","tree":{"sha":"0d2bbff9804284bd3088ade93289281e22684c79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/0d2bbff9804284bd3088ade93289281e22684c79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/853e66623f5b8b52a60156d53d6d57cc283b0c2b","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d2bbff9804284bd3088ade93289281e22684c79\nparent 170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788413534 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788413534 +0200\n\nfix(diff): authorise the viewer in the workspace being rendered (#15)\n\nComparing two revisions answered ''One of the selected revisions is not\npart of this history.'' for anyone not logged in, on entirely public content.\n\nThe permission gate asked JCRSessionFactory.getCurrentUserSession(), which\nresolves the current USER from the thread but hard-defaults the WORKSPACE to\n''default'' (verified in the 8.2.3.2 bytecode). So a visitor was asked whether\nthey could read the history in the EDIT workspace, and Jahia does not grant\njcr:read_default to guest -- the answer was always no. Editors passed the\nsame gate, which is why it survived review and testing as root. The\nworkspace now comes from the view''s own renderContext.\n\nTwo further consequences of the same root cause, also fixed:\nrenderingWorkspace() could never return ''live'' except by throwing, so a live\nvisitor''s comparison described DRAFT entries and now describes published\nones; and snapshotsFor()''s page-level gate had the identical defect, failing\nmore quietly as an empty panel.\n\nEvery Cypress spec logs in first and cy.request carries the session cookie,\nso 34 tests asserting the public surface ran as root. The two new tests\ncompare as a genuine guest and prove they are one by asserting the edit\nworkspace refuses them first.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmQZeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArPkQABOemI5tjZzbCUQf4ysIp/an\n/V0SE6XK0FdCIxkj1tXe8xS/P3MCOR0pvE+tUNQ3ClGaOih9RoAcK+P2cfWMKPig\n7IQGFLPOcN0grIt9Q1ra3+L1bdzuB4s/q/4jCuV2wu0Nu17qzxx1FQFXwxfYmhfT\nBCAg4thOvtZcqea/l3p0evRFo8VC6782uRchJqK1zHU6XVWtE6WC4jTiWsphkve0\noJg6VoshuVo59BxN7a5H2AU/+nTb6wZ3hsm7//bBblhumPBydDF2XC7PbFfSZkxf\nHzcOmiW4XGi7nmOOF9IcaoM/vdz+6Cy3mH7vYAdyctDJLyDFZivyF3qPPzyA8iST\ngFmtNfUgBkAOtZoQVs0mA6V8TNmbGW9oWHvzixzNJoe5uaDptRzRnfzprUDGxMv8\nnTaJOlb6VD58Sh7ZjuMkN20gWaJpF0wP2iWwRe6+tsrVes4olRZY/wVihK5VNG9O\n7n+RRMRaIW7qoRx36YzZTGcgxTvCPclAYPP6LmIsfDdZvjpO3nHguLbCSrsTAcqA\nv1v79ELcjBgeMWKLBz01UIBTh9XB5DGbABrV4AXYVnVSfNVbZvcMeoJfqawwup8p\nJPNoLovGG5crZrNveo8cNNUVcUWsp6XyaHtlbpwhkxYxVBjT1bIELyno11KletIZ\nSBS2iwuaqLP5oSmShu9C\n=v3f8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T05:32:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/853e66623f5b8b52a60156d53d6d57cc283b0c2b","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDg1M2U2NjYyM2Y1YjhiNTJhNjAxNTZkNTNkNmQ1N2NjMjgzYjBjMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64","sha":"170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64"}],"sha":"853e66623f5b8b52a60156d53d6d57cc283b0c2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/853e66623f5b8b52a60156d53d6d57cc283b0c2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T05:31:31Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T05:31:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(backfill): reconstruct a content node through its own view (#16)\n\nTwo defects reported from real Academy content.\n\nAn empty jmix:list no longer aborts the run: the empty-body guard could not\ntell a legitimately empty container from silent content loss, so an empty\nlist that existed at the target revision now emits its separator and is\nskipped.\n\nA content node is no longer reconstructed as though it were a page. A\njacademy:kbEntry keeps its body in the i18n ''answer'' property ON the node,\nwhich a child walk never sees, so the snapshot held only the title -- and a\ncomparison against it would have reported the whole body as removed.\nreconstruct() now mirrors the three markdown views: jnt:page composes\nheading-then-areas, a SELF_RENDERING type is fetched directly, and anything\nelse emits its own title, its own text properties, then its children.\n\nKnown gap, recorded rather than hidden: nothing in the suite exercises the\nempty-container branch.","tree":{"sha":"fda3b244a82ecc76a02ce21144f0b4a5f5be42eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/fda3b244a82ecc76a02ce21144f0b4a5f5be42eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64","verification":{"payload":"tree fda3b244a82ecc76a02ce21144f0b4a5f5be42eb\nparent 6c705671eaac4ad914d2fbe8808ca1b31cc412ad\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788413491 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788413491 +0200\n\nfix(backfill): reconstruct a content node through its own view (#16)\n\nTwo defects reported from real Academy content.\n\nAn empty jmix:list no longer aborts the run: the empty-body guard could not\ntell a legitimately empty container from silent content loss, so an empty\nlist that existed at the target revision now emits its separator and is\nskipped.\n\nA content node is no longer reconstructed as though it were a page. A\njacademy:kbEntry keeps its body in the i18n ''answer'' property ON the node,\nwhich a child walk never sees, so the snapshot held only the title -- and a\ncomparison against it would have reported the whole body as removed.\nreconstruct() now mirrors the three markdown views: jnt:page composes\nheading-then-areas, a SELF_RENDERING type is fetched directly, and anything\nelse emits its own title, its own text properties, then its children.\n\nKnown gap, recorded rather than hidden: nothing in the suite exercises the\nempty-container branch.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmQYzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0C0QAF1ghT/7UbeFIKPPrgIWKp3K\nnjD8kJ0cffmeggs3Ka4bBgw0mbiiQYSwD9XNFL+6f7GImiWxj3RBwpUIQLYIBCKw\nDz4QZugtXOt/V4JgdBiiqgjEAP5xnP+y3JdNvCfBL/HaEN1whGye8Ukj0gVcrvJA\nlmjf5k5E3BATTnZtF68D5U1RBfkiHvwfHFYbleR43+N1azB3KKkFIzA5y7L0Mz1w\n2YjV0MVkZTx/gC/y5OrP1+j8ZW2xT8LKxt+2/2ecxSDfDboPaqfC1NQIeB6ieeFx\nO6AHZVfY8XH/pnpcn1YG2E/QZLgDt7ixwI6MUoeLvHhnaTzmbGp/dTEmeX5HQax7\nsnSLKbNJKw9ndbTTDs0PX0Gj1EAjfG99ftCqwYih90v66A/1sfZbfOMLXPGvwuzL\ngp8SO3oLOIKfkapmYHe82Xjgwisq0V+hJyzmgXJiYeIHDIlj81PDSNoETAU5LEoW\nkC9SKYTyNxz1OE1X2xcF7BT6JtanMhUvTON7bpRaRr97qJwbFfAsU6nd+D7nJV4m\nqc23eum4Y60PEZFd001mYrMolfcobpWKXThn4CvNEq5PDbLctKy2wq71+n0TytGo\nob9e/GyD/xc/YY/Hp+ffoNoPPuAyyXAX2TmDhaR/+oI3x1cAZ7cTdrk0oT8rNNr6\nV7BOPLw6MM/PfQBMcOpU\n=cSP3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T05:31:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDE3MGQ0MGNmYTlhNjMyYTEwM2U3ZGU0YWEzM2I3MzNjMjJmM2JhNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/6c705671eaac4ad914d2fbe8808ca1b31cc412ad","sha":"6c705671eaac4ad914d2fbe8808ca1b31cc412ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6c705671eaac4ad914d2fbe8808ca1b31cc412ad"}],"sha":"170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/170d40cfa9a632a103e7de4aa33b733c22f3ba64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6c705671eaac4ad914d2fbe8808ca1b31cc412ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T14:44:26Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T14:44:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(model): file the components under a real category, not \"base\" (#14)\n\n* feat(model): file the components under a real category, not \"base\"\n\nBoth component types now carry jmix:structuredContent.\n\nCorrects a factual error I shipped in the 1.4.5 release notes as well. That note\nsaid a type with no category mixin \"does not appear in a GENERIC add-content\nlist\". It does appear: contentTypesAsTree is a tree whose branches are the\ncategory mixins, and a type carrying none lands in the default nt:base branch,\nlabelled simply \"base\". Findable, merely filed badly. The CHANGELOG entry and the\npublished GitHub release notes for 1.4.5 are both corrected, since leaving a\nfalse claim in a release is worse than the error itself.\n\nContent:Structured is where jnt:banner, jnt:event and jnt:introduction live --\npurpose-built editorial components, which is what these are. Not jmix:listContent\n(\"Jahia - Lists\"), which holds generic containers like jnt:contentList: a\nrevision history is a list in its mechanics and a component in its purpose, and\nthe picker groups by purpose.\n\ncrh:revisionEntry is categorised too, so the \"base\" branch disappears from the\npicker rather than lingering with one entry in it. Functionally that changes\nnothing -- an entry is only ever legal inside a crh:revisionHistory, whose child\ndefinition names the type explicitly, and the picker filters by allowed child\ntypes before it consults the category.\n\ncrh:revisionSnapshot and crh:snapshotFolder are deliberately left alone: they are\nwritten by capture and must not be creatable by an editor, and they were already\nabsent from the picker.\n\nMeasured on 8.2.4.0 rather than assumed: adding a supertype is not a MAJOR\ndefinition change (\"Adding content-revision-history definitions, updating\ndatabase cnd\"), both types move to Content:Structured, and the nt:base branch is\ngone.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore: set the development version to 1.4.6-SNAPSHOT\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2070a2c564f44857a0b5cae18128606232ff2876","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/2070a2c564f44857a0b5cae18128606232ff2876"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/6c705671eaac4ad914d2fbe8808ca1b31cc412ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 2070a2c564f44857a0b5cae18128606232ff2876\nparent bbe7d5daf6bd11313b0ad952712836b3bc1627b5\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788360266 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788360266 +0200\n\nfeat(model): file the components under a real category, not \"base\" (#14)\n\n* feat(model): file the components under a real category, not \"base\"\n\nBoth component types now carry jmix:structuredContent.\n\nCorrects a factual error I shipped in the 1.4.5 release notes as well. That note\nsaid a type with no category mixin \"does not appear in a GENERIC add-content\nlist\". It does appear: contentTypesAsTree is a tree whose branches are the\ncategory mixins, and a type carrying none lands in the default nt:base branch,\nlabelled simply \"base\". Findable, merely filed badly. The CHANGELOG entry and the\npublished GitHub release notes for 1.4.5 are both corrected, since leaving a\nfalse claim in a release is worse than the error itself.\n\nContent:Structured is where jnt:banner, jnt:event and jnt:introduction live --\npurpose-built editorial components, which is what these are. Not jmix:listContent\n(\"Jahia - Lists\"), which holds generic containers like jnt:contentList: a\nrevision history is a list in its mechanics and a component in its purpose, and\nthe picker groups by purpose.\n\ncrh:revisionEntry is categorised too, so the \"base\" branch disappears from the\npicker rather than lingering with one entry in it. Functionally that changes\nnothing -- an entry is only ever legal inside a crh:revisionHistory, whose child\ndefinition names the type explicitly, and the picker filters by allowed child\ntypes before it consults the category.\n\ncrh:revisionSnapshot and crh:snapshotFolder are deliberately left alone: they are\nwritten by capture and must not be creatable by an editor, and they were already\nabsent from the picker.\n\nMeasured on 8.2.4.0 rather than assumed: adding a supertype is not a MAJOR\ndefinition change (\"Adding content-revision-history definitions, updating\ndatabase cnd\"), both types move to Content:Structured, and the nt:base branch is\ngone.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore: set the development version to 1.4.6-SNAPSHOT\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmDZKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiZMQAGIPc10QE2NX9lRWoFfMSM2N\nV31ML9vSgi7z50xdyEaXOH9z4dPd7KH2F8mslmIIQs7//6gfrarXk2bnZL/SJofA\n3c42snjuLPAliDVsbZT+gRtW5dpHCobKIec0Drj8FaoYfgySAxOARgjrAaIobPHe\nMeopOf1MdzM2YP/v5doVuFPCdf0QKezTkxX1P3jV5npaiMgBYgcCNEQA72whH9lx\nuXNPob9yoNJBKgeMXns7+W8Mgcnkt60ioP0bq9i3uzI8iWdUkXfwh/rImkDh7KyB\neYj8qynXevqb43hqZ0y6EweYU2jqp2QGeLMHEG7+g7q/nse6X4D/MCDPNivBXmeo\nTAYhrishB8Oizv+8O1y2lz9/90X8nP9PGvg9rXjm7lGMZp45x4XsT7b7kgZCQlDE\nImmxq9dt78fiNOykLhnoIFr/BguUDhUAUcX/yoZa0tqjG4XRMRBmXCurizMHvCl2\n8+jWeqfTCbLgNTicNKQrgKx7RBuiZZIh1/3P/n3twFtM8sNDukwhucuxlUXnWtLj\n0ec/XnT43Ncyjc9kXYwWbpljp0AFk5/i/+IsEUW4jCYsnvJmuGpCa9otVZW25yll\nY2FRElbkmB1hyrBm6c4vFRJg43bxr0FDGnxWMLwhEDTUlFWtYolekRRzIhpTBYBj\nCMNNm/JMFprOnIwq2dsO\n=6ljH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T14:44:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"ht