s/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/199aea38af56f01401c9a6bbf06e6cf18ddb772c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/dc67332735220967bf39cb9880194e4624ff9a39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:22:58Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:22:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: let a host view actually create the revision history slot (#13)\n\nReported from a jacademy:kbEntry: with the slot typed as the component itself,\nedit mode showed no add button at all.\n\ntemplate:area creates its area node as a jnt:contentList, and a slot typed\n(crh:revisionHistory) rejects a list -- so the area node could never come into\nexistence, nothing was creatable, and edit mode offered nothing. The previous\nattempt, template:module path=\"*\", failed differently: `path` INCLUDES a node\nrather than creating one, so it rendered a generic drop zone and left Jahia to\ngenerate the child''s name, which no definition on that type matched.\n\n(jmix:droppableContent) mirrors the `relatedlinks` definition on\njacademy:kbEntry, which is a pattern working in production rather than one\nreasoned out from the taglib documentation. The area node is the list; the\ncomponent goes inside it, constrained by the view''s own nodeTypes. Confirmed\nworking on a real kbEntry by the reporter.\n\nMeasured on 8.2.4.0 rather than assumed:\n  - widening a child definition''s required type is NOT a MAJOR change\n    (\"Adding content-revision-history definitions, updating database cnd\")\n  - a jnt:contentList can be created in the widened slot, which is exactly what\n    template:area does\n  - contentTypesAsTree -- the API Content Editor builds its add list from --\n    offers crh:revisionHistory inside that list, so the button appears\n\nThe cost, stated because it is a real loss: the list can hold more than one\nrevision history. The host view''s nodeTypes keeps them to histories, but nothing\nat the definition level now says \"exactly one\", which the typed slot did say and\ncould not deliver.\n\nAlso worth recording for the next person: crh:revisionHistory carries no\ncategory mixin (jmix:basicContent and friends), so it never appears in a GENERIC\nadd-content list -- contentTypesAsTree groups by category and a type with none\nhas no branch to sit under. It is only offerable where a view names it\nexplicitly via nodeTypes. Every e2e test creates it over GraphQL, which bypasses\nthe picker entirely, so nothing here exercises the path an editor uses.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"56b6428aa932bd7f9fadaf5744972420b2e1e8c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/56b6428aa932bd7f9fadaf5744972420b2e1e8c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/dc67332735220967bf39cb9880194e4624ff9a39","verification":{"payload":"tree 56b6428aa932bd7f9fadaf5744972420b2e1e8c7\nparent fddb31e220cce6f303236d4eec2d2e11cfcc4410\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788355378 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788355378 +0200\n\nfix: let a host view actually create the revision history slot (#13)\n\nReported from a jacademy:kbEntry: with the slot typed as the component itself,\nedit mode showed no add button at all.\n\ntemplate:area creates its area node as a jnt:contentList, and a slot typed\n(crh:revisionHistory) rejects a list -- so the area node could never come into\nexistence, nothing was creatable, and edit mode offered nothing. The previous\nattempt, template:module path=\"*\", failed differently: `path` INCLUDES a node\nrather than creating one, so it rendered a generic drop zone and left Jahia to\ngenerate the child''s name, which no definition on that type matched.\n\n(jmix:droppableContent) mirrors the `relatedlinks` definition on\njacademy:kbEntry, which is a pattern working in production rather than one\nreasoned out from the taglib documentation. The area node is the list; the\ncomponent goes inside it, constrained by the view''s own nodeTypes. Confirmed\nworking on a real kbEntry by the reporter.\n\nMeasured on 8.2.4.0 rather than assumed:\n  - widening a child definition''s required type is NOT a MAJOR change\n    (\"Adding content-revision-history definitions, updating database cnd\")\n  - a jnt:contentList can be created in the widened slot, which is exactly what\n    template:area does\n  - contentTypesAsTree -- the API Content Editor builds its add list from --\n    offers crh:revisionHistory inside that list, so the button appears\n\nThe cost, stated because it is a real loss: the list can hold more than one\nrevision history. The host view''s nodeTypes keeps them to histories, but nothing\nat the definition level now says \"exactly one\", which the typed slot did say and\ncould not deliver.\n\nAlso worth recording for the next person: crh:revisionHistory carries no\ncategory mixin (jmix:basicContent and friends), so it never appears in a GENERIC\nadd-content list -- contentTypesAsTree groups by category and a type with none\nhas no branch to sit under. It is only offerable where a view names it\nexplicitly via nodeTypes. Every e2e test creates it over GraphQL, which bypasses\nthe picker entirely, so nothing here exercises the path an editor uses.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmCMyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZFMQAHBY96UHzOvz+43YWeFFQSge\ncFNAiGOG/YyJv4YFNp0t1D2KnZAF24IIM6n6XDVTJbCsdX9h2epQEQWusLCeQzoM\n1+MX92Na4VVaBoX9QMExKSZ4j10PRTAg6Z6Hyh4oTdcgBufBz8dv7jGhGFfE6/px\nYqiLfJisLB4OwDI1I5ZKZvgCMSScyi9BTwe/X0T2QaUgmDXwE9nkPkkPCG2Rq8Ox\nR7Tuzi/+p6JTlO9KdKlhHy8mPK8L1ODXG4ozeuq8onL6wjtRtyzWPX/IbUCOcL/y\n5WvqRidlNklFkRs03VWHsdCeaq4v3pzgwCzBkUYQLxEFhzO7IPLyfZZZVDtglFJi\nwzruMhYBR9PWEezqYkazxN4DUJ6a0MbwIeBSLWW01M5vb3egkbaQdQsSu8SFMgxC\njJDxczaNnJGp4vHf+9HbLsp4+tyzSmCIBw+NubzENA7qyzD3o7xPmz7SyFW0ws+Z\n/Slgn3idY54VZ+GsjDoGgbfIDH0zbsgmryr9eBaxDy9sGA4m9w26mkc7U8Xvpyek\nUqkLc4Jidd5jwM2QOpLjrk+SkYySGMamIampE206nilqgX6cSQ8Mqwgi6MwTwdEo\nh6q4J/wnEXerlQ/OaX8qZxaH2XK/cf1IR5kAgoi4ObKRGHUEh+ovuHikymsEWHgb\n6x3AS6SRe8Dc6IHYJa3L\n=ybh8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T13:22:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/user