:"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/b73a6891a03f33d9d13df30988bc49bfb9db1390","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGI3M2E2ODkxYTAzZjMzZDlkMTNkZjMwOTg4YmM0OWJmYjlkYjEzOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/94880cca6074f5487eced8d08f7b375ea7ae6c2c","sha":"94880cca6074f5487eced8d08f7b375ea7ae6c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/94880cca6074f5487eced8d08f7b375ea7ae6c2c"}],"sha":"b73a6891a03f33d9d13df30988bc49bfb9db1390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/b73a6891a03f33d9d13df30988bc49bfb9db1390"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/94880cca6074f5487eced8d08f7b375ea7ae6c2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:36:03Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:36:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: give a revisioned node a legal place for its revision history (#12)\n\njmix:publiclyRevisioned now carries the slot as well as the marker:\n\n    + revisionHistory (crh:revisionHistory)\n\nTicking \"Public revision history\" is what should make it possible to put the\nlist on the node, and until now it was not. A page has wildcard areas, so the\ncomponent can simply be dropped into one; a structured content type usually\ncannot. jacademy:kbEntry declares exactly one named child (relatedlinks) and no\nwildcard, so there was no legal place for the list inside it -- the type could be\nrevisioned and still have nowhere to render its own history.\n\nIt has to be INSIDE the revisioned node, which is why this is a slot rather than\nadvice about placement: RevisionedAncestor walks UP from the component to find\nits owner and stops at the first page, so a history sitting in a page area beside\na revisioned content node resolves to no owner and reports \"no snapshot recorded\"\npermanently.\n\nDeclared here rather than in each consuming module on purpose. The alternative\nwas for every module owning a revisionable type to add the child definition\nitself, which makes that module refuse to start unless this one is deployed -- a\nhard dependency for one optional feature on one content type. This way a consumer\nneeds no change to its CND and no jahia-depends entry.\n\nSingle and named, not `+ * (crh:revisionHistory)`: one node has one authoritative\npublic revision history, and a wildcard would let an editor create several with\nnothing to say which one counts.\n\nNo conflict with content that already exists, verified rather than reasoned\nabout. An optional child definition that is not mandatory, autocreated or\nprotected can only permit more. On one revisioned page, with this deployed, all\nthree placements were accepted together: a history in a page area (the shape\nevery existing install has), a direct child named exactly revisionHistory, and a\ndirect child under the page''s own wildcard. Publishing that page then captured\nnormally and the binder bound entries from two different histories to the same\nsnapshot, which is correct -- they are all entries about that node.\n\nThe e2e test asserts both halves. The negative control is the important one:\nwithout the mixin the same mutation fails with \"No child node definition for\nrevisionHistory\", so the test cannot pass because some parent happened to allow\nany child.\n\n95 -> 96 end-to-end tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2371faadd462e13fdd04502f5ea375fee8b3c5fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/2371faadd462e13fdd04502f5ea375fee8b3c5fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/94880cca6074f5487eced8d08f7b375ea7ae6c2c","verification":{"payload":"tree 2371faadd462e13fdd04502f5ea375fee8b3c5fa\nparent 3df3458f35e5f26e65e34b95a1fe8bd5bb07d76a\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788352563 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788352563 +0200\n\nfeat: give a revisioned node a legal place for its revision history (#12)\n\njmix:publiclyRevisioned now carries the slot as well as the marker:\n\n    + revisionHistory (crh:revisionHistory)\n\nTicking \"Public revision history\" is what should make it possible to put the\nlist on the node, and until now it was not. A page has wildcard areas, so the\ncomponent can simply be dropped into one; a structured content type usually\ncannot. jacademy:kbEntry declares exactly one named child (relatedlinks) and no\nwildcard, so there was no legal place for the list inside it -- the type could be\nrevisioned and still have nowhere to render its own history.\n\nIt has to be INSIDE the revisioned node, which is why this is a slot rather than\nadvice about placement: RevisionedAncestor walks UP from the component to find\nits owner and stops at the first page, so a history sitting in a page area beside\na revisioned content node resolves to no owner and reports \"no snapshot recorded\"\npermanently.\n\nDeclared here rather than in each consuming module on purpose. The alternative\nwas for every module owning a revisionable type to add the child definition\nitself, which makes that module refuse to start unless this one is deployed -- a\nhard dependency for one optional feature on one content type. This way a consumer\nneeds no change to its CND and no jahia-depends entry.\n\nSingle and named, not `+ * (crh:revisionHistory)`: one node has one authoritative\npublic revision history, and a wildcard would let an editor create several with\nnothing to say which one counts.\n\nNo conflict with content that already exists, verified rather than reasoned\nabout. An optional child definition that is not mandatory, autocreated or\nprotected can only permit more. On one revisioned page, with this deployed, all\nthree placements were accepted together: a history in a page area (the shape\nevery existing install has), a direct child named exactly revisionHistory, and a\ndirect child under the page''s own wildcard. Publishing that page then captured\nnormally and the binder bound entries from two different histories to the same\nsnapshot, which is correct -- they are all entries about that node.\n\nThe e2e test asserts both halves. The negative control is the important one:\nwithout the mixin the same mutation fails with \"No child node definition for\nrevisionHistory\", so the test cannot pass because some parent happened to allow\nany child.\n\n95 -> 96 end-to-end tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmBgzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUjsQABdoUhBUnDbJCVj5bQe2irYk\nXPh4ab51eJ7X1ES6vObMoLWXCZCgBSgJpJAF3JEKIb9TZsdKXmFyS4HvhFUIngoy\nTamMh3VpSenCVsGLM+19fbmEfyTkowAYVstooP3l51Dx5/FfVtFMCILo/ZD1JriW\nVJWcSwI7jOr55kZ9K9I6kU+zOlTX13uROJecWp2OCLIfDMQe9haqf2y+D5iVIz2K\nHEl6e0Cr59Wi3JTmMraXMqore80wsxN9bScdccVRpjIO5NmZpOOeWi9v/wR+dvO5\nQf2+H7reDjWdJynjqNHpkV6MHbqT6ZSz9TAagvbmJ+/6qosufBh3PS3XCOfHnSIP\npfLxsaujUw/iaAfTsV/bPNKe1BdHrEW6H6uBKXil9qSyj1ToEl59sLbe5CyRJF8Q\nNmVjzno2380UAy/64zkpmdEKb/Ze8mEQkVPXUoL/clF67N0mKOW/hXD5EfQ9Rpwr\nODsPV14ZT/QdXKgziHBc4sauQuL+plwZt46OCE5tTy0AgDeWO3Z80hz3UC1x8CHC\nJzBz0FYKHYdvyKpTPwQTMjrO5iA1kQ/Fo2fHG8GloPTzIdMPWVziNNWkylQFUnA4\nzPuBqTY6xJs+w/ij/YmLcx8X8CcfGuCrRZkYGatbKd7Ek+E/7DtGI0YR5J/hUB54\n6FX4BFoPhmCCdBUGRbV4\n=i+VG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:36:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/94880cca6074f5487eced8d08f7b375ea7ae6c2c","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDk0ODgwY2NhNjA3NGY1NDg3ZWNlZDhkMDhmN2IzNzVlYTdhZTZjMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/3df3458f35e5f26e65e34b95a1fe8bd5bb07d76a","sha":"3df3458f35e5f26e65e34b95a1fe8bd5bb07d76a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/3df3458f35e5f26e65e34b95a1fe8bd5bb07d76a"}],"sha":"94880cca6074f5487eced8d08f7b375ea7ae6c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/94880cca6074f5487eced8d08f7b375ea7ae6c2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/3df3458f35e5f26e65e34b95a1fe8bd5bb07d76a/comments","commit":{"