rs/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/bd3a81adc98ad20669800079956cf89f499cc5bc","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGJkM2E4MWFkYzk4YWQyMDY2OTgwMDA3OTk1NmNmODlmNDk5Y2M1YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/d67c4d5f7e77182677f2f828b5ea58043b8efa49","sha":"d67c4d5f7e77182677f2f828b5ea58043b8efa49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/d67c4d5f7e77182677f2f828b5ea58043b8efa49"}],"sha":"bd3a81adc98ad20669800079956cf89f499cc5bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/bd3a81adc98ad20669800079956cf89f499cc5bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/d67c4d5f7e77182677f2f828b5ea58043b8efa49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:08:39Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:08:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: revision content that is published without a page of its own (#11)\n\njmix:publiclyRevisioned now extends jnt:content as well as jnt:page, so a policy\nblock reused across pages, or any component with its own editorial lifecycle,\ngets a revision history on the same terms. Nothing in the storage was ever\npage-shaped: the folder is keyed on the marked node''s UUID.\n\nWidening the mixin was NOT enough, and the way it failed is why most of this\ncommit is not the CND line. The walk that answers \"which node owns this history\"\nasked \"am I a page?\" BEFORE \"am I revisioned?\", so a revisioned content node was\nadded to the visited list and walked straight past. Content published outside any\npage then resolved to no owner and was never captured -- and resolving to no\nowner is also the correct answer for content nobody asked to revision, so there\nwas nothing to see: no error, no status, no folder. Found by publishing such a\nnode against a running 8.2.4.0 and watching nothing happen, not by reading.\n\nThat question was answered in THREE places and two answered it differently: the\nlistener walked pages-then-mixin, while the comparison service and the snapshot\npicker walked to the nearest jnt:page and never consulted the mixin at all.\nIndistinguishable while pages were the only revisionable thing; with the mixin\nwidened, capture would key snapshots on the content node while the comparison\nlooked for them under the enclosing page, and every comparison would report \"no\nsnapshot recorded\" for a history whose snapshots exist and are correct. All three\nnow go through RevisionedAncestor, which checks the mixin first.\n\nTwo behaviours preserved on purpose:\n  - A page that is NOT revisioned still ends the search. A page owns its own\n    content, so its children do not belong to a history above it.\n  - The NEAREST owner wins, so a revisioned block inside a revisioned page keeps\n    its own history rather than being folded into the page''s text.\n\nREVISIONED_PAGE_MIXIN is renamed REVISIONED_MIXIN: the name had become a lie, and\nit is the central concept of the module.\n\nVerified on a running instance rather than argued: the CND change deploys with no\nMAJOR-change refusal (unlike an i18n flag, which Jahia rejects outright), the\nmixin applies to a jnt:bigText under /sites/<site>/contents, and publishing it\nstores a snapshot keyed on its own UUID with status STORED and generator 5.\n\nMutation-verified: restoring the pages-then-mixin order fails exactly the two\ntests that state the consequences --\n\n    revisionedContentOwnsItself: expected <mock> but was <null>\n    nearestOwnerWins:            returned the page, not the block\n\n257 -> 265 unit tests, 94 -> 95 end-to-end. The pre-existing test that a\ndeeply-nested non-page node maps to its owning page still passes, which is what\nproves widening the mixin did not change how pages resolve.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1f9d7704fa9e9be77ae17e18083be5acdc28b52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/e1f9d7704fa9e9be77ae17e18083be5acdc28b52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/d67c4d5f7e77182677f2f828b5ea58043b8efa49","verification":{"payload":"tree e1f9d7704fa9e9be77ae17e18083be5acdc28b52\nparent 53c8b7ef07e7e2037dbce778a1b1a8015efbdfd4\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788347319 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788347319 +0200\n\nfeat: revision content that is published without a page of its own (#11)\n\njmix:publiclyRevisioned now extends jnt:content as well as jnt:page, so a policy\nblock reused across pages, or any component with its own editorial lifecycle,\ngets a revision history on the same terms. Nothing in the storage was ever\npage-shaped: the folder is keyed on the marked node''s UUID.\n\nWidening the mixin was NOT enough, and the way it failed is why most of this\ncommit is not the CND line. The walk that answers \"which node owns this history\"\nasked \"am I a page?\" BEFORE \"am I revisioned?\", so a revisioned content node was\nadded to the visited list and walked straight past. Content published outside any\npage then resolved to no owner and was never captured -- and resolving to no\nowner is also the correct answer for content nobody asked to revision, so there\nwas nothing to see: no error, no status, no folder. Found by publishing such a\nnode against a running 8.2.4.0 and watching nothing happen, not by reading.\n\nThat question was answered in THREE places and two answered it differently: the\nlistener walked pages-then-mixin, while the comparison service and the snapshot\npicker walked to the nearest jnt:page and never consulted the mixin at all.\nIndistinguishable while pages were the only revisionable thing; with the mixin\nwidened, capture would key snapshots on the content node while the comparison\nlooked for them under the enclosing page, and every comparison would report \"no\nsnapshot recorded\" for a history whose snapshots exist and are correct. All three\nnow go through RevisionedAncestor, which checks the mixin first.\n\nTwo behaviours preserved on purpose:\n  - A page that is NOT revisioned still ends the search. A page owns its own\n    content, so its children do not belong to a history above it.\n  - The NEAREST owner wins, so a revisioned block inside a revisioned page keeps\n    its own history rather than being folded into the page''s text.\n\nREVISIONED_PAGE_MIXIN is renamed REVISIONED_MIXIN: the name had become a lie, and\nit is the central concept of the module.\n\nVerified on a running instance rather than argued: the CND change deploys with no\nMAJOR-change refusal (unlike an i18n flag, which Jahia rejects outright), the\nmixin applies to a jnt:bigText under /sites/<site>/contents, and publishing it\nstores a snapshot keyed on its own UUID with status STORED and generator 5.\n\nMutation-verified: restoring the pages-then-mixin order fails exactly the two\ntests that state the consequences --\n\n    revisionedContentOwnsItself: expected <mock> but was <null>\n    nearestOwnerWins:            returned the page, not the block\n\n257 -> 265 unit tests, 94 -> 95 end-to-end. The pre-existing test that a\ndeeply-nested non-page node maps to its owning page still passes, which is what\nproves widening the mixin did not change how pages resolve.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmAO3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMswQAJRtVqcdX4ksryIEk0nvjyvA\n4Nn6dIpy8unE4MkOknxMpfcvc+easuHOAEUAGcS7I6+tKoBq/5QPc7jJ6o8zY/1l\ns3tVaAUBfAjMdh290JyGqSPjo4q+6+A6Et5Fj+ASCOLcQHe1nQxefe8MPf46yS69\nYF05fREtpg7kMO5wku2+GbS1c35CkXYrBYW5E50PjuheqEFylzU4txbJcFTupHut\ns5giE5garG8vOuLKKM2QhcNPxmjNvSMsOiLTmXzsWH+fkuj+cMeGJMRyV5kdStr5\ndcuvcciUoOV8wOjMepqzJ2PFuiccgJE4qCt2k2SSLsDjEqOoWMgCgSDYT3nkXX06\nT/s29TBJY1t0g9UrpjnTJylmLqx4oamEaEiF7KZCNYwHykEgi4d1ulww0goueCk8\ntSbZhAl2p75+sOyL/mzeDOeMgy4MF02l1PTPYRcu845ThfmqPD9b+HcsD4lFwljg\n3+f+bzxIUmgA7gVm0Yg3C+02rDNxo33Sy6gpra4+pLnDheKIWdoHmtSu55CWN6AV\n42JFQhNYIQ7i3iEvECsU4WBSuZ1pMsslEEzwSPGZEnzKOye7rm/n2tronvByufVX\nVhfaWSsujakTcrfs5/js7UiJaXTzQo6U8YCgprwr8T6hNL+tsL1z5VA4fzyzVWfD\ntM2cSMmAKTIymcji8nWM\n=zzQ8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T11:08:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/d67c4d5f7e77182677f2f828b5ea58043b8efa49","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGQ2N2M0ZDVmN2U3NzE4MjY3N2YyZjgyOGI1ZWE1ODA0M2I4ZWZhNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/53c8b7ef07e7e2037dbce778a1b1a8015efbdfd4","sha":"53c8b7ef07e7e2037dbce778a1b1a8015efbdfd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/53c8b7ef07e7e2037dbce778a1b1a8015efbdfd4"}],"sha":"d67c4d5f7e77182677f2f828b5ea58043b8efa49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/d67c4d5f7e77182677f2f828b5ea58043b8efa49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/53c8b7ef07e7e2037dbce778a1b1a8015efbdfd4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T09:27:57Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T09:27:57Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore: return master to 1.5.0-SNAPSHOT after 1.4.2\n\nBack to the SNAPSHOT master was already on, matching what followed 1.3.1 and\n1.4.1: a patch released off master does not advance the minor line.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"46cf0949016459e7ebbda4ce417f481db54f25a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/46cf0949016459e7ebbda4ce417f481db54f25a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/53c8b7ef07e7e2037dbce778a1b1a8015efbdfd4","verification":{"payload":"tree 46cf0949016459e7ebbda4ce417f481db54f25a2\nparent 2ac9650f543c8f1322f3ee6af3182ba9eb20a619\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788341277 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788341277 +0200\n\nchore: return master to 1.5.0-SNAPSHOT after 1.4.2\n\nBack to the SNAPSHOT master was already on, matching what followed 1.3.1 and\n1.4.1: a patch released off master does not advance the minor line.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqX7B0ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lwdQgAya4HhTgnjKd24+yulX3n2xLZz0YrGMLYFatG38mddTQ4TDxHLdcRXDuc\n1bTX2i1p9Rbp9B1oT6SFE3ToNQnKDMxdnUftr7tzts5axPvrTOEkhmK/JbPmYni5\nODe9xf1BNPJhb0EWZ8GiyyYUh559c7wAbk3m3jMIrNvkCl9WTg9I3GMcT4dbKmYd\nTVAakjpeHmiaS1Oyq7We5ZTrNOue8SBdrxsUeGibUqq9cM3zr4DI/a/qP+O+YFm5\njoEJMZ6eGXTcNhqGp36UAGnCYAcYyVJMiWAkMKUSwN1Yu5QZF9DXKSQCmNHvE17l\nY14+As/tF5rEerKjpDWm5KSlMwizRw==\n=HDqY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T09:28:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/53c8b7ef07e7e2037dbce778a1b1a8015efbdfd4","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDUzYzhiN2VmMDdlN2UyMDM3ZGJjZTc3OGExYjFhODAxNWVmYmRmZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/2ac9650f543c8f1322f3ee6af3182ba9eb20a619","sha":"2ac9650f543c8f1322f3ee6af3