"verification":{"payload":"tree 6e08e017a9533ecf1ed514e44a126d41e93ae71a\nparent 40c07657bb7f0dd0a2ec9788efc365bdad7840ad\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788341247 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788341247 +0200\n\nrelease: 1.4.2\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqX6/8ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nMawgAsiq/sckKozI73olOG9GzDeEyLpoKjDm54fo/MPqmRctFM4SQN5oVeyXB\nJ5/bBZRnMwITnBoxtcMdAejxLP9+/N3fRxZR8FEmG3tAEd1xBZBo+kziCaJWJeyB\n7Kf8YnG9E3BdWMELx/6U+x/IymIf/3oaHFUvCs2II0kkprK+DA5dvh8gqWTYFIWt\nxMvIsdOaf9J+gFxJDqve5ttqiD2aXg43MmcsIRuxT6p1IZNzwZafFdJP/aGyV1D8\nAzQAlhtpITqQC2e9LuSs+1Oep29yDLJwIL3hEqnX37wQxLyErmNhqXoPN1pybid+\nWwstRcGsspFI6jSOj+k40p0m6ztm5w==\n=Nqvt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T09:27:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/2ac9650f543c8f1322f3ee6af3182ba9eb20a619","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDJhYzk2NTBmNTQzYzhmMTMyMmYzZWU2YWYzMTgyYmE5ZWIyMGE2MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/40c07657bb7f0dd0a2ec9788efc365bdad7840ad","sha":"40c07657bb7f0dd0a2ec9788efc365bdad7840ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/40c07657bb7f0dd0a2ec9788efc365bdad7840ad"}],"sha":"2ac9650f543c8f1322f3ee6af3182ba9eb20a619","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/2ac9650f543c8f1322f3ee6af3182ba9eb20a619"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/40c07657bb7f0dd0a2ec9788efc365bdad7840ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T09:26:26Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T09:26:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(diff): render the snapshot markdown in the comparison rows (#10)\n\nThe rows showed the module''s own generated syntax literally: \"## Support policy\",\n\"**not**\", \"- item\", and even the normaliser''s \\[ \\] escapes, which are its own\nbookkeeping. They now render.\n\nThe diff is still computed on the RAW Markdown and always will be. That is what\nmakes one snapshot comparable to another regardless of how either is displayed;\nrendering is derived afterwards, purely presentational.\n\nThe hard part is that rendering DELETES characters -- delimiters, escapes, the\nline prefix -- while MarkdownDiff''s word-level segments are expressed in\npositions in the raw line. The two are only consistent if every visible\ncharacter is tracked back to where it came from, so each run carries its raw\nspan and the changed flags are crossed onto it. Off by three and \"## Support\npolicy\" highlights the wrong word. Most of the new unit tests are about that\ncrossing rather than about syntax, and it is mutation-verified: using the\nvisible index instead of the raw offset gives\n\n    expected: <policy>    but was: <icy>        (off by \"## \")\n    expected: <not>       but was: <t i>        (off by \"**\")\n    expected: <withdrawn> but was: <thdrawn>    (off by the escape)\n\nInlineMarkdown is not a Markdown parser and the module still has none. It reads\nonly the closed grammar MarkdownNormalizer emits, which is what keeps a\nthird-party parser and its HTML sink out of a public page built from captured\ncontent. Anything unrecognised stays literal text, exactly as everything did\nbefore. No HTML is produced in Java either: the view still escapes every piece.\n\nThree deliberate limits:\n\n- Links and images keep their literal [text](href) form. Collapsing them to\n  their text would hide an href change -- same words, new destination, no\n  visible difference -- in a record whose whole purpose is showing what changed.\n- Heading levels are classes, never real <h1>-<h6>. The panel sits inside the\n  host page, so real headings would splice the snapshot''s outline into the\n  page''s own and break heading order for anyone navigating by it. Appearance is\n  what was wanted; the row''s meaning is already carried by <del>/<ins> and the\n  +/- marker.\n- List markers are emitted as text, not drawn with ::before. An ordered list''s\n  number is information -- a list that renumbers has changed -- and this module\n  having no ::before of its own is what lets it neutralise a host theme''s list\n  decoration outright.\n\nFormatting inherits the row''s colour and adds none of its own, so a row is still\nadded or removed with the stylesheet missing entirely.\n\nFound by its own tests along the way: `closesLater` correctly refuses to open a\nbold span with no partner (\"2 ** 8 is 256\") and was wrongly asked the same of\nthe CLOSING delimiter, where nothing follows for it to find -- so \"**not**\"\nrendered as \"not**\".\n\n243 -> 257 unit tests, 93 -> 94 end-to-end. The existing assertions on\n<mark>twelve</mark> and <mark>eighteen</mark> still pass, which is the proof that\nrendering did not cost the word-level highlighting.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc7e7608b3c10ca92c77ddf2fe97e42296a27037","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/fc7e7608b3c10ca92c77ddf2fe97e42296a27037"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/40c07657bb7f0dd0a2ec9788efc365bdad7840ad","verification":{"payload":"tree fc7e7608b3c10ca92c77ddf2fe97e42296a27037\nparent 932afe8f9011bf79178b20095138a8601ff01267\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788341186 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788341186 +0200\n\nfeat(diff): render the snapshot markdown in the comparison rows (#10)\n\nThe rows showed the module''s own generated syntax literally: \"## Support policy\",\n\"**not**\", \"- item\", and even the normaliser''s \\[ \\] escapes, which are its own\nbookkeeping. They now render.\n\nThe diff is still computed on the RAW Markdown and always will be. That is what\nmakes one snapshot comparable to another regardless of how either is displayed;\nrendering is derived afterwards, purely presentational.\n\nThe hard part is that rendering DELETES characters -- delimiters, escapes, the\nline prefix -- while MarkdownDiff''s word-level segments are expressed in\npositions in the raw line. The two are only consistent if every visible\ncharacter is tracked back to where it came from, so each run carries its raw\nspan and the changed flags are crossed onto it. Off by three and \"## Support\npolicy\" highlights the wrong word. Most of the new unit tests are about that\ncrossing rather than about syntax, and it is mutation-verified: using the\nvisible index instead of the raw offset gives\n\n    expected: <policy>    but was: <icy>        (off by \"## \")\n    expected: <not>       but was: <t i>        (off by \"**\")\n    expected: <withdrawn> but was: <thdrawn>    (off by the escape)\n\nInlineMarkdown is not a Markdown parser and the module still has none. It reads\nonly the closed grammar MarkdownNormalizer emits, which is what keeps a\nthird-party parser and its HTML sink out of a public page built from captured\ncontent. Anything unrecognised stays literal text, exactly as everything did\nbefore. No HTML is produced in Java either: the view still escapes every piece.\n\nThree deliberate limits:\n\n- Links and images keep their literal [text](href) form. Collapsing them to\n  their text would hide an href change -- same words, new destination, no\n  visible difference -- in a record whose whole purpose is showing what changed.\n- Heading levels are classes, never real <h1>-<h6>. The panel sits inside the\n  host page, so real headings would splice the snapshot''s outline into the\n  page''s own and break heading order for anyone navigating by it. Appearance is\n  what was wanted; the row''s meaning is already carried by <del>/<ins> and the\n  +/- marker.\n- List markers are emitted as text, not drawn with ::before. An ordered list''s\n  number is information -- a list that renumbers has changed -- and this module\n  having no ::before of its own is what lets it neutralise a host theme''s list\n  decoration outright.\n\nFormatting inherits the row''s colour and adds none of its own, so a row is still\nadded or removed with the stylesheet missing entirely.\n\nFound by its own tests along the way: `closesLater` correctly refuses to open a\nbold span with no partner (\"2 ** 8 is 256\") and was wrongly asked the same of\nthe CLOSING delimiter, where nothing follows for it to find -- so \"**not**\"\nrendered as \"not**\".\n\n243 -> 257 unit tests, 93 -> 94 end-to-end. The existing assertions on\n<mark>twelve</mark> and <mark>eighteen</mark> still pass, which is the proof that\nrendering did not cost the word-level highlighting.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql+vCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWeoQAHTYrsKDjvBMTTQWWmGeEe67\nA1zyPBV5RheneoIlZsPH6dfC2H/uohlasvf6d3Aq6R2ANpZdQcVexutr9Q5t/X8V\nvt5vayXNKiNszQx+lz0f+UtnYF/WElao4PgcafwLaBWaMcZxFd6yVMFzCo6hE8rs\nAvXVo4D5pdnXPeD25eOAeN0IORPHacTLDDIFYt68Uj7dU8nW6fIddj7AF93ri/Gx\niTNPxIZSFN9SYdIEm+9QJEJV/G0hBnXATA2LGFNe81jXwJrfge+zKSGMEz+kaN5n\nL2Gv5T37hlcxLTBHOoCy90aVOIs5UQoIKQnQR8PScU3b8uBuGZCfKrO9+gHgh/WQ\n1pnAmPn/nus5wmETqqP8IOxGo/FzAvLq65XwOOctXXoCrkB7nzsfRZ5eAP9yMmlJ\njA3HlnzuA35sx5oGH11BZga19vfI7ad6Er9pmc3w89Ytj98jQy1sE+fd5HwD/7kV\nw4A/P9t4kz95w6zQ0kkPCRVy+e/03XnX1/NdDbivF3+mdcL/rhoj/ydQvgWb96fj\nplqmmpegIaaLzVOhUwT2xiL6DsZqZkO7RDXOgmXYaJH9RTAJvvrUMloV51TsFlOb\nCVwggl4rTQ1p0chJoimUyxQ+S0j6P1hkSYgGfhLI15AN4tAJxzOI4Cr1WxkLnch3\ndzHgO4HjmLizDzWuKLH/\n=/7Xl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T09:26:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-