ignature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqX2n8ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lsxAf+LK/67x0GGWXFnZBVsILLbm5GXAnQPQJHUTz6az4oCvzQLoPKEz40v7Ga\nQ3u7xKUkKRkMeS0dR7cNp6EIkb16Y/bFuQQaYABtQDLaAtPq/rGVD1ZFWzQhvYLX\nstwrt/PtLw755nDjQ7Twcm/pPSh3peojPlKOa9O4ZHP7ieZso9pW3UPFbzSa8ffe\n2Lq6XYvbVKQK1vsNAil85hLNf5PMUcJjtu6YajS3CmARThwTRWosKH2bcgGT5+EG\nuaZhZbQUw+HisJVLb5TCAyOUGbyrjv9bS7vNcOecgTkHi+aYVCPF8SHtjtK9sz4r\nMBr5v0gRaBddJ/6sGhwVPSfPW99cnw==\n=HfLQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T08:12:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/0c2dc5775868251a495e42b36bf81b2fb3f7547c","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDBjMmRjNTc3NTg2ODI1MWE0OTVlNDJiMzZiZjgxYjJmYjNmNzU0N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/1e3215d827fb9c703cc1a09f11c56ef715999e05","sha":"1e3215d827fb9c703cc1a09f11c56ef715999e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1e3215d827fb9c703cc1a09f11c56ef715999e05"}],"sha":"0c2dc5775868251a495e42b36bf81b2fb3f7547c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0c2dc5775868251a495e42b36bf81b2fb3f7547c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1e3215d827fb9c703cc1a09f11c56ef715999e05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T08:11:29Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T08:11:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(css): stop a host theme numbering the module''s own list items (#9)\n\nReported from the Jahia Academy, whose theme carries\n\n    .jac-content ol>li:before { content: counters(b,\".\"); counter-increment: b;\n                                background-color:#209fda; border-radius:50rem; ... }\n\nwhich puts a numbered blue badge on every ordered-list item on the page. This\nmodule renders inside .jac-content and emits two <ol>s, so the badge landed on\nevery revision in the list and on every row of every comparison -- and a diff\ncan be hundreds of rows, which makes the panel the worse of the two surfaces.\n\nBoth lists already set `list-style: none`. That removes the NATIVE marker and\ndoes nothing whatever about a generated one, which is why the badge painted\nstraight through a stylesheet that looks like it should have prevented it.\n\nThe selectors name the component root as well as the list, and that is\nload-bearing rather than verbose. The host rule is (0,1,3); the obvious\n`.crh-revision-list > li::before` is only (0,1,2) and LOSES, which would look\nexactly like the fix not working. Naming the root makes each selector (0,2,2),\nand two classes beat one whatever the source order -- which matters, because a\nhost stylesheet may load after this one. Not `!important`: if some other host\nrule ever outranks even this, the answer is another level of specificity, and\nthis module has no business winning an arms race inside someone else''s theme by\nforce.\n\ncounter-increment is reset as well as content, though `content: none` alone\nmeans the pseudo-element is never generated. The host rule advances a counter it\nshares with the page''s own ordered lists, so left running, our rows would\nsilently renumber a genuine numbered list further down the Academy page -- a\ndefect in their content, caused by ours, with nothing pointing back here.\n\nThis module renders no ::before of its own, so nothing of its own styling is\nlost.\n\nThe test asserts what a browser computes rather than what I calculated, and\ninjects a control <ol> the module does not own to prove the host rule is in\nforce -- without it, a silently failed style injection would report ''none''\neverywhere and pass for the wrong reason.\n\nVerified by mutation: with the selectors weakened to the naive one-class form and\nthat build deployed, the suite goes 92/93 with only this test failing, on the\nreal badge content:\n\n    the revision list must not carry the host theme''s numbering:\n      expected ''counters(b, \".\")'' to equal ''none''\n\n92 -> 93 end-to-end tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"df5695c768c25d815891561b33ac543a188c431c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/df5695c768c25d815891561b33ac543a188c431c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/1e3215d827fb9c703cc1a09f11c56ef715999e05","verification":{"payload":"tree df5695c768c25d815891561b33ac543a188c431c\nparent 7174a105ea88027b21ecc510032328f578b6e825\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788336689 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788336689 +0200\n\nfix(css): stop a host theme numbering the module''s own list items (#9)\n\nReported from the Jahia Academy, whose theme carries\n\n    .jac-content ol>li:before { content: counters(b,\".\"); counter-increment: b;\n                                background-color:#209fda; border-radius:50rem; ... }\n\nwhich puts a numbered blue badge on every ordered-list item on the page. This\nmodule renders inside .jac-content and emits two <ol>s, so the badge landed on\nevery revision in the list and on every row of every comparison -- and a diff\ncan be hundreds of rows, which makes the panel the worse of the two surfaces.\n\nBoth lists already set `list-style: none`. That removes the NATIVE marker and\ndoes nothing whatever about a generated one, which is why the badge painted\nstraight through a stylesheet that looks like it should have prevented it.\n\nThe selectors name the component root as well as the list, and that is\nload-bearing rather than verbose. The host rule is (0,1,3); the obvious\n`.crh-revision-list > li::before` is only (0,1,2) and LOSES, which would look\nexactly like the fix not working. Naming the root makes each selector (0,2,2),\nand two classes beat one whatever the source order -- which matters, because a\nhost stylesheet may load after this one. Not `!important`: if some other host\nrule ever outranks even this, the answer is another level of specificity, and\nthis module has no business winning an arms race inside someone else''s theme by\nforce.\n\ncounter-increment is reset as well as content, though `content: none` alone\nmeans the pseudo-element is never generated. The host rule advances a counter it\nshares with the page''s own ordered lists, so left running, our rows would\nsilently renumber a genuine numbered list further down the Academy page -- a\ndefect in their content, caused by ours, with nothing pointing back here.\n\nThis module renders no ::before of its own, so nothing of its own styling is\nlost.\n\nThe test asserts what a browser computes rather than what I calculated, and\ninjects a control <ol> the module does not own to prove the host rule is in\nforce -- without it, a silently failed style injection would report ''none''\neverywhere and pass for the wrong reason.\n\nVerified by mutation: with the selectors weakened to the naive one-class form and\nthat build deployed, the suite goes 92/93 with only this test failing, on the\nreal badge content:\n\n    the revision list must not carry the host theme''s numbering:\n      expected ''counters(b, \".\")'' to equal ''none''\n\n92 -> 93 end-to-end tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql9oxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyJ0QAKyB258PL+9WTdykK1NIG92S\nQrFd1fSvxJ3TgcUG2ADGWGCtCo8cGR3oTtQ2Shqx20fd0mKDWH3avPQ3zrJAunBn\n9Iz0tf+7GHjRWDHMXlg9q1Br02M6LYe/LjlJPG8L07nI5fa6uVh64SWrjHElz/fx\n8Ur3ZHTHsXeH4O2thx0aBfbubZeLOeaQriGK189Xg+oJRMZsHakfF1oP5pee2Loa\nUy/uj+lbRnxWq3AdceAIFsnGzDB8tpNV2/lSIlAMUqeC6/omHEFU3sBvG6nzL7o5\nYKNu3mKUcporrbEdciPFq+HVkphvDbKQ+DstIK1+dIdJW4G4Qsls6tx1p7S4o6fa\nu8kUffIK3+N5HKLIVcAsageodAsvRBkCMlPe3NvdY+MIidycrNASry1LVepWrEsG\n4/hQA128JTgvfwKrHKljxLJtaWZ0h3ZuNR4sjsYfutu+0A504PG8LPAP5YQClujE\nEtiNWXIuXVMipEao3iO5oVoyusLOdfnqsK36lFhveqK7yrpwyLgGIsdIXXhQZ2rv\nv3TEmv98gA3UFyOl8m8HUmpcIDNGbdJ5