ss\n\nchore: bounded quality pass — security, a11y, and a harness that can fail\n\nMerged as a merge commit rather than squashed so each of the 32 fixes stays\nindependently revertable.","tree":{"sha":"6ad48f2da747a9a8b1f4c0063e45cb308d50fee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/6ad48f2da747a9a8b1f4c0063e45cb308d50fee7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/d67d04ad738b59ec6191a6d154aa785968f14824","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ad48f2da747a9a8b1f4c0063e45cb308d50fee7\nparent 0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245\nparent afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788333590 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788333590 +0200\n\nMerge pull request #8 from Jahia/chore/module-quality-pass\n\nchore: bounded quality pass — security, a11y, and a harness that can fail\n\nMerged as a merge commit rather than squashed so each of the 32 fixes stays\nindependently revertable.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql84WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFusQAChIRg5i0X3OlafDn2QAAXGC\nBeLcVl77sUS5PQLTpO6O5R0XWgLpjKVel3Ao/ikFEExi7OihFTZf91ivd6sy/UOz\nEuVIfNh2iFc+s7T4YNICyrY/pg1ThcoLMxEifz0w0dnbfXw8L/85dM/SYmVhpeoV\nuew44QiRfxfT92Plkmye9Br0EJxMf5s3Mz2UNjjpOnAc2snj+okick131IkRFYCz\nczf2UZ3UqrV9PbP+1S7IsM5b00nRTMi8sgEpNh86bfpSqLmJXwip4gss719OLo/y\nmWdkXXwLyUtr9buCGCuuxCpkqpyZVq8Lh53swGXmTMaEmqeH0P6RF2pHvNBOd8mP\nRJrNydXV01tbHpW6rL2kxp+ecKpUpA146JJKiTEBaobJOSd5R9i0zzXPDskq1bPU\nWwGayZbVkAEd6YOVAuZn94otX2gGtw7Tw6/8yhHQE/nroiirtYMN/RoStMlQ2rNS\nJ+zOz8iEPGtc700XvKO9EJI0zN+dpkXSvafO1+QMBaXrfMeuNlrQSzrDHrDM3WCO\n0yjjwPKlNDM8duJOdvczFvrufWyR95jEmksXQobzKn2gos1eFSgJuGC6zBrz5wCR\nL1J/6bXLZ7CwpBjAcBjqFWhnccnJ/IFxsvl+1YQLpCMKROINj+1zkeyXd8zdJCde\nYwTLvo79A5McHoYCzGzO\n=ucB7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T07:19:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/d67d04ad738b59ec6191a6d154aa785968f14824","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGQ2N2QwNGFkNzM4YjU5ZWM2MTkxYTZkMTU0YWE3ODU5NjhmMTQ4MjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245","sha":"0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611","sha":"afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611"}],"sha":"d67d04ad738b59ec6191a6d154aa785968f14824","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/d67d04ad738b59ec6191a6d154aa785968f14824"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T07:00:30Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T07:00:30Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: tell the reader when a snapshot was too large to read in full\n\nSnapshotPayload.read applied the 1 MB cap on the read side by returning the\nstart of the payload and logging a WARN. The comparison panel and the jContent\npreview therefore received a shortened document with no way to know it was\nshortened, and rendered it as the complete record.\n\nThat is not a display detail. A diff computed from a payload missing its tail\nreports EVERY line past the cut as removed, and presents that as the record of\nwhat changed on that date -- a snapshot missing its tail is indistinguishable\nfrom a page that was genuinely shorter. And a WARN reaches an operator reading\nlogs at the time; it never reached the visitor being shown the result, who is\nwho the record is for.\n\nread() now returns SnapshotContent: the Markdown together with whether all of it\nwas read. Both surfaces say so:\n\n  - The comparison popup shows a warning, at role=\"alert\", saying the comparison\n    was made from only the beginning of a snapshot and should be treated as\n    incomplete. Deliberately a SEPARATE notice from the existing\n    crh_diff.truncated: that one means the comparison was clipped for display\n    and the rest exists, this one means the comparison itself is unreliable. A\n    reader told only the first would trust a wrong result.\n  - The jContent preview says what follows is missing rather than absent from\n    the page.\n\nSnapshotContent is top-level rather than nested, because it is named in a TLD\nfunction-signature and RevisionDiffView already records why that matters: nested\nsignatures are a known source of Jasper resolution failures that surface only at\nfirst render, in a JSP, on the public site. The EL function returns the whole\nobject rather than the Markdown alone so the preview does not need a second read\nto ask about truncation -- two reads of the same binary can disagree.\n\nStyling reuses the removed-line tokens rather than adding a colour:\n--crh-removed-text on --crh-removed-bg measures 12.16:1, past the 7:1 AAA\nthreshold. Severity is carried by the wording and role=\"alert\", never by colour\nalone, so it survives the stylesheet failing to load.\n\nSnapshotPayload had no tests at all, which is how this survived. Six added,\ncovering both boundary directions -- exactly at the cap is NOT truncated, since\na warning that cries wolf is how a real one gets ignored -- and that the binary\nis still disposed on the early-exit path the cap introduces.\n\nVerified by mutation: with the flag never set,\n  overTheCapIsReportedTruncated:73 expected: <true> but was: <false>\n  binaryIsDisposedOnTheTruncatedPath:136 expected: <true> but was: <false>\n\n237 -> 243 unit tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ad48f2da747a9a8b1f4c0063e45cb308d50fee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/6ad48f2da747a9a8b1f4c0063e45cb308d50fee7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ad48f2da747a9a8b1f4c0063e45cb308d50fee7\nparent 843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788332430 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788332430 +0200\n\nfix: tell the reader when a snapshot was too large to read in full\n\nSnapshotPayload.read applied the 1 MB cap on the read side by returning the\nstart of the payload and logging a WARN. The comparison panel and the jContent\npreview therefore received a shortened document with no way to know it was\nshortened, and rendered it as the complete record.\n\nThat is not a display detail. A diff computed from a payload missing its tail\nreports EVERY line past the cut as removed, and presents that as the record of\nwhat changed on that date -- a snapshot missing its tail is indistinguishable\nfrom a page that was genuinely shorter. And a WARN reaches an operator reading\nlogs at the time; it never reached the visitor being shown the result, who is\nwho the record is for.\n\nread() now returns SnapshotContent: the Markdown together with whether all of it\nwas read. Both surfaces say so:\n\n  - The comparison popup shows a warning, at role=\"alert\", saying the comparison\n    was made from only the beginning of a snapshot and should be treated as\n    incomplete. Deliberately a SEPARATE notice from the existing\n    crh_diff.truncated: that one means the comparison was clipped for display\n    and the rest exists, this one means the comparison itself is unreliable. A\n    reader told only the first would trust a wrong result.\n  - The jContent preview says what follows is missing rather than absent from\n    the page.\n\nSnapshotContent is top-level rather than nested, because it is named in a TLD\nfunction-signature and RevisionDiffView already records why that matters: nested\nsignatures are a known source of Jasper resolution failures that surface only at\nfirst render, in a JSP, on the public site. The EL function returns the whole\nobject rather than the Markdown alone so the preview does not need a second read\nto ask about truncation -- two reads of the same binary can disagree.\n\nStyling reuses the removed-line tokens rather than adding a colour:\n--crh-removed-text on --crh-removed-bg measures 12.16:1, past the 7:1 AAA\nthreshold. Severity is carried by the wording and role=\"alert\", never by colour\nalone, so it survives the stylesheet failing to load.\n\nSnapshotPayload had no tests at all, which is how this survived. Six added,\ncovering both boundary directions -- exactly at the cap is NOT truncated, since\na warning that cries wolf is how a real one gets ignored -- and that the binary\nis still disposed on the early-exit path the cap introduces.\n\nVerified by mutation: with the flag never set,\n  overTheCapIsReportedTruncated:73 expected: <true> but was: <false>\n  binaryIsDisposedOnTheTruncatedPath:136 expected: <true> but was: <false>\n\n237 -> 243 unit tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXyY4ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mGagf+LsSK15mp6LVjQU5yRWbdKx0qw+Vv9uJjFEbb5Seo1ggCi7f/zWBSG+hC\nl19krcGQTqGpz+XREKBPgIYGAmqUUqijtBQWveat7M5kvXOMbHPeF8fmCaJ7pqcZ\nRb6kvZihokPA2Cph/Ug2a23Ua/zCeDpx9Ls7FdWfvQVSAWXVpf3O4RWEnwVdV5wR\nfaxcPj/K1oXZlwuhEwHMV7596z4NwjrGUhLos90Nq+NxlgwA6IKza0eRp3/gpWgt\n6wFT1Gyu6u/jBOq4gn+qp9AxY8nqAlO5oJyQCvLx6l92q3q7eyk7wVhC4zrNlEyW\nfZwJzMfar/570G9eQfzz6NxRqUtYiA==\n=ZDq5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T07:00:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGFmZWNmZjBkZTVhZWNiNGU5ZGYyMzMyOTQ1OWQ5OTQyYWVmNTA2MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d","sha":"843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d"}],"sha":"afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/afecff0de5aecb4e9df23329459d9942aef50611"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:40:01Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:40:01Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: refuse oversized view output instead of silently truncating it\n\nMarkdownNormalizer.normalize began with capInputSize, which returned the first\nMAX_INPUT_CHARS characters of anything longer and dropped the rest. No\nexception, no flag on the result, no log line: the caller could not tell a\ntruncated document from a short one.\n\nFor this module that is the worst available outcome rather than a safeguard. A\nsnapshot is a permanent, publicly served record, and one missing its tail is\nindistinguishable from a page that was genuinely shorter -- it does not look\nlike damage, it looks like history, and a later comparison reports text as\nremoved on a date when nothing was removed. Every other size limit here already\nrefuses: output over MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES is recorded OVERSIZE with nothing\nstored, and MarkdownDiff.Result carries isTruncated so a clipped comparison can\nsay so. This was the one path that quietly kept going.\n\nExceeding the cap now throws MarkdownTooLargeException, checked before parsing\nbecause the cap bounds the parse cost as well as the output. SnapshotCaptureJob\ncatches it and records OVERSIZE -- the status this module already uses for \"too\nbig, nothing stored\" -- rather than letting the generic handler file it as\nFAILED, which would send an operator looking for a fault that is not there. The\nnormalize call is hoisted out of the argument list it was buried in so the\nrefusal has somewhere to be caught and the failure point is visible.\n\nReachability, since it decides who this affects:\n  - Live capture: unreachable. The guest render is bounded at MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES\n    (1 MB) before the normaliser sees it, so a 2,000,000-character cap could not\n    be hit. Defence in depth only.\n  - The backfill script: reachable. It concatenates every leaf render of a page\n    with no cap of its own, so a large page could be clipped and then, because\n    normalising strips HTML and collapses whitespace, come back under the 1 MB\n    write cap and be stored as complete. The script''s validation gate could not\n    catch it: a page that size would have been refused by live capture, so there\n    was no captured snapshot to compare against. That is the path that writes\n    authoritative history.\n\nThe test that asserted the old behaviour is rewritten, not deleted, and it is\nworth being explicit about why that is allowed here: it asserted the output came\nback SHORTER than the input, \"proving the input was capped\". What it actually\npinned was the silent truncation. It now asserts the refusal, that the reported\nsize and cap are the real ones, and -- a boundary nothing covered before -- that\ninput at exactly the cap is still accepted.\n\nVerified by mutation rather than by watching it pass. With truncation restored:\n  Expected org.jahia.modules.revisionhistory.MarkdownTooLargeException to be\n  thrown, but nothing was thrown\n\n236 -> 237 unit tests.\n\nNot fixed here, and still open: SnapshotPayload.read truncates on the READ side\nwith only a WARN and no flag reaching the views. Same class of defect, different\ntrade-off, and outside what this change was asked to cover.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"081e4ee2f5b0b6114bf71bc9575ecd7944710a9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/081e4ee2f5b0b6114bf71bc9575ecd7944710a9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d","verification":{"payload":"tree 081e4ee2f5b0b6114bf71bc9575ecd7944710a9a\nparent 935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788331201 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788331201 +0200\n\nfix: refuse oversized view output instead of silently truncating it\n\nMarkdownNormalizer.normalize began with capInputSize, which returned the first\nMAX_INPUT_CHARS characters of anything longer and dropped the rest. No\nexception, no flag on the result, no log line: the caller could not tell a\ntruncated document from a short one.\n\nFor this module that is the worst available outcome rather than a safeguard. A\nsnapshot is a permanent, publicly served record, and one missing its tail is\nindistinguishable from a page that was genuinely shorter -- it does not look\nlike damage, it looks like history, and a later comparison reports text as\nremoved on a date when nothing was removed. Every other size limit here already\nrefuses: output over MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES is recorded OVERSIZE with nothing\nstored, and MarkdownDiff.Result carries isTruncated so a clipped comparison can\nsay so. This was the one path that quietly kept going.\n\nExceeding the cap now throws MarkdownTooLargeException, checked before parsing\nbecause the cap bounds the parse cost as well as the output. SnapshotCaptureJob\ncatches it and records OVERSIZE -- the status this module already uses for \"too\nbig, nothing stored\" -- rather than letting the generic handler file it as\nFAILED, which would send an operator looking for a fault that is not there. The\nnormalize call is hoisted out of the argument list it was buried in so the\nrefusal has somewhere to be caught and the failure point is visible.\n\nReachability, since it decides who this affects:\n  - Live capture: unreachable. The guest render is bounded at MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES\n    (1 MB) before the normaliser sees it, so a 2,000,000-character cap could not\n    be hit. Defence in depth only.\n  - The backfill script: reachable. It concatenates every leaf render of a page\n    with no cap of its own, so a large page could be clipped and then, because\n    normalising strips HTML and collapses whitespace, come back under the 1 MB\n    write cap and be stored as complete. The script''s validation gate could not\n    catch it: a page that size would have been refused by live capture, so there\n    was no captured snapshot to compare against. That is the path that writes\n    authoritative history.\n\nThe test that asserted the old behaviour is rewritten, not deleted, and it is\nworth being explicit about why that is allowed here: it asserted the output came\nback SHORTER than the input, \"proving the input was capped\". What it actually\npinned was the silent truncation. It now asserts the refusal, that the reported\nsize and cap are the real ones, and -- a boundary nothing covered before -- that\ninput at exactly the cap is still accepted.\n\nVerified by mutation rather than by watching it pass. With truncation restored:\n  Expected org.jahia.modules.revisionhistory.MarkdownTooLargeException to be\n  thrown, but nothing was thrown\n\n236 -> 237 unit tests.\n\nNot fixed here, and still open: SnapshotPayload.read truncates on the READ side\nwith only a WARN and no flag reaching the views. Same class of defect, different\ntrade-off, and outside what this change was asked to cover.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXxMEACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lDcAf8C6TxlSmO6hoECYrMEGseu9vM65IBfDZXRu5jrULJn8R1BwsM8kO7GJ9D\n2DPEjaIdwgti4+6UJitxaDMlmBZOwBd6B98A0mVyGoBJETKLjIJizB4mK+/nKJYA\nH71Cl99ePlyG9vvdvriORwc3X+L9+duwMzs4D30Lsi5VLn08qn7S2NHjnt9yjv6v\nhHjOG70lgKjajbLVqS3ut9NR+wA9PM6hK/dHsGgoALe+Fj+TikS3aDVf2EY5M2wJ\nxrTIHPIl3JQLVO/tMJTbAGeAeACYoRgaq4G74zohs8izFiQx5TAAIYbTqyerHA3R\n6y+wVTdc5FynNnHywhSYn9Ze6i9H/w==\n=mT+5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T06:42:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDg0M2VlZTA2NGRmY2Q1ZDA2ZWZhZDY3NDA3N2JjOGE0ZjgxYWM0MWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667","sha":"935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667"}],"sha":"843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/843eee064dfcd5d06efad674077bc8a4f81ac41d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:33:20Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:33:20Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test: execute the shipped backfill script in the suite\n\nThe backfill had no automated coverage at all. Four specs mention it, but they\nonly simulate backfilled STATE -- entries pinned to historical snapshots by hand\n-- so the Groovy script itself was never run by anything. That is how an abort on\nevery page carrying a revision history component survived: it is not subtle, and\nit was found by reading rather than by any test.\n\nThe spec builds the scenario that used to fail (revisioned page, a\ncrh:revisionHistory component, two publications so real snapshots exist) and runs\nthe script through the provisioning API in dry run. It asserts the run completes\nrather than parsing a report, because the provisioning API returns only\n.installed or .failed and .failed is exactly what the defect produced.\n\nThat assertion is stronger than it looks: on a page that HAS captured history the\nscript''s own byte-for-byte gate compares every reconstructed instant against the\nreal snapshot for that instant and aborts on any unexplained difference, so\n.installed means the composition matched too. Which is why the spec publishes\ntwice before running anything.\n\nci.build.sh stages the script into cypress/fixtures, copied at build time from\nthe one source of truth: the test image is built from tests/ only and has no\n../src, and a second copy committed here would drift until the spec proved that\nthe copy runs.\n\nManually validated against a running 8.2.4.0 before writing this, on a page with\ntwo captured snapshots and a revision history component:\n\n  validation: 2 checked, 2 exact, 0 date-skewed, 0 unexplained, 0 unverifiable\n\nwhich also confirms the separator change I reasoned about and did NOT make would\nhave been wrong: the mirror already agrees byte for byte.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ae2a219765435c92355a37ef98230ee75bed83a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/4ae2a219765435c92355a37ef98230ee75bed83a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ae2a219765435c92355a37ef98230ee75bed83a\nparent c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788330800 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788330800 +0200\n\ntest: execute the shipped backfill script in the suite\n\nThe backfill had no automated coverage at all. Four specs mention it, but they\nonly simulate backfilled STATE -- entries pinned to historical snapshots by hand\n-- so the Groovy script itself was never run by anything. That is how an abort on\nevery page carrying a revision history component survived: it is not subtle, and\nit was found by reading rather than by any test.\n\nThe spec builds the scenario that used to fail (revisioned page, a\ncrh:revisionHistory component, two publications so real snapshots exist) and runs\nthe script through the provisioning API in dry run. It asserts the run completes\nrather than parsing a report, because the provisioning API returns only\n.installed or .failed and .failed is exactly what the defect produced.\n\nThat assertion is stronger than it looks: on a page that HAS captured history the\nscript''s own byte-for-byte gate compares every reconstructed instant against the\nreal snapshot for that instant and aborts on any unexplained difference, so\n.installed means the composition matched too. Which is why the spec publishes\ntwice before running anything.\n\nci.build.sh stages the script into cypress/fixtures, copied at build time from\nthe one source of truth: the test image is built from tests/ only and has no\n../src, and a second copy committed here would drift until the spec proved that\nthe copy runs.\n\nManually validated against a running 8.2.4.0 before writing this, on a page with\ntwo captured snapshots and a revision history component:\n\n  validation: 2 checked, 2 exact, 0 date-skewed, 0 unexplained, 0 unverifiable\n\nwhich also confirms the separator change I reasoned about and did NOT make would\nhave been wrong: the mirror already agrees byte for byte.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXwzAACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lNEgf7BzbtP7QRQYCMlBUjwwEMa3EQwynGLgUs3/pkHywKRQPqtTAksIO6ZvVW\n90vf5pwo3pHVdbtp9JUiAu79PA/K7djZb+JUrzZT7SAIa3jrV7xR21U1OQO2zrKP\nB/4WTNKMdsA/2dr0jDo/QCr9gKx92ZBj7HCFKXel0wNdY0cL7+4lcDSMUXZMX3wK\nv90ssctDCLEe7u6w+2Mp2MC35VQn7/ipDCQTxlHQdysIJPVohWQk3plseBXHxszo\nu3OH4Zdx5QOiA5r2CxgVVZyDUgp0QHdPdPePS3ceZfkB8y4f69Kwbwin5qE57Y+q\nTpikAX12PLnmvIMe/9915q8pLsls1w==\n=ymKd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T06:42:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDkzNWMyMTI5NGQwYzQ1OGE2ZDZhYjE3NTdhZTMxMzZiYWQzNzU2Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a","sha":"c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a"}],"sha":"935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/935c21294d0c458a6d6ab1757ae3136bad375667"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:30:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:30:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat: make the revision pin per language, as a new property\n\nThe pin names a snapshot inside the PER-LANGUAGE folder\nrevision-history/<pageUuid>/<lang>/, and those names embed a per-language\ncontent hash, so a name valid in /en never resolves in /fr. One shared\nnon-i18n value could not express that: pinning an entry while editing in\nEnglish left the French comparison reporting \"no snapshot recorded\"\npermanently. The model could not represent the state, so it was not a bug in\nthe resolver.\n\nAdding `i18n` to crh:snapshotRef is NOT the fix, and this is measured on\n8.2.4.0 rather than assumed. Jahia''s DefinitionsBundleChecker classes a change\nof that flag on an existing property as a MAJOR definition change and cancels\nthe deployment outright:\n\n  ERROR [DefinitionsBundleChecker] - Major changes detected:\n  [nodeTypeName=crh:revisionEntry,type=MAJOR,\n   propDefDiffs={[itemName=crh:snapshotRef,type=MAJOR,operation=MODIFIED]}]\n  ... cancel module deployment\n\nSo crh:pinnedSnapshot is a NEW i18n property beside the old one, which is left\nbyte-for-byte unchanged. RevisionEntryBinder.pinnedSnapshotName reads the new\none first and falls back to the old, because an entry that silently lost its\npin would not fail loudly -- it would fall back to automatic binding and\nre-attach a published revision to whatever snapshot is current. Nothing\nmigrates the old values: a capture job is the wrong place for a migration, and\na rule that only reads cannot lose an editor''s value.\n\nRevisionDiffService now reads the pin through that same method instead of the\nproperty directly, so the comparison and the binder cannot disagree about what\nan entry is pinned to. Both their sessions now carry the language as a Locale,\nwithout which an i18n property has no translation subnode to resolve against\nand every pinned entry would read as unpinned.\n\nVerified on a running 8.2.4.0: crh:snapshotRef internationalized=false,\ncrh:pinnedSnapshot internationalized=true, module installs and starts clean.\n\nDefinitionLabelsTest caught the missing resource-bundle label for the new\nproperty before an editor would have seen a raw key.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d09ecac4f9b70f52223d4324e59c1d5f6e0dba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/9d09ecac4f9b70f52223d4324e59c1d5f6e0dba0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d09ecac4f9b70f52223d4324e59c1d5f6e0dba0\nparent eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788330634 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788330634 +0200\n\nfeat: make the revision pin per language, as a new property\n\nThe pin names a snapshot inside the PER-LANGUAGE folder\nrevision-history/<pageUuid>/<lang>/, and those names embed a per-language\ncontent hash, so a name valid in /en never resolves in /fr. One shared\nnon-i18n value could not express that: pinning an entry while editing in\nEnglish left the French comparison reporting \"no snapshot recorded\"\npermanently. The model could not represent the state, so it was not a bug in\nthe resolver.\n\nAdding `i18n` to crh:snapshotRef is NOT the fix, and this is measured on\n8.2.4.0 rather than assumed. Jahia''s DefinitionsBundleChecker classes a change\nof that flag on an existing property as a MAJOR definition change and cancels\nthe deployment outright:\n\n  ERROR [DefinitionsBundleChecker] - Major changes detected:\n  [nodeTypeName=crh:revisionEntry,type=MAJOR,\n   propDefDiffs={[itemName=crh:snapshotRef,type=MAJOR,operation=MODIFIED]}]\n  ... cancel module deployment\n\nSo crh:pinnedSnapshot is a NEW i18n property beside the old one, which is left\nbyte-for-byte unchanged. RevisionEntryBinder.pinnedSnapshotName reads the new\none first and falls back to the old, because an entry that silently lost its\npin would not fail loudly -- it would fall back to automatic binding and\nre-attach a published revision to whatever snapshot is current. Nothing\nmigrates the old values: a capture job is the wrong place for a migration, and\na rule that only reads cannot lose an editor''s value.\n\nRevisionDiffService now reads the pin through that same method instead of the\nproperty directly, so the comparison and the binder cannot disagree about what\nan entry is pinned to. Both their sessions now carry the language as a Locale,\nwithout which an i18n property has no translation subnode to resolve against\nand every pinned entry would read as unpinned.\n\nVerified on a running 8.2.4.0: crh:snapshotRef internationalized=false,\ncrh:pinnedSnapshot internationalized=true, module installs and starts clean.\n\nDefinitionLabelsTest caught the missing resource-bundle label for the new\nproperty before an editor would have seen a raw key.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXwooACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lpeggAl15qun/wm0gqd4uT+Q8QI8hMJ+QGwF0lJnnCiKse8LNdwmilbdkqr587\n9BfEmVSDu2MJNvT8GhPSnXqBk4aYUREpYs07xXlt/Yzy9rylbnFJoKq2SoEG6QM5\nau31BJm9UZcJ4+w1M9VlCNH4si0praef0UuujmUU4X29u2/DNnjGkRnjEJ2DYBJl\nSrPweEb8OWTGuqQoEUcbqzwtJ9P5+vWHhkENM+04m22Y2uV4ZPFOvyUmUzrs54us\nQK6hfhn4lyqMq6zuBeMvG3SMHgS/DvhI2G9kge6YtRyRf6YUbhQu1xUpv3K6cDEH\nOLhAAvITl8cYe1my7gmWok9KxAkY/A==\n=GVsC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T06:42:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGMxYjNlYjQ3OTliMmZkOWRlY2E0NWIyMzFmZDM0NjBlYjdjZWE0M2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff","sha":"eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff"}],"sha":"c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c1b3eb4799b2fd9deca45b231fd3460eb7cea43a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:00:08Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:00:08Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"docs: correct comments and docs that no longer describe the code\n\nA dedicated pass over comment rot, kept out of the fix commits so those stayed\nreviewable. Each of these was verified against the code, not taken on report.\nThe ones that could actively mislead someone making a decision come first.\n\nClaims that could cause a wrong call about safety:\n\n- RevisionDiffService and SnapshotChoiceListInitializer both asserted the\n  snapshot tree is \"locked down so that no ordinary user can read them\n  directly\". restoreInheritance repairs that pre-1.4 lockdown on every capture,\n  so any contributor with read on /sites/<site>/contents can open a snapshot in\n  jContent. A reviewer weighing whether a configured capture principal is safe\n  for a site would have read those as a guarantee and enabled it on that basis.\n- README said snapshot types carry jmix:hiddenType, contradicting its own\n  section above, the CND and the resource bundle. Read as written it told an\n  operator the store is hidden from contributors and therefore needs no\n  restricting.\n- RevisionHistoryConstants.CAPTURE_PRINCIPAL still called itself \"the one and\n  only principal a capture may run as\", fifty lines below a comment correcting\n  exactly that. A maintainer treating it as the invariant would hard-code guest\n  back into createSnapshot and stamp it on snapshots taken by a privileged\n  account.\n\nClaims that were simply false:\n\n- The CND said crh:revisionSnapshot carries jmix:droppableContent and that\n  jContent''s browse filter is includeTypes [jmix:droppableContent, jnt:page,\n  jnt:file]. That is the content PICKER''s filter, and it is the exact wrong\n  belief that left 28 snapshots present and 0 shown through two releases. The\n  browser filters flat views on [jmix:editorialContent, jmix:queryContent] and\n  recurses only into container types. 07-jcontentUi.cy.ts was written to kill\n  this belief; the CND was the last place still holding it.\n- A NOTE directly under the crh:snapshotRef declaration said \"there is\n  deliberately NO snapshotRef property here any more\".\n- RevisionEntryBinder said the rate limiter \"serialises attempts to one per\n  second\". It rejects, and bounds nothing about how long an accepted capture runs.\n- MarkdownNormalizer justified its input cap by \"this runs on a live render\n  thread for every publish\" and \"partial data beats a failed publish\". Capture\n  has been a background job since; there is no publish to fail. Its silent\n  truncation is now flagged as inconsistent with MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES, which\n  refuses rather than truncates.\n- The cache opt-out cited ?crhDiff=, which appears nowhere else in the module.\n- SnapshotCaptureJob claimed \"a missing snapshot always leaves a status\". A job\n  that never executes writes nothing; the gap and why it is not patched here are\n  now stated where the claim was.\n- MAX_CHOICES was justified against 500 as a hard cap; 500 is a default with no\n  ceiling, so a site above 100 has snapshots that cannot be pinned at all.\n- README promised re-pointing an entry at an unresolvable snapshot leaves it\n  unbound. repin leaves it on the snapshot it already had.\n- The editor-facing description of crh:entryRefs said \"set once and never\n  changed afterwards\", which repin deliberately does not honour.\n- The 1.4.0 notes said referenced snapshots are no longer pinned and retention\n  applies normally. The code never did that.\n\nTwo orphaned Javadoc blocks removed or reattached (SnapshotCaptureJob,\nSiteSettingsRegistry), same defect as the two fixed earlier this pass.\n\nRelease notes also amended for the behaviour changes made in this pass: the\ncapture endpoint is now refused rather than warned about, a field can be cleared,\nand retention.maxSnapshots = 1 is refused with a floor of 2.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"76de125708ceb1dca107a9037e4206881c253afe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/76de125708ceb1dca107a9037e4206881c253afe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff","verification":{"payload":"tree 76de125708ceb1dca107a9037e4206881c253afe\nparent 8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788328808 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788328808 +0200\n\ndocs: correct comments and docs that no longer describe the code\n\nA dedicated pass over comment rot, kept out of the fix commits so those stayed\nreviewable. Each of these was verified against the code, not taken on report.\nThe ones that could actively mislead someone making a decision come first.\n\nClaims that could cause a wrong call about safety:\n\n- RevisionDiffService and SnapshotChoiceListInitializer both asserted the\n  snapshot tree is \"locked down so that no ordinary user can read them\n  directly\". restoreInheritance repairs that pre-1.4 lockdown on every capture,\n  so any contributor with read on /sites/<site>/contents can open a snapshot in\n  jContent. A reviewer weighing whether a configured capture principal is safe\n  for a site would have read those as a guarantee and enabled it on that basis.\n- README said snapshot types carry jmix:hiddenType, contradicting its own\n  section above, the CND and the resource bundle. Read as written it told an\n  operator the store is hidden from contributors and therefore needs no\n  restricting.\n- RevisionHistoryConstants.CAPTURE_PRINCIPAL still called itself \"the one and\n  only principal a capture may run as\", fifty lines below a comment correcting\n  exactly that. A maintainer treating it as the invariant would hard-code guest\n  back into createSnapshot and stamp it on snapshots taken by a privileged\n  account.\n\nClaims that were simply false:\n\n- The CND said crh:revisionSnapshot carries jmix:droppableContent and that\n  jContent''s browse filter is includeTypes [jmix:droppableContent, jnt:page,\n  jnt:file]. That is the content PICKER''s filter, and it is the exact wrong\n  belief that left 28 snapshots present and 0 shown through two releases. The\n  browser filters flat views on [jmix:editorialContent, jmix:queryContent] and\n  recurses only into container types. 07-jcontentUi.cy.ts was written to kill\n  this belief; the CND was the last place still holding it.\n- A NOTE directly under the crh:snapshotRef declaration said \"there is\n  deliberately NO snapshotRef property here any more\".\n- RevisionEntryBinder said the rate limiter \"serialises attempts to one per\n  second\". It rejects, and bounds nothing about how long an accepted capture runs.\n- MarkdownNormalizer justified its input cap by \"this runs on a live render\n  thread for every publish\" and \"partial data beats a failed publish\". Capture\n  has been a background job since; there is no publish to fail. Its silent\n  truncation is now flagged as inconsistent with MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES, which\n  refuses rather than truncates.\n- The cache opt-out cited ?crhDiff=, which appears nowhere else in the module.\n- SnapshotCaptureJob claimed \"a missing snapshot always leaves a status\". A job\n  that never executes writes nothing; the gap and why it is not patched here are\n  now stated where the claim was.\n- MAX_CHOICES was justified against 500 as a hard cap; 500 is a default with no\n  ceiling, so a site above 100 has snapshots that cannot be pinned at all.\n- README promised re-pointing an entry at an unresolvable snapshot leaves it\n  unbound. repin leaves it on the snapshot it already had.\n- The editor-facing description of crh:entryRefs said \"set once and never\n  changed afterwards\", which repin deliberately does not honour.\n- The 1.4.0 notes said referenced snapshots are no longer pinned and retention\n  applies normally. The code never did that.\n\nTwo orphaned Javadoc blocks removed or reattached (SnapshotCaptureJob,\nSiteSettingsRegistry), same defect as the two fixed earlier this pass.\n\nRelease notes also amended for the behaviour changes made in this pass: the\ncapture endpoint is now refused rather than warned about, a field can be cleared,\nand retention.maxSnapshots = 1 is refused with a floor of 2.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXu2gACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lhNAgAzfJu6V7W2aJVmWNo1YkfHVg8ZUbxk1UbLHLLhEYSWaNPzr6uXhTJVrG0\nIvAgmYPxMbj3UCdJqTBlHdVSljMws4mbbty2K0PEHKi+P0dfMJw5RMbyzr1smjur\n3JEDm/SULNgKZoCR4zEzZtiZnmnrcNhGz9l3VVhbnlohMePJhwJ8HvbmRb8/nU1V\nI6a/gKwpk0Lm+Qi2DwwRNP4b5VNxKEnXQLjEa2p29x8anWR2PxoJbNP8aQtt+hIS\nG92QRzsYy10jO+33raFRZp0JLvHEwzyJiCaUn49kEET74VhjL3Hz/xA34l49666c\nuHldLZTui077fXR8uuRiwW+rn0/m2w==\n=sfxL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T06:00:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGVhZTdlZWNjYTQ2YTZhYmRjZGQ2ZWI0NzNkMGFkMmU5ZTRlOGJmZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6","sha":"8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6"}],"sha":"eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/eae7eecca46a6abdcdd6eb473d0ad2e9e4e8bfff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:53:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:53:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: stop the backfill aborting on every page that has a revision history\n\ncrh:revisionHistory sat in SELF_RENDERING, which put two correct intentions in\ndirect collision. Its markdown view renders empty on purpose, so a page''s own\nchangelog never lands inside the record it describes. fetchMarkdown refuses an\nempty 200 body, because splicing '''' into a reconstruction is how a page that\nchanged gets stored as one that did not. So fetching it threw, and every page\ncarrying the component aborted the run -- which is every page with captured\nhistory, and therefore exactly the page README tells you to backfill FIRST to\nprove the composition is faithful before touching pages that have none.\n\nWalking it instead would have been worse than the abort: the entries would render\nthrough the generic fallback, so each revision''s summary would land inside the\nsnapshot it describes and every later diff would show the changelog rather than\nthe change. It is now in its own set, neither fetched nor walked, contributing\nonly the line separator the parent view emits for any child whatever it rendered\n-- byte-identical to what the old code would have produced had fetchMarkdown\nreturned '''' instead of refusing.\n\nSecond drift, from the generator-5 change: content.jsp emits a container''s own\ntext properties between its title and its children, and compose emitted only the\ntitle. A container carrying its own text (a subtitle, say) was recorded live and\nlost in reconstruction, so the gate reported an unexplained MISMATCH -- or, forced\npast with ALLOW_UNEXPLAINED, stored snapshots permanently missing text. It now\ncalls the module''s own RevisionHistoryFunctions.textProperties reflectively,\nwhich is the same function the view calls, so the two cannot drift again.\n\nA third possible drift is documented in place and deliberately NOT acted on: the\nparent view emits a separator after a container module and this mirror does not,\nbut content.jsp also emits literal template newlines the mirror never reproduced,\nso the real delta needs a run to establish. The self-validation gate is that\nmeasurement and aborts rather than storing a mismatch.\n\nNot machine-checked: no Groovy CLI here. Verified by reading, and by confirming\nRevisionHistoryFunctions.textProperties(JCRNodeWrapper) is public static so the\nreflective lookup resolves.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"b1330641e3bc85fc85ee1b8418f31b70629892e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/b1330641e3bc85fc85ee1b8418f31b70629892e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6","verification":{"payload":"tree b1330641e3bc85fc85ee1b8418f31b70629892e8\nparent be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788328418 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788328418 +0200\n\nfix: stop the backfill aborting on every page that has a revision history\n\ncrh:revisionHistory sat in SELF_RENDERING, which put two correct intentions in\ndirect collision. Its markdown view renders empty on purpose, so a page''s own\nchangelog never lands inside the record it describes. fetchMarkdown refuses an\nempty 200 body, because splicing '''' into a reconstruction is how a page that\nchanged gets stored as one that did not. So fetching it threw, and every page\ncarrying the component aborted the run -- which is every page with captured\nhistory, and therefore exactly the page README tells you to backfill FIRST to\nprove the composition is faithful before touching pages that have none.\n\nWalking it instead would have been worse than the abort: the entries would render\nthrough the generic fallback, so each revision''s summary would land inside the\nsnapshot it describes and every later diff would show the changelog rather than\nthe change. It is now in its own set, neither fetched nor walked, contributing\nonly the line separator the parent view emits for any child whatever it rendered\n-- byte-identical to what the old code would have produced had fetchMarkdown\nreturned '''' instead of refusing.\n\nSecond drift, from the generator-5 change: content.jsp emits a container''s own\ntext properties between its title and its children, and compose emitted only the\ntitle. A container carrying its own text (a subtitle, say) was recorded live and\nlost in reconstruction, so the gate reported an unexplained MISMATCH -- or, forced\npast with ALLOW_UNEXPLAINED, stored snapshots permanently missing text. It now\ncalls the module''s own RevisionHistoryFunctions.textProperties reflectively,\nwhich is the same function the view calls, so the two cannot drift again.\n\nA third possible drift is documented in place and deliberately NOT acted on: the\nparent view emits a separator after a container module and this mirror does not,\nbut content.jsp also emits literal template newlines the mirror never reproduced,\nso the real delta needs a run to establish. The self-validation gate is that\nmeasurement and aborts rather than storing a mismatch.\n\nNot machine-checked: no Groovy CLI here. Verified by reading, and by confirming\nRevisionHistoryFunctions.textProperties(JCRNodeWrapper) is public static so the\nreflective lookup resolves.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXueIACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nh2QgAoGmMf+63jRBCb9CATrFAY6UWFttQIfRUMTmRG1jYvL+iEruZ0H2+WUDO\nadMmPXTpYSIJ28qnUXIrqPQH/u7sg3aDtzUjyMRVkdXG6XlOgZv0/xyAStEb+fFu\nY2J/0/Yh3P2YPx1kUCEEh38vVEGfz/c+2iA2cP12b912bsd5lKP9lzGvT8CWeu/3\n6Du8J0wnMCF6mQSd1+MEMjCLX4ONgEVIWuqvAeByI86dr9deoirwbcBXCQw7l38N\nWV7sfY9rz/PDQoBuHXez9TP3ibzWh2FMuo+ngmpT2VipXF4R47DcJBZ78EVglyAe\nF6bxQOQbaHwcJ8UA4h/Qif+MprmLsg==\n=n2YI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T06:00:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDhjMDZhN2UzMGIyM2JhNGU5NGNhZmMyMDIxOGMwYWU3Y2VkYzBlZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60","sha":"be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60"}],"sha":"8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8c06a7e30b23ba4e94cafc20218c0ae7cedc0ee6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:35:29Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:35:29Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: keep the editable capture account separate from the effective one\n\nA regression introduced earlier in this pass. Making captureUser report the\nEFFECTIVE account fixed the reporting defect and created a worse one: the panel\nbinds that field to an editable input, so a site inheriting the module-wide\naccount would display that name, and saving anything at all in the panel would\nwrite it as this site''s own capture.user. A site that names an account uses that\naccount''s credential and no other, and no per-site secret exists for it -- so\ncapture for that site would silently fall back to anonymous while the panel went\non showing the same name.\n\nTwo questions, two fields. captureUser is this site''s own value and stays empty\nwhen it has none, which is what the input edits. effectiveCaptureUser is what\ncapture actually renders as, read-only, and the help text names it when the site\nis inheriting -- so \"this site has no account of its own\" no longer reads as\n\"nothing privileged is captured here\", without putting a value in the input that\nsaving would adopt.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"5ca80b3204d3cca38434455c49bcf23f362af923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/5ca80b3204d3cca38434455c49bcf23f362af923"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ca80b3204d3cca38434455c49bcf23f362af923\nparent bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788327329 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788327329 +0200\n\nfix: keep the editable capture account separate from the effective one\n\nA regression introduced earlier in this pass. Making captureUser report the\nEFFECTIVE account fixed the reporting defect and created a worse one: the panel\nbinds that field to an editable input, so a site inheriting the module-wide\naccount would display that name, and saving anything at all in the panel would\nwrite it as this site''s own capture.user. A site that names an account uses that\naccount''s credential and no other, and no per-site secret exists for it -- so\ncapture for that site would silently fall back to anonymous while the panel went\non showing the same name.\n\nTwo questions, two fields. captureUser is this site''s own value and stays empty\nwhen it has none, which is what the input edits. effectiveCaptureUser is what\ncapture actually renders as, read-only, and the help text names it when the site\nis inheriting -- so \"this site has no account of its own\" no longer reads as\n\"nothing privileged is captured here\", without putting a value in the input that\nsaving would adopt.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXtaEACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nhFwgAxhaKWM9/FAU3dif34mJ+LIzqqa45ww2dprM/NQlMOhZK5PJxREUJyXPr\n0myTXXqOgM8U6Fl80evvrKaZjjDbf1/9H2+9yKWDjA//EY3ikIDCn0UeuSslkzbV\n5ljkWpEwworeXyL7ZWHvbtqX9+vWxVpDyAxjOruCBxnd6EdkV74v0W+4NUbgq4+M\nO1dUjc22S5zA2m6V0qI8RD/1GCTc9x9RQUVyBXfns1JSvMaL8nlezigeMbB4qQeg\nOHr8+SIiDDJ7T33VYHLfl0eVZBOP6zkzUVqU0BLCuk9fdBeicqPo/xqyIc41SJVD\nbXmTr8XmwP3mL5H/l0nhFA1ecvpO0Q==\n=2pLi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:43:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGJlOTdmN2E0ZmQzMDI5YWIwMTU1ZGMxZjZjMjQ1ZDU1ZTMzZjdiNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4","sha":"bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4"}],"sha":"be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/be97f7a4fd3029ab0155dc1f6c245d55e33f7b60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:31:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:31:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test: assert the retention contract, not the sentence that carried it\n\nThe e2e assertion required the refusal message to say \"at least 1\". That was an\nobservation of the wording rather than the property, and the wording itself was\nthe defect: prune never removes a page''s newest snapshot and runs before the\nincoming one is written, so a cap of 1 leaves the existing snapshot in place and\nthe folder settles at 2 forever. The module advertised a retention level it could\nnot deliver, and this test held it there.\n\nWhat it asserts now is the contract -- every value the module will not honour is\nrefused before it can reach the file -- and it covers 1 as well as 0, which is\nthe boundary that actually moved.\n\nAdds the matching case for the capture endpoint: an outward-facing baseUrl is\nrefused through the real mutation and never reaches the file. Nothing covered\nthat, which is how a site-scoped role could reach an arbitrary host.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e08a2fd4392b36582d3c48e7ba70c5926dcd933","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/9e08a2fd4392b36582d3c48e7ba70c5926dcd933"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e08a2fd4392b36582d3c48e7ba70c5926dcd933\nparent ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788327105 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788327105 +0200\n\ntest: assert the retention contract, not the sentence that carried it\n\nThe e2e assertion required the refusal message to say \"at least 1\". That was an\nobservation of the wording rather than the property, and the wording itself was\nthe defect: prune never removes a page''s newest snapshot and runs before the\nincoming one is written, so a cap of 1 leaves the existing snapshot in place and\nthe folder settles at 2 forever. The module advertised a retention level it could\nnot deliver, and this test held it there.\n\nWhat it asserts now is the contract -- every value the module will not honour is\nrefused before it can reach the file -- and it covers 1 as well as 0, which is\nthe boundary that actually moved.\n\nAdds the matching case for the capture endpoint: an outward-facing baseUrl is\nrefused through the real mutation and never reaches the file. Nothing covered\nthat, which is how a site-scoped role could reach an arbitrary host.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXtMEACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lIBAf/WwqdE+NeqigSHocWYq+bK5yBdU5A71O8ns2Fz2IdWNn5KEo/KJcFtPur\nLsTtjfnxrZRQBR4ieOiWCwOzr6Ira2cbrNzxBGPAX7M8g92de84T8r5/bPhdF+y+\nU+W2lcGaBKcUwCniE/nR0cXc+XGRWYTgYhL3kfjeEIYq455q5E+aou+6FBb2l5mp\n72SmwOWDkpM75YD+fxpPu9yq6isT1TyMZnSbRJVE9UarxSCq09BSP89bkCB+rmob\nu3Mqs37zD5qqRyS3WPxrCPXBp6de8Rz1vfd/sEbNbl57+UEQHBmitkJfP68Ouzso\nvTO8XPEkRE+bhw2HUwbchZeL3WndQw==\n=69Ru\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:32:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGJkNjczOTBkODM4OTY1ZTEwNTczODgyZjMzMjcyZDZlNTY1NzRiZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685","sha":"ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685"}],"sha":"bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/bd67390d838965e10573882f33272d6e56574be4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:26:13Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:26:13Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: stop pruning evidence a published revision still cites\n\nhasEntryReferences resolved crh:entryRefs through the capture session, which is\nalways `default`. An entry an editor deleted in jContent and has not published\nhas already vanished from there, while the PUBLISHED revision is still on the\nlive page citing that snapshot as the text it describes. Retention then deleted\nit -- and because crh:entryRefs lives on the snapshot, deleting the node also\ndestroyed the record that the entry ever described it, so the binder rebinds\nthat revision to the current text on the next capture and a years-old revision\nsilently begins claiming today''s page. Absent from `default` is not gone; `live`\nis now consulted before believing it.\n\nThe lookup is a package-private seam so pruning stays testable without a\nrepository. Letting a missing JCRTemplate decide would have made \"is this\nevidence still cited\" depend on whether a session could be opened, and that\nquestion has no safe default.\n\nThree smaller ones:\n\n- The backfill script normalised with the locale-less overload while live\n  capture uses the locale-aware one, reproducing in the migration script the\n  exact defect SnapshotCaptureJob records as fixed: a reconstructed zh or ja page\n  could never match a captured one, so the byte-for-byte gate aborted the run.\n- A requested comparison did not force the revision list open, contradicting both\n  the comment above the expression and the README. With JavaScript disabled the\n  panel named two revisions inside a <details> that stayed shut.\n- The app-shell dynamic import had no .catch, so a failed load became an\n  unhandled rejection: blank screen, and a console entry naming neither this\n  module nor what it was loading.\n\nNot machine-checked: no Groovy CLI is available here, so the backfill edit was\nverified by reading, and by confirming both reflected methods are public static.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"744660a158abed2f8377301fe2d79a9fcb7fa516","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/744660a158abed2f8377301fe2d79a9fcb7fa516"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685","verification":{"payload":"tree 744660a158abed2f8377301fe2d79a9fcb7fa516\nparent 552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788326773 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788326773 +0200\n\nfix: stop pruning evidence a published revision still cites\n\nhasEntryReferences resolved crh:entryRefs through the capture session, which is\nalways `default`. An entry an editor deleted in jContent and has not published\nhas already vanished from there, while the PUBLISHED revision is still on the\nlive page citing that snapshot as the text it describes. Retention then deleted\nit -- and because crh:entryRefs lives on the snapshot, deleting the node also\ndestroyed the record that the entry ever described it, so the binder rebinds\nthat revision to the current text on the next capture and a years-old revision\nsilently begins claiming today''s page. Absent from `default` is not gone; `live`\nis now consulted before believing it.\n\nThe lookup is a package-private seam so pruning stays testable without a\nrepository. Letting a missing JCRTemplate decide would have made \"is this\nevidence still cited\" depend on whether a session could be opened, and that\nquestion has no safe default.\n\nThree smaller ones:\n\n- The backfill script normalised with the locale-less overload while live\n  capture uses the locale-aware one, reproducing in the migration script the\n  exact defect SnapshotCaptureJob records as fixed: a reconstructed zh or ja page\n  could never match a captured one, so the byte-for-byte gate aborted the run.\n- A requested comparison did not force the revision list open, contradicting both\n  the comment above the expression and the README. With JavaScript disabled the\n  panel named two revisions inside a <details> that stayed shut.\n- The app-shell dynamic import had no .catch, so a failed load became an\n  unhandled rejection: blank screen, and a console entry naming neither this\n  module nor what it was loading.\n\nNot machine-checked: no Groovy CLI is available here, so the backfill edit was\nverified by reading, and by confirming both reflected methods are public static.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXs3UACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mRsggAnTSMqxgAZsj1EgUo0e6VH5/ypqgBPAaFRPg8sacEvkoIkx0TI/PJ3n02\n9cyko2gqv3Uve8xP11sFJ2ejMeAwMDNL+/WsGxrKf2HcSirnWIZTmtb1rBMqX07/\nnwfHquqYpQg+mijgM0imZFZPKtaBVBoi0F/PFTN9mwYjmmNAir/+PaTFHQ02jg3Z\nF0nWl4TVJRZkFICvji+03LUDZXS+uGhsKKmYIk3M9qPMEQNq5Y+icG+tuZxQ6TRD\n0epOybuj1DQ05p4W/nfN9ydEzgI6J9V276MoyuZ55V6HHQwy6Qv52LL2RMM2MMZD\n6obWFQ9UTJZFIp1zt6cuPA0bv5jrVg==\n=hTXl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:26:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGVkMzljODRjMDBiNDRjMTg0ZmRjMGU3MTgxYTg3MzA2Yzk4NmQ2ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a","sha":"552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a"}],"sha":"ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/ed39c84c00b44c184fdc0e7181a87306c986d685"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:36:02Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:36:02Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: keep an operator''s comments when rewriting a per-site config file\n\npreservedLines skipped comment lines instead of keeping them, so every note in a\nhand-edited .cfg was deleted on the next save from the panel. The secret itself\nsurvived; the line saying who owns it and when it was last rotated did not, which\nloses the provenance of a live credential silently and with nothing recording\nthat anything was dropped.\n\nA comment run now travels with the key below it. A run above a key this module\nrewrites is discarded rather than left describing a value it no longer matches.\n\nThe loop is an if/else chain rather than early continues: three of them tripped\njava:S135, which was the single new maintainability issue failing the quality\ngate, and the nesting here is shallow enough that guard clauses bought nothing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf430670176a7e5130ce4b250c2799407f8fd8e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/cf430670176a7e5130ce4b250c2799407f8fd8e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a","verification":{"payload":"tree cf430670176a7e5130ce4b250c2799407f8fd8e5\nparent 38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294962 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294962 +0200\n\nfix: keep an operator''s comments when rewriting a per-site config file\n\npreservedLines skipped comment lines instead of keeping them, so every note in a\nhand-edited .cfg was deleted on the next save from the panel. The secret itself\nsurvived; the line saying who owns it and when it was last rotated did not, which\nloses the provenance of a live credential silently and with nothing recording\nthat anything was dropped.\n\nA comment run now travels with the key below it. A run above a key this module\nrewrites is discarded rather than left describing a value it no longer matches.\n\nThe loop is an if/else chain rather than early continues: three of them tripped\njava:S135, which was the single new maintainability issue failing the quality\ngate, and the nesting here is shallow enough that guard clauses bought nothing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXNzIACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kW0Qf/Y2elggHaHRHr8sBeLTRVumlO36eq0vUgM+cPyITIqrUk7MKhdYXJtvLH\niUIoMrXCBZKfuT4LzCmy7Wnh6qDrcOB9uO8TSf8RiEEREE4E6GOotNRnbdUyPse8\nfERJsjobts2tN10w9kzWdvLORmapNEcYwHxlQr76/hbAstlSlg/kzmi9MqdWt70f\nI/XOKDAX++ZMTZAJ+lvMUQBpw+COdbADVSfaIO96UFxLDNYI0xYsuTwcBExmcvHO\nFo3BBPaKML7DwEb4WNJUJf5dcu4oBypHCpK+x2jIoIQ1oxa3EgCaTf6cD5J+7T5Y\n9P3RFJJcXm/ejFQ3N3jaoW5AiW9SOQ==\n=G3pS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:16:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDU1MmU1MGM3MDVlMDc1NjVmOWFkZmUwOTM2M2Q1ODc1Y2ViMTVhMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5","sha":"38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5"}],"sha":"552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/552e50c705e07565f9adfe09363d5875ceb15a0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:31:02Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:31:02Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test: prove the credential guard on the wire, not in the predicate\n\nreachesJahiaDirectly was already pinned by a unit test, and that proved nothing\nabout the guard: it could be deleted from doFetch, or inverted, and every one of\nthose assertions would still pass. The property is about the request that leaves\nthe JVM, so the test now observes the request that leaves the JVM.\n\nBoth branches get a live server and the test stays hermetic, because the whole\n127/8 range is loopback to the kernel while reachesJahiaDirectly matches the host\nliterally and anchored: 127.0.0.2 is bindable and reachable, and is correctly\n\"not this node''s own connector\" as far as the guard is concerned.\n\nVerified by mutation rather than by watching it pass. With the guard disabled the\ntwo withholding tests fail and name the transmitted header, so they are sensitive\nto the thing they are about:\n\n  expected: <null> but was: <Basic Y3JoLWNhcHR1cmU6...>\n\nAlso covered, all previously untested: save() refusing an outward-facing\nendpoint and a retention cap below the achievable floor, every loopback spelling\naccepted and the near-misses rejected (localhost.example.com, 127.0.0.2), the\nrule that a site naming its own account never inherits the module-wide\ncredential, and statusForHttp''s authenticated branch, where a refused capture\naccount is a misconfiguration rather than a private page.\n\n224 -> 234 unit tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c785cab9b73df35f838c1368fe0507800779937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/2c785cab9b73df35f838c1368fe0507800779937"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c785cab9b73df35f838c1368fe0507800779937\nparent 4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294662 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294662 +0200\n\ntest: prove the credential guard on the wire, not in the predicate\n\nreachesJahiaDirectly was already pinned by a unit test, and that proved nothing\nabout the guard: it could be deleted from doFetch, or inverted, and every one of\nthose assertions would still pass. The property is about the request that leaves\nthe JVM, so the test now observes the request that leaves the JVM.\n\nBoth branches get a live server and the test stays hermetic, because the whole\n127/8 range is loopback to the kernel while reachesJahiaDirectly matches the host\nliterally and anchored: 127.0.0.2 is bindable and reachable, and is correctly\n\"not this node''s own connector\" as far as the guard is concerned.\n\nVerified by mutation rather than by watching it pass. With the guard disabled the\ntwo withholding tests fail and name the transmitted header, so they are sensitive\nto the thing they are about:\n\n  expected: <null> but was: <Basic Y3JoLWNhcHR1cmU6...>\n\nAlso covered, all previously untested: save() refusing an outward-facing\nendpoint and a retention cap below the achievable floor, every loopback spelling\naccepted and the near-misses rejected (localhost.example.com, 127.0.0.2), the\nrule that a site naming its own account never inherits the module-wide\ncredential, and statusForHttp''s authenticated branch, where a refused capture\naccount is a misconfiguration rather than a private page.\n\n224 -> 234 unit tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXNgYACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3k5hggAobfO8henBvzpWS+ErTbFr2fuiaoA1MG0ibuv4yqJwz5dRi7sxN9W+ve5\n/GWJy2/I24XeFb4U6gcepfkt9fgvRjBoZ2QQah+lakoITasUBtTz58CllBF3uC3S\nWbrd3hqJtgox+H0vC2lh4h13l0ACWgTGBjspf0CJqtroKEQaZVS3SyBUpsHF8Cez\n8h04waclwVRLS/xaiN38u/qHRqtj54du0EdcoruVq4yeYOaLdVrxZf++WY32+mr0\nuWNoDqKTwTssAbg3IAjU1gXog/ssfyiFnfrWtXIgxKaVhRunXmT3jBurH7mS9Due\n8C+6XU2TdC5eMRQCwWXTbuCqAjIPLQ==\n=sG6A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:16:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDM4YWY0MWUyODg1NGJlMGFlYTIwNDkxYjViZDY1NmY5Zjc3N2Q5YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956","sha":"4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956"}],"sha":"38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/38af41e28854be0aea20491b5bd656f9f777d9c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: honour the guarantees these three classes advertise\n\n- CaptureStatus had two doc comments in a row, so \"Rendering or storing threw\"\n  attached to nothing and FAILED -- the most operationally important value --\n  shipped undocumented.\n- RevisionDiffView says it is immutable and returned live Calendar objects.\n  Copied on the way out.\n- SiteSettingsAccess.registry() threw a raw IllegalStateException, the exact\n  pattern requireSiteAdmin''s own comment argues against, so an administrator\n  opening the panel during a bundle restart saw \"Internal Server Error(s) while\n  executing query\" instead of \"retry shortly\".\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"755c8afee4e4c59d642c50d6845af654bc9fcbfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/755c8afee4e4c59d642c50d6845af654bc9fcbfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956","verification":{"payload":"tree 755c8afee4e4c59d642c50d6845af654bc9fcbfc\nparent 605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294412 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294412 +0200\n\nfix: honour the guarantees these three classes advertise\n\n- CaptureStatus had two doc comments in a row, so \"Rendering or storing threw\"\n  attached to nothing and FAILED -- the most operationally important value --\n  shipped undocumented.\n- RevisionDiffView says it is immutable and returned live Calendar objects.\n  Copied on the way out.\n- SiteSettingsAccess.registry() threw a raw IllegalStateException, the exact\n  pattern requireSiteAdmin''s own comment argues against, so an administrator\n  opening the panel during a bundle restart saw \"Internal Server Error(s) while\n  executing query\" instead of \"retry shortly\".\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXNQwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nmoAgAgZ2AEThunZGaRyFFE0hCBJvEze4JuhRQGX9mYJpPB6rJvesLC/e/Fs7X\n+91xKkr2icZrhoBsFIbJNJRdU/y6RyCrv6j53m2Sb92GsCs3+2JKeF8oGQ20PeXF\nePt6IlLn4qi1AVzbUOStYiyymbpPWcrwUpOKzqLSL+68aXDz34TtBT5NBw7qDcaW\nckp6Vlnq0fOgre1MFVQuwAhwXW4GUyb4H9CgmxtlTUn5s3jqfaoqeeWvQk2Lfq+B\nTrel5044uGi3ys62MLCKNBIQplt/pUoeDcLaRwEEQZyc4HaAIJdsFmmyfACY+eNr\nTQz6jLuDnRc9Z3z0NT7FbGmReZT9+A==\n=WxVn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:16:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDQyMDFjYWUyMTc1NTJmZTRiNzUzNWNlNzlkOGRkMTNlMjZmZDI5NTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a","sha":"605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a"}],"sha":"4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4201cae217552fe4b7535ce79d8dd13e26fd2956"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: make the comparison panel''s focus, state and ordering correct\n\nAccessibility, against WCAG 2.2 AAA:\n\n- The panel''s focus ring used the accent, which is 7.40:1 on white but about\n  2.2:1 against the darkened ::backdrop it actually sits on once the panel is a\n  popup -- under the 3:1 floor, on the one element the script moves focus to by\n  itself (SC 2.4.13). White outline in the popup state, accent kept as an inner\n  ring.\n- The settings panel''s role=\"status\" region rendered '''' as children and changed\n  only its title, which Banner surfaces as the region''s aria-label. A live region\n  announces changed content, so the state change after a Save was silent (SC\n  4.1.3). This is the same defect already fixed on the two Banners above it.\n- The snapshot preview lacked overflow-wrap, so a long captured URL scrolled the\n  narrow box sideways instead of wrapping (SC 1.4.10).\n\nCorrectness in the same file:\n\n- Overlapping comparisons applied whichever response arrived last, so the slower\n  first request could land after the second and leave the panel showing a\n  comparison that did not match the selected revisions. Each submission now\n  takes a sequence number and only the newest is applied.\n- Resubmitting while maximised left crh-diff-panel--full on the panel while the\n  replacement toggle came back reporting aria-pressed=\"false\" (SC 4.1.2).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"16fe1100563467a3bf3149b3d0a3f8aca5142d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/16fe1100563467a3bf3149b3d0a3f8aca5142d92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a","verification":{"payload":"tree 16fe1100563467a3bf3149b3d0a3f8aca5142d92\nparent 9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294412 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294412 +0200\n\nfix: make the comparison panel''s focus, state and ordering correct\n\nAccessibility, against WCAG 2.2 AAA:\n\n- The panel''s focus ring used the accent, which is 7.40:1 on white but about\n  2.2:1 against the darkened ::backdrop it actually sits on once the panel is a\n  popup -- under the 3:1 floor, on the one element the script moves focus to by\n  itself (SC 2.4.13). White outline in the popup state, accent kept as an inner\n  ring.\n- The settings panel''s role=\"status\" region rendered '''' as children and changed\n  only its title, which Banner surfaces as the region''s aria-label. A live region\n  announces changed content, so the state change after a Save was silent (SC\n  4.1.3). This is the same defect already fixed on the two Banners above it.\n- The snapshot preview lacked overflow-wrap, so a long captured URL scrolled the\n  narrow box sideways instead of wrapping (SC 1.4.10).\n\nCorrectness in the same file:\n\n- Overlapping comparisons applied whichever response arrived last, so the slower\n  first request could land after the second and leave the panel showing a\n  comparison that did not match the selected revisions. Each submission now\n  takes a sequence number and only the newest is applied.\n- Resubmitting while maximised left crh-diff-panel--full on the panel while the\n  replacement toggle came back reporting aria-pressed=\"false\" (SC 4.1.2).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXNQwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lv4QgAoEPpncusIm73jl9iVTxJAfgWTPWQr0cX+PLIZsPrmF4YIh/W3aeWhnKD\nh5WRRm53xr9m5zDkD9C1lWSGeXmzyxch57l/vwDcY/Czorll5pkIci+Be85c4kO+\nFs8/Ms9OIgL92fMeSqR171A273Xc8PPHidD5vkYFrmAzOi10Iaw2bSNydzYtVA+f\nj6xfZLCnfHDnAA8A+JCLku9yt7dKH8P9B5qM1d5M4/DZmCGXuSPkokgHdfh2xTgN\nLS8M9nzn+rB4LlTA9XrvGNI6UcsJK+rEdwCyEs9cKErne65WYiTwizr0qSt9QmUW\nN7GAkOIZcoqg38OpcPNE8JyzoYBTYw==\n=NWlA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:16:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDYwNTMxMzUzNWVhMDEzOGJlYTdlYjhiZTQxMGEzMTVhZDFhNDI2NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c","sha":"9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c"}],"sha":"605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/605313535ea0138bea7eb8be410a315ad1a4265a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: withhold the backfill credential from a non-loopback endpoint\n\nThe README states as a critical security note that a capture credential is sent\nonly to loopback addresses. The module''s Java path does that. The Groovy backfill\nscript shipped in the same module warned about a non-loopback BASE_URL and then\nsent the Authorization header to it anyway -- so an operator setting BASE_URL to\nthe address they know base64-encoded a real account''s password to a public host\nand whatever proxy, CDN or WAF logs sit in front of it. Warning about a value\nwhile still sending the password to it is worse than not warning.\n\nThe pre-commit hook that exists because this leak already happened once was\nanchored on a literal `String X = ` prefix, so Groovy''s other idiomatic\ndeclarations passed straight through, and its general net required 12 characters\nwhere this repository''s own documented test default is 8. Both widened.\n\nNot verified end to end: the environment guard refuses shell commands containing\ncredential-shaped assignments, which is correct, so the new patterns were checked\nfor shell syntax but not exercised against a staged sample.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e269b323e1d2436e92c53e7b9c661adcadaab09e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/e269b323e1d2436e92c53e7b9c661adcadaab09e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c","verification":{"payload":"tree e269b323e1d2436e92c53e7b9c661adcadaab09e\nparent 6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294412 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294412 +0200\n\nfix: withhold the backfill credential from a non-loopback endpoint\n\nThe README states as a critical security note that a capture credential is sent\nonly to loopback addresses. The module''s Java path does that. The Groovy backfill\nscript shipped in the same module warned about a non-loopback BASE_URL and then\nsent the Authorization header to it anyway -- so an operator setting BASE_URL to\nthe address they know base64-encoded a real account''s password to a public host\nand whatever proxy, CDN or WAF logs sit in front of it. Warning about a value\nwhile still sending the password to it is worse than not warning.\n\nThe pre-commit hook that exists because this leak already happened once was\nanchored on a literal `String X = ` prefix, so Groovy''s other idiomatic\ndeclarations passed straight through, and its general net required 12 characters\nwhere this repository''s own documented test default is 8. Both widened.\n\nNot verified end to end: the environment guard refuses shell commands containing\ncredential-shaped assignments, which is correct, so the new patterns were checked\nfor shell syntax but not exercised against a staged sample.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXNQwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mRnwgAywJ5wFyQAY3wdOHAkTquQcTZ3l3Mfn7E0kgiupnyUqByUdSM0VbJpX+F\nASVg77Yo2VRVJrXsZpZQs0U9jZ+RsL/bIvDT5cHLhFZEPFa/h1VqO33uUy14A5ZJ\n+EJVeVbQnElBotYf3Z+yq26MQYO7VQzvcvYhu3qkI7dN/gdVkVJCcNXX4YLwRC9t\nhFKoEo0/iXX8dWgY3qKitLyE+PWcYoHu9pYumr4PT4cTLPHi5B987Sy7XoNJF3E7\nMhQ7+86ccnqlncJ+ZgnyQADPHnqJ/x8CWTQLFrktcwvyIKqiaTwlLVe7E1/wlaB+\n4tXxR4KZpVjkqVqPKW7nJk24kRReHw==\n=PqlU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:16:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDlmZjU1YzgzNDVmMDUyMDc0Y2VlNzhmNDJmZGExOWRiMGNjMjNiNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da","sha":"6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da"}],"sha":"9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/9ff55c8345f052074cee78f42fda19db0cc23b6c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: never record one language''s failure against another, and authorise the page\n\nThree correctness fixes, all in the class of defect this module exists to\nprevent: a durable record that asserts something untrue.\n\ncaptureOnePageSafely caught around the whole per-language loop and then wrote\nFAILED for EVERY language of the page. capture() leaves settingsFor(), the rate\nlimiter, the cache flush and fetch() outside its own try, so a throw on the\nsecond language of a bilingual page overwrote the first language''s already\ndurable STORED with FAILED. A stored snapshot whose folder says the capture\nfailed, and no later capture corrects it. The catch is now scoped to the\nlanguage that actually threw; a failure to resolve the page still records all\nof them, because there no language was attempted.\n\nRevisionDiffService authorised the history component but served snapshots of the\nenclosing page, read with a system session. Its Javadoc justified this on the\ngrounds that reading the component implies reading the page -- which holds only\nwhile the component inherits the page''s ACLs. An editor breaking inheritance to\npublish a changelog on a restricted page (a reasonable thing to want) falsified\nit, and the flattened text of the restricted page was then served to anyone the\ncomponent was opened to. It now checks the object whose content is returned.\n\nCaptureEndpoint cleared its static state unconditionally on @Deactivate, unlike\nthe two sibling components that guard the same race and carry a comment\nasserting it is real. Made consistent: the failure it prevents is silent.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"41ed043e36a271e6480f6425921f78d806e6a91d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/41ed043e36a271e6480f6425921f78d806e6a91d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da","verification":{"payload":"tree 41ed043e36a271e6480f6425921f78d806e6a91d\nparent 3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294412 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294412 +0200\n\nfix: never record one language''s failure against another, and authorise the page\n\nThree correctness fixes, all in the class of defect this module exists to\nprevent: a durable record that asserts something untrue.\n\ncaptureOnePageSafely caught around the whole per-language loop and then wrote\nFAILED for EVERY language of the page. capture() leaves settingsFor(), the rate\nlimiter, the cache flush and fetch() outside its own try, so a throw on the\nsecond language of a bilingual page overwrote the first language''s already\ndurable STORED with FAILED. A stored snapshot whose folder says the capture\nfailed, and no later capture corrects it. The catch is now scoped to the\nlanguage that actually threw; a failure to resolve the page still records all\nof them, because there no language was attempted.\n\nRevisionDiffService authorised the history component but served snapshots of the\nenclosing page, read with a system session. Its Javadoc justified this on the\ngrounds that reading the component implies reading the page -- which holds only\nwhile the component inherits the page''s ACLs. An editor breaking inheritance to\npublish a changelog on a restricted page (a reasonable thing to want) falsified\nit, and the flattened text of the restricted page was then served to anyone the\ncomponent was opened to. It now checks the object whose content is returned.\n\nCaptureEndpoint cleared its static state unconditionally on @Deactivate, unlike\nthe two sibling components that guard the same race and carry a comment\nasserting it is real. Made consistent: the failure it prevents is silent.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXNQwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kbewf+Ok2+7R5MwGZxM326COTgRUO8/WHF7tF7Yl1lEoqM/bxqZQEFnRitGprF\n4SL3FrsjfgY+KmebdAiYcK1KulMB0YOeLrlryZ8/9eFr23pEeqiuGTWfNCaXx/q5\nvcQtZBBekJIukFp9WiNV2aauNdf/59lROzXAkM3t/Si8iqQ7d4tK/ZGPMeOCZHcv\nKUcGqwd4oGoR6ydmhQAEs0BRS5Qt1lKaoiRYta2w0h28tE1gFZV4UJAZ/BP6o2tG\nna3u3oA1d7e2SKG/G7RuDueRyt/w/u7gNjwPLx93VNgQAP1AFM8q6oSpolWriLpO\n5fYgUm4ar/c689kN/aL+Fzh0dX8IFQ==\n=9inY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:16:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDYyODZhMWMxNTkwODMxNWY5NTdiOWZkOTllZTdmMGRjNDAxNjkyZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097","sha":"3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097"}],"sha":"6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6286a1c15908315f957b9fd99ee7f0dc401692da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:26:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: refuse a capture endpoint that does not address this node\n\ncapture.baseUrl decides which host the server issues its capture GET to, and\nwhatever answers is normalised and stored as that site''s public revision\nsnapshot. The value is writable by a SITE administrator through the settings\npanel, so a role scoped to one site could obtain an arbitrary outbound GET from\ninside the network plus a forged record of what a page said. Two blind reviews\nfound this independently, and GuestMarkdownFetcher''s own Javadoc claimed \"no\nSSRF surface: the caller cannot influence the host\" -- true only before the\nvalue became site-configurable.\n\nsave() now refuses a non-loopback endpoint, and the mutation refuses it first so\nthe administrator gets a validation error naming the field. updated() still\naccepts one from the file itself: the escape hatch exists for a server\nadministrator who owns karaf/etc, and they already hold every privilege it\nwould grant.\n\nAlso, because a bad endpoint now has to be recoverable: an empty string clears a\nfield, where previously null was the only way to say \"no value\" and was read as\n\"leave unchanged\" -- so neither captureUser nor baseUrl could ever be emptied\nonce set.\n\nTwo credential-reporting defects found alongside it:\n\n- A site naming its own capture.user silently inherited the module-wide\n  credential whenever its own failed to resolve, inverting the documented rule\n  that a user without a usable secret leaves capture anonymous. A site scoped to\n  a narrow account was captured with the broad one.\n- The panel read captureUser/credentialResolved from this site''s own file only,\n  so a site with no file of its own was reported \"anonymous\" while its captures\n  authenticated module-wide -- inviting an administrator to publish a revision\n  history for a page holding restricted content.\n\nBoth now go through one rule, and withChanges no longer carries a resolved\ncredential across a change of account.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"66d6a978e583f7406dd41ceaf70e3ef83053500a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/66d6a978e583f7406dd41ceaf70e3ef83053500a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097","verification":{"payload":"tree 66d6a978e583f7406dd41ceaf70e3ef83053500a\nparent 1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294383 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788294383 +0200\n\nfix: refuse a capture endpoint that does not address this node\n\ncapture.baseUrl decides which host the server issues its capture GET to, and\nwhatever answers is normalised and stored as that site''s public revision\nsnapshot. The value is writable by a SITE administrator through the settings\npanel, so a role scoped to one site could obtain an arbitrary outbound GET from\ninside the network plus a forged record of what a page said. Two blind reviews\nfound this independently, and GuestMarkdownFetcher''s own Javadoc claimed \"no\nSSRF surface: the caller cannot influence the host\" -- true only before the\nvalue became site-configurable.\n\nsave() now refuses a non-loopback endpoint, and the mutation refuses it first so\nthe administrator gets a validation error naming the field. updated() still\naccepts one from the file itself: the escape hatch exists for a server\nadministrator who owns karaf/etc, and they already hold every privilege it\nwould grant.\n\nAlso, because a bad endpoint now has to be recoverable: an empty string clears a\nfield, where previously null was the only way to say \"no value\" and was read as\n\"leave unchanged\" -- so neither captureUser nor baseUrl could ever be emptied\nonce set.\n\nTwo credential-reporting defects found alongside it:\n\n- A site naming its own capture.user silently inherited the module-wide\n  credential whenever its own failed to resolve, inverting the documented rule\n  that a user without a usable secret leaves capture anonymous. A site scoped to\n  a narrow account was captured with the broad one.\n- The panel read captureUser/credentialResolved from this site''s own file only,\n  so a site with no file of its own was reported \"anonymous\" while its captures\n  authenticated module-wide -- inviting an administrator to publish a revision\n  history for a page holding restricted content.\n\nBoth now go through one rule, and withChanges no longer carries a resolved\ncredential across a change of account.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXNO8ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nl4wf/ROokHTq5e9Y0FY8fTe6dkzAUvrs02JOWDcGqv4y8TcO6tDmynEZMq3fv\n8c+MwugZ3lKxuXoeqcjB3QK8RSFHxSWxk9qFbyDQ0rAb5aYxao+ICZ3P3voljsxb\nDl+8z1oHgmESsBJM/j62cdi94EqlDmY7QEU2SIkGFLFIIwbmVS1Aw2DeBOUnEZ9q\ntN1mAyBfAtlk3C+dUujwuDRTkM1/2qEI6ahAadNJLHvLiP7VNGo7KBA3liTn2Za1\nfMKcd8H2Eb2Ug8+sreUY5KG1yCYmywE69HJ5aI1lI4m3FRjkAPDop0SaSIuBj3FG\nU5RsJdG8/gOBjn1SJZkizPZARf57lQ==\n=hAbV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T05:16:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDM5MjZlMTdkMDE2MGEzOGQ4YWFlODljMzQ3ZjlkOGM5NzRjMzcwOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066","sha":"1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066"}],"sha":"3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/3926e17d0160a38d8aae89c347f9d8c974c37097"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T19:30:43Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T19:30:43Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"docs: reconcile the README and write 1.4.0 release notes\n\nPhase 7 of the quality pass, delegated to a documentation agent working from the\ncode rather than from the README, then corrected on two points I could verify it\nhad got wrong.\n\nREADME gains the one thing the code does that it did not say: a configured capture\ncredential is sent ONLY to this node''s loopback connector, and is withheld for any\nother capture.baseUrl. That is the control which stops a site administrator\npointing baseUrl at a host they own and receiving the operator''s capture password,\nso an operator needs to know it exists before wondering why their restricted pages\nreport NOT_PUBLIC.\n\nRELEASE-NOTES-1.4.0.md covers 1_3_1..HEAD grouped by what changes for an operator\nor editor rather than by commit.\n\nTwo corrections to the delegated draft:\n\n- It said \"Required Actions: None\", which is wrong for the one case that matters.\n  An operator who captures restricted pages with a non-loopback capture.baseUrl\n  will find the credential withheld and those pages silently recorded NOT_PUBLIC.\n  That is a behaviour change requiring action, not a no-op, and it is now stated as\n  required rather than recommended.\n- It did not mention the generator version at all, which is the most visible\n  consequence of the upgrade. GENERATOR_VERSION moves 4 to 5 because the generic\n  fallback view now emits every text-bearing property instead of only jcr:title, so\n  the same unchanged page composes different Markdown. Two things follow and both\n  will be seen: one extra snapshot per revisioned page on the first publication\n  after upgrading, and a comparison spanning the upgrade showing the content the\n  older generator was dropping. Neither is a fault, but discovering either without\n  warning would read as one.\n\nThe \"behaves exactly as 1.3.1\" compatibility claim is qualified for the same\nreason.\n\nNo code, test, pom or hook was touched.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"856528cdc7021a2f385c56b53e7284db1907c872","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/856528cdc7021a2f385c56b53e7284db1907c872"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066","verification":{"payload":"tree 856528cdc7021a2f385c56b53e7284db1907c872\nparent cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788291043 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788291043 +0200\n\ndocs: reconcile the README and write 1.4.0 release notes\n\nPhase 7 of the quality pass, delegated to a documentation agent working from the\ncode rather than from the README, then corrected on two points I could verify it\nhad got wrong.\n\nREADME gains the one thing the code does that it did not say: a configured capture\ncredential is sent ONLY to this node''s loopback connector, and is withheld for any\nother capture.baseUrl. That is the control which stops a site administrator\npointing baseUrl at a host they own and receiving the operator''s capture password,\nso an operator needs to know it exists before wondering why their restricted pages\nreport NOT_PUBLIC.\n\nRELEASE-NOTES-1.4.0.md covers 1_3_1..HEAD grouped by what changes for an operator\nor editor rather than by commit.\n\nTwo corrections to the delegated draft:\n\n- It said \"Required Actions: None\", which is wrong for the one case that matters.\n  An operator who captures restricted pages with a non-loopback capture.baseUrl\n  will find the credential withheld and those pages silently recorded NOT_PUBLIC.\n  That is a behaviour change requiring action, not a no-op, and it is now stated as\n  required rather than recommended.\n- It did not mention the generator version at all, which is the most visible\n  consequence of the upgrade. GENERATOR_VERSION moves 4 to 5 because the generic\n  fallback view now emits every text-bearing property instead of only jcr:title, so\n  the same unchanged page composes different Markdown. Two things follow and both\n  will be seen: one extra snapshot per revisioned page on the first publication\n  after upgrading, and a comparison spanning the upgrade showing the content the\n  older generator was dropping. Neither is a fault, but discovering either without\n  warning would read as one.\n\nThe \"behaves exactly as 1.3.1\" compatibility claim is qualified for the same\nreason.\n\nNo code, test, pom or hook was touched.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXJ+MACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nksQf/X698dpfBnJxFWUAzJS3KF409+vpbrafp/uaRdmB+pGUfPUuIH81yKzQ/\nKimE1zd75KBkgfRRi9SmLyS16lAn+AhWzwmmL2iP7EvNNL2FRa+4ynZdm8gYrsn9\ncV+7lt3bPb7F7aiEHRjdh+0K9fdtkbRQql9Nzj6EHmrRJ6doVVD1Hxmb9JwrDOQc\n4PKF4f7rKKoujoke/xkoF2fungC2FnZ5axInbKfYo+7P3e6kAgjUn7dlxht2HPfq\nyqRoLnCvN1OqrcSFPBsnxBobm25zZILVLMpdYwjVuWNK7jZrXQl1xnhhAi3bSKxC\nGd/A03suOS7uQHMwS2TfsZw2Dj5www==\n=ZaSF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T19:30:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDFhYTExZWU4MzRiNjY1MjJmMjE4NzIxZjgwZDZhMDg0NDRiZTkwNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83","sha":"cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83"}],"sha":"1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1aa11ee834b66522f218721f80d6a08444be9066"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T18:37:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T18:37:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(security): bind the capture credential to loopback, and close four config-file holes\n\nThe blind security review of this branch found that one of my own earlier fixes\ncreated an escalation. Preserving capture.secret and capture.secretFile across a\npanel save was correct on its own, but it removed an accidental mitigation: before\nit, a save dropped the secret and capture fell back to anonymous, so nothing went\nout. With the secret preserved and capture.baseUrl still only WARNED about, a site\nadministrator could set baseUrl to a host they control and receive\nAuthorization: Basic with the operator''s capture password on the next publication.\n\nThe credential is now sent only when the destination is this node''s own loopback\nconnector, using the reachesJahiaDirectly predicate that already existed for the\nwarning. That closes it however baseUrl was set, and because the recorded principal\nis derived from what is actually sent, the snapshot is correctly marked guest\nrather than claiming privileged provenance for an anonymous render.\n\nFour more holes in the same file, each verified against java.util.Properties\nsemantics rather than assumed:\n\n- singleLine refused a newline but not a BACKSLASH, which is the properties escape\n  character; a trailing one continues the value onto the next line and consumes the\n  setting written after it, so capture.baseUrl could be made to vanish while the\n  panel reported it as applied. Backslashes are now refused outright.\n- indexOfSeparator read only ''='' and '':'', but whitespace is also a legal separator,\n  so a hand-written `capture.enabled false` was classed as unmanaged and\n  re-appended BELOW the module''s own line, where the last occurrence wins. The file\n  then said the opposite of what the panel reported.\n- The file was read as UTF-8 and written as UTF-8, though a properties file is\n  ISO-8859-1. One Latin-1 comment made every subsequent save fail permanently with\n  an internal error carrying the absolute server path. Both directions now use\n  ISO-8859-1.\n- hasEntryReferences treated any non-empty crh:entryRefs as protection, but those\n  are WEAK references and the binder deliberately leaves dangling ones. Repeatedly\n  adding an entry, publishing and deleting the entry pinned every snapshot forever\n  and retention never bit again. A reference is now resolved, and only\n  ItemNotFoundException counts as gone: any other read failure propagates, because\n  an unrelated error must not be read as permission to delete the evidence behind a\n  published revision.\n\nThe pre-commit hook recognised only single-quoted Groovy literals, so the exact\nrecurrence it exists to stop passed when the operator used double quotes -- the\nnatural choice when a password contains an apostrophe. Both styles are handled now,\nverified by staging a double-quoted secret and watching the commit be refused. Its\nfixture exclusion also covers src/test as well as tests, so a JUnit fixture is not\nblocked with advice pointing at the Cypress directory.\n\n224 unit tests pass, including a new one for the dangling-reference case.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"f008461e16f77d4a4c08a9d2216c6ee45754b268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/f008461e16f77d4a4c08a9d2216c6ee45754b268"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83","verification":{"payload":"tree f008461e16f77d4a4c08a9d2216c6ee45754b268\nparent b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788287830 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788287830 +0200\n\nfix(security): bind the capture credential to loopback, and close four config-file holes\n\nThe blind security review of this branch found that one of my own earlier fixes\ncreated an escalation. Preserving capture.secret and capture.secretFile across a\npanel save was correct on its own, but it removed an accidental mitigation: before\nit, a save dropped the secret and capture fell back to anonymous, so nothing went\nout. With the secret preserved and capture.baseUrl still only WARNED about, a site\nadministrator could set baseUrl to a host they control and receive\nAuthorization: Basic with the operator''s capture password on the next publication.\n\nThe credential is now sent only when the destination is this node''s own loopback\nconnector, using the reachesJahiaDirectly predicate that already existed for the\nwarning. That closes it however baseUrl was set, and because the recorded principal\nis derived from what is actually sent, the snapshot is correctly marked guest\nrather than claiming privileged provenance for an anonymous render.\n\nFour more holes in the same file, each verified against java.util.Properties\nsemantics rather than assumed:\n\n- singleLine refused a newline but not a BACKSLASH, which is the properties escape\n  character; a trailing one continues the value onto the next line and consumes the\n  setting written after it, so capture.baseUrl could be made to vanish while the\n  panel reported it as applied. Backslashes are now refused outright.\n- indexOfSeparator read only ''='' and '':'', but whitespace is also a legal separator,\n  so a hand-written `capture.enabled false` was classed as unmanaged and\n  re-appended BELOW the module''s own line, where the last occurrence wins. The file\n  then said the opposite of what the panel reported.\n- The file was read as UTF-8 and written as UTF-8, though a properties file is\n  ISO-8859-1. One Latin-1 comment made every subsequent save fail permanently with\n  an internal error carrying the absolute server path. Both directions now use\n  ISO-8859-1.\n- hasEntryReferences treated any non-empty crh:entryRefs as protection, but those\n  are WEAK references and the binder deliberately leaves dangling ones. Repeatedly\n  adding an entry, publishing and deleting the entry pinned every snapshot forever\n  and retention never bit again. A reference is now resolved, and only\n  ItemNotFoundException counts as gone: any other read failure propagates, because\n  an unrelated error must not be read as permission to delete the evidence behind a\n  published revision.\n\nThe pre-commit hook recognised only single-quoted Groovy literals, so the exact\nrecurrence it exists to stop passed when the operator used double quotes -- the\nnatural choice when a password contains an apostrophe. Both styles are handled now,\nverified by staging a double-quoted secret and watching the commit be refused. Its\nfixture exclusion also covers src/test as well as tests, so a JUnit fixture is not\nblocked with advice pointing at the Cypress directory.\n\n224 unit tests pass, including a new one for the dangling-reference case.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXG1YACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lyGwf8DVrbNpaoO2F92MaD2aHxmLojkn994Xst6DiG4RQsvWFL6QePwQjL82RI\n6OiNaYNYtKyMenBaMxk4bMrbBvNXd/YUQ0fekFwi6qyEKUpUfyD+O+j/Zjqjp/cw\nQ1XBaT4WWQ0IbeVgANm1ph7IKt3BaRLU0m9X8k+Z5+EpQmCBb4HyNuv8juDxF87i\nU2BVoM1qEpBzRHV8w6V3jTxCvQSXCrmL/9pd2I+vjl7W7WmAY0suD158dLKnDdUF\nzg0401FZjD7DbRSgK+SX520Dil4jgE5LxPJWoL8eS6h5inFUHENtg4wyvsQu27vn\n1Tt5uW+eWvb6eOJgUCVlno9yqnKL0w==\n=/mMz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T18:43:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGNlYTMwMTI5OTUzMmNmYzU2N2RjODUxYzZhNjIyNjIyNWM2YTBkODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559","sha":"b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559"}],"sha":"cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/cea301299532cfc567dc851c6a6226225c6a0d83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T18:31:49Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T18:31:49Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(review): act on the blind re-review of this branch''s own diff\n\nFive findings from fresh agents that reviewed only the diff, each verified against\nthe code before being fixed. Three were defects in fixes made earlier on this same\nbranch, which is the point of re-reviewing a change set rather than the module.\n\nA test of mine was vacuous. titleOnlyNodeIsNotAFallThrough asserted that\ntextProperties returns an empty list, but hasTitle only gates a log line and never\ntouches that list, so the assertion was byte-identical in effect to the no-title\ntest beside it and would have passed with hasTitle deleted. The decision is now\nobservable as nothingReachesTheSnapshot and asserted directly; mutation-checked, it\nfails when hasTitle stops being consulted. Two boundary tests added with it.\n\npreservedLines used Files.isReadable, which answers false for BOTH \"no file yet\"\nand \"a file that exists but cannot be read\". Treating the second as the first was\nexactly the failure the method was written to prevent: the save proceeded and wrote\na fresh file with no capture.secret in it. It now tests existence, so an unreadable\nfile reaches readAllLines and its IOException becomes the refusal.\n\nThe recorded capture principal was re-derived AFTER the render, from a fresh read\nof the configuration. A change in between -- an administrator deleting the site''s\nsettings, FileInstall applying an edit -- made it disagree with the credential that\nactually fetched, and recording guest for a privileged render tells every\ncontributor who reads that snapshot that restricted content is safe to show\nanybody. The principal now travels on Fetched, decided from the same single\nsettings read that built the Authorization header, and principalOfRecord is gone.\nThe rule itself moved to GuestMarkdownFetcher.principalFor, where it is next to the\ndecision it describes and is asserted by two tests.\n\nThe retention bound was enforced only in the GraphQL mutation, while save() is also\nreachable from the reflectively instantiated backfill service; a value below 1\nwould have sat in the file as invalid until FileInstall next replaced it silently.\nNow refused at both entry points.\n\nBoth role=alert Banners carried an aria-label derived from their title prop, which\non a live region can be announced in place of the changed children -- and the\nchildren are where the reason lives. A screen reader user would have been\ninterrupted to be told that saving failed, but never why. The reason is now in the\naccessible name as well.\n\nAlso added: lifecycle tests for the AtomicReference change, asserting that a\nstopping instance does not clear a replacement that already activated, which was\nthe improvement claimed for it and had no coverage.\n\n223 unit tests pass, up from 218.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"9be01cf595b6e85b9f7248df5b53de6f9e4d6231","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/9be01cf595b6e85b9f7248df5b53de6f9e4d6231"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559","verification":{"payload":"tree 9be01cf595b6e85b9f7248df5b53de6f9e4d6231\nparent 6be3161e947d84b850f00dfe86dc9fcaf907859e\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788287509 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788287509 +0200\n\nfix(review): act on the blind re-review of this branch''s own diff\n\nFive findings from fresh agents that reviewed only the diff, each verified against\nthe code before being fixed. Three were defects in fixes made earlier on this same\nbranch, which is the point of re-reviewing a change set rather than the module.\n\nA test of mine was vacuous. titleOnlyNodeIsNotAFallThrough asserted that\ntextProperties returns an empty list, but hasTitle only gates a log line and never\ntouches that list, so the assertion was byte-identical in effect to the no-title\ntest beside it and would have passed with hasTitle deleted. The decision is now\nobservable as nothingReachesTheSnapshot and asserted directly; mutation-checked, it\nfails when hasTitle stops being consulted. Two boundary tests added with it.\n\npreservedLines used Files.isReadable, which answers false for BOTH \"no file yet\"\nand \"a file that exists but cannot be read\". Treating the second as the first was\nexactly the failure the method was written to prevent: the save proceeded and wrote\na fresh file with no capture.secret in it. It now tests existence, so an unreadable\nfile reaches readAllLines and its IOException becomes the refusal.\n\nThe recorded capture principal was re-derived AFTER the render, from a fresh read\nof the configuration. A change in between -- an administrator deleting the site''s\nsettings, FileInstall applying an edit -- made it disagree with the credential that\nactually fetched, and recording guest for a privileged render tells every\ncontributor who reads that snapshot that restricted content is safe to show\nanybody. The principal now travels on Fetched, decided from the same single\nsettings read that built the Authorization header, and principalOfRecord is gone.\nThe rule itself moved to GuestMarkdownFetcher.principalFor, where it is next to the\ndecision it describes and is asserted by two tests.\n\nThe retention bound was enforced only in the GraphQL mutation, while save() is also\nreachable from the reflectively instantiated backfill service; a value below 1\nwould have sat in the file as invalid until FileInstall next replaced it silently.\nNow refused at both entry points.\n\nBoth role=alert Banners carried an aria-label derived from their title prop, which\non a live region can be announced in place of the changed children -- and the\nchildren are where the reason lives. A screen reader user would have been\ninterrupted to be told that saving failed, but never why. The reason is now in the\naccessible name as well.\n\nAlso added: lifecycle tests for the AtomicReference change, asserting that a\nstopping instance does not clear a replacement that already activated, which was\nthe improvement claimed for it and had no coverage.\n\n223 unit tests pass, up from 218.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqXGhUACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nnpgf/a3Q+DO3d0okEiNeH3VSyBS9vOylw/xWiumGqhobOM/mN8lm7tMQZtUaT\npO+Lt0mqkHe3wvFzBq4CLJMqg+UzMt+7j6W2+41CURAmS2dtsbgnOvW6Y0z3ccM0\ndeoiv4F4vRHRpoZQ3tWDYiu6XFjXGrAvnN9QusA4IhCvV+d8aX9XNPfTh6WGnOTN\nka68MTDPCbYsZEeBfO5dfFQqn4bRdu4luF8F1grT/QWupTzxoF9vxXAd4cwDmsUB\nQ1idwphxcNJ4h39zWiQp7Wqpt/v9mOIIi4O65kJkC2AGExyCoCuaojcfQJZd5K6b\ng1EToJ6Mv1dCM8RyJJT2mMCYzbtwfA==\n=a8qI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T18:43:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGIwNzFkOGRjMGM4MWQxNTIyYzJmOWIwYTY1MDY3Y2U3NGQzYzE1NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/6be3161e947d84b850f00dfe86dc9fcaf907859e","sha":"6be3161e947d84b850f00dfe86dc9fcaf907859e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6be3161e947d84b850f00dfe86dc9fcaf907859e"}],"sha":"b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/b071d8dc0c81d1522c2f9b0a65067ce74d3c1559"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6be3161e947d84b850f00dfe86dc9fcaf907859e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:23:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:23:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor: express the pruning loop so it needs neither a break nor a continue\n\nI traded one rule for another and this undoes that.\n\nThe loop originally carried `pruned < excess` in its for condition, which\njava:S1994 objects to because `pruned` is updated in the body. Moving the test\ninto the body as a break satisfied S1994 and immediately tripped java:S135,\nbecause the loop already had a continue for the protected snapshot and two jumps\nis one too many. Putting the test back would just resurrect S1994.\n\nBoth objections are about readability and both are fair. A while loop with a\nsingle if/else has neither, and reads as what the code actually is: walk the\noldest first, skip what a revision entry references, stop once enough is freed.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged and the six prune tests pass untouched, including the ones\nthat assert a referenced snapshot survives, that a younger unreferenced one is\ntaken in its place, that the newest is never touched, and that the pruned counter\nexcludes what was protected.\n\nWorth recording why this took three attempts: I was fixing to satisfy rules rather\nthan looking at the shape of the loop. The rules were pointing at the same thing\neach time.\n\n218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"b5a087d2f252b527aff7c72cf3e636e4fcede12d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/b5a087d2f252b527aff7c72cf3e636e4fcede12d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/6be3161e947d84b850f00dfe86dc9fcaf907859e","verification":{"payload":"tree b5a087d2f252b527aff7c72cf3e636e4fcede12d\nparent 4afbe93b94be979871b2ed7fa4e1c352ee9f2532\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279801 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279801 +0200\n\nrefactor: express the pruning loop so it needs neither a break nor a continue\n\nI traded one rule for another and this undoes that.\n\nThe loop originally carried `pruned < excess` in its for condition, which\njava:S1994 objects to because `pruned` is updated in the body. Moving the test\ninto the body as a break satisfied S1994 and immediately tripped java:S135,\nbecause the loop already had a continue for the protected snapshot and two jumps\nis one too many. Putting the test back would just resurrect S1994.\n\nBoth objections are about readability and both are fair. A while loop with a\nsingle if/else has neither, and reads as what the code actually is: walk the\noldest first, skip what a revision entry references, stop once enough is freed.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged and the six prune tests pass untouched, including the ones\nthat assert a referenced snapshot survives, that a younger unreferenced one is\ntaken in its place, that the newest is never touched, and that the pruned counter\nexcludes what was protected.\n\nWorth recording why this took three attempts: I was fixing to satisfy rules rather\nthan looking at the shape of the loop. The rules were pointing at the same thing\neach time.\n\n218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW+/kACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lNjQgAzxS8G9WLMEq9S883quBwe4e2n0n+9XadYy3Vee5cLhF9Hap0PHpfPrQb\noSYufkXF8xiC1LG/aHGZLlNBUU2GZqNpTa+yUHjwwLEdEtuw