rcontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4afbe93b94be979871b2ed7fa4e1c352ee9f2532/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:20:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:20:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"perf: do not make repository calls for a log line that may not be written\n\njava:S2629 on the fall-through warning. safePath and safeType were passed as\narguments, so both were invoked whether or not anything would be written, and each\nmakes a repository call. On a page of many unspecialised nodes that is a real cost\npaid for nothing. Guarded with isWarnEnabled.\n\nThis was the last maintainability issue the previous commit''s decomposition left in\nthis file: that refactor cleared java:S3776, java:S135 and java:S1141 together, and\nthe project''s debt ratio went 0.7 to 0.6.\n\n218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"c9ebe26cc3f1377fb8c8ca499447f8268ef15e29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/c9ebe26cc3f1377fb8c8ca499447f8268ef15e29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/4afbe93b94be979871b2ed7fa4e1c352ee9f2532","verification":{"payload":"tree c9ebe26cc3f1377fb8c8ca499447f8268ef15e29\nparent 0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279604 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279604 +0200\n\nperf: do not make repository calls for a log line that may not be written\n\njava:S2629 on the fall-through warning. safePath and safeType were passed as\narguments, so both were invoked whether or not anything would be written, and each\nmakes a repository call. On a page of many unspecialised nodes that is a real cost\npaid for nothing. Guarded with isWarnEnabled.\n\nThis was the last maintainability issue the previous commit''s decomposition left in\nthis file: that refactor cleared java:S3776, java:S135 and java:S1141 together, and\nthe project''s debt ratio went 0.7 to 0.6.\n\n218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW+zQACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kKqgf+KkX6coN0UdDG/9K2fuSu/9FAjyC/6q9OP4eZFGwY06V8MmMRv4PGFaZc\n6dynOr4+Oh/t0KNtGnNcqs3xuZ5RPBNoLoi0MiaPnQbDHrJJQAGFjAz+KQOn25Po\nrCRYNcrltSVrRMpzeLvRZ8F7at4J73loa48flqPmtd6YYiEDvPDlqBJEM7kuESbp\nsQ+K/7Ad2OnunTgKOoIV+LzonI27LMojPUdWlE38ZXKn34ilMZlS3narhUvgOhsI\n28hHk+zMdU+QnlDsu7DBXs51Ls4NffJTTgmiSceeMw08mT9+P9fI45hFSJhI+CAy\nas4tkca0CsDsW5YK1dKnImWpc8fkgw==\n=+lrl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:24:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/4afbe93b94be979871b2ed7fa4e1c352ee9f2532","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDRhZmJlOTNiOTRiZTk3OTg3MWIyZWQ3ZmE0ZTFjMzUyZWU5ZjI1MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586","sha":"0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586"}],"sha":"4afbe93b94be979871b2ed7fa4e1c352ee9f2532","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4afbe93b94be979871b2ed7fa4e1c352ee9f2532"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:17:15Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:17:15Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor: decompose textProperties, whose complexity I had pushed to 33\n\nCognitive complexity 33 against an allowed 15, and it was my doing: adding\nmulti-valued handling put a second nested loop and another branch inside a method\nthat already had a nested try, two continues and a trailing report.\n\nSplit along the seams that were already there rather than mechanically:\n\n- collectInto walks the properties and answers whether they could be listed at\n  all, so the caller can stop instead of reporting an empty node as a\n  fall-through, which was a real distinction buried in a return statement.\n- collectOne decides whether one property counts as prose and records it.\n- textOf extracts the non-blank values of one property, single or multi-valued.\n- addIfNotBlank removes the blank check repeated in both branches.\n- reportIfNothingReachesTheSnapshot holds the loud fall-through and reads as one\n  condition instead of trailing the collection logic.\n\ncollectOne also now names the property in its warning even when getName() is what\nfailed, which the previous version could not.\n\nNo behaviour change: all 218 unit tests pass unmodified, including the nine that\ncover property selection, ordering, multi-valued inclusion, blank handling and the\nfall-through warning. Those tests are why this refactor is safe to make at all.\n\nThis should also clear java:S135 and java:S1141 on the same method, which were\nreported against the same nesting.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"54daab2beacc596343e7cd5e98a951b8142744e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/54daab2beacc596343e7cd5e98a951b8142744e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586","verification":{"payload":"tree 54daab2beacc596343e7cd5e98a951b8142744e0\nparent e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279435 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279435 +0200\n\nrefactor: decompose textProperties, whose complexity I had pushed to 33\n\nCognitive complexity 33 against an allowed 15, and it was my doing: adding\nmulti-valued handling put a second nested loop and another branch inside a method\nthat already had a nested try, two continues and a trailing report.\n\nSplit along the seams that were already there rather than mechanically:\n\n- collectInto walks the properties and answers whether they could be listed at\n  all, so the caller can stop instead of reporting an empty node as a\n  fall-through, which was a real distinction buried in a return statement.\n- collectOne decides whether one property counts as prose and records it.\n- textOf extracts the non-blank values of one property, single or multi-valued.\n- addIfNotBlank removes the blank check repeated in both branches.\n- reportIfNothingReachesTheSnapshot holds the loud fall-through and reads as one\n  condition instead of trailing the collection logic.\n\ncollectOne also now names the property in its warning even when getName() is what\nfailed, which the previous version could not.\n\nNo behaviour change: all 218 unit tests pass unmodified, including the nine that\ncover property selection, ordering, multi-valued inclusion, blank handling and the\nfall-through warning. Those tests are why this refactor is safe to make at all.\n\nThis should also clear java:S135 and java:S1141 on the same method, which were\nreported against the same nesting.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW+osACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mOgAf/UABL54AhH0VnTSBFbvRDYodR8Baub7FVOOK1NrfYH1TgBeeKeXH34xIK\n2OUFQ/XejQxRUw6/foCNshImV7GCr1DybebvJ05rpu4ZqsaQZxSZTHJ5DUKe9+x8\n2XiyJsfgK4KHaXfGDlqpzvsbzz8vRPwiyKG7aBJzyOvk4nMFEByMGzO9HOCJdXD1\n/E8X79lgWc1WKnidxv94Ow94ZjwcVcEhAD4B3yKMG02+q1Zuc419ZHUs1B5JcC92\nKq9sS8iron0Sgjg1DdBo73Od+CvSaUl8kUVA4s01kIm7AzKHr0tk0GQD7E90NpxT\nVpGTbHISfe6BUaDAf3bFyrJ7QyMhLA==\n=F7Ge\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:24:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDBmNjhjZGM5ZmM0MTY4NjUwZjAzYmUwMzZjZjA4YzM2MjlmNjE1ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f","sha":"e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f"}],"sha":"0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0f68cdc9fc4168650f03be036cf08c3629f61586"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:13:47Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:13:47Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore: stop writing comments that Sonar reads as commented-out code\n\nTwo comment lines ended in a semicolon, which is exactly java:S125''s heuristic\nfor commented-out code, so both were reported as dead code to remove. Rewrapped\nso no comment line ends in one. A rule worth knowing when writing prose comments\nin Java: end a wrapped line on a word, not on punctuation that parses.\n\nAlso clears java:S1994 on the pruning loop. It flagged `pruned` being tested in\nthe loop condition while updated in the body, which a conditional increment makes\nunavoidable, so the test moves into the body as an explicit break. Behaviour is\nidentical: the loop still stops once it has freed enough, and still never\nconsiders the newest snapshot.\n\n218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc20adc9375b879049a7c216414d90fea12faff6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/fc20adc9375b879049a7c216414d90fea12faff6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f","verification":{"payload":"tree fc20adc9375b879049a7c216414d90fea12faff6\nparent c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279227 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279227 +0200\n\nchore: stop writing comments that Sonar reads as commented-out code\n\nTwo comment lines ended in a semicolon, which is exactly java:S125''s heuristic\nfor commented-out code, so both were reported as dead code to remove. Rewrapped\nso no comment line ends in one. A rule worth knowing when writing prose comments\nin Java: end a wrapped line on a word, not on punctuation that parses.\n\nAlso clears java:S1994 on the pruning loop. It flagged `pruned` being tested in\nthe loop condition while updated in the body, which a conditional increment makes\nunavoidable, so the test moves into the body as an explicit break. Behaviour is\nidentical: the loop still stops once it has freed enough, and still never\nconsiders the newest snapshot.\n\n218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW+bsACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kjAwf+O2YWtn66pnkL5FO/93wvUEYpgokHCCh7eBcRSEJYsQhg/J7FFJkRl9uM\nItd1z3sol+5+3ASMJz2DYdOJJu2aQcTcgVQW7DvX4ISyAD3r9ilgcP1zucJh4Kx+\n5AvA6ZDMqaKhHwImJYDQ7eSgnhbef01oRAdDxVs7ySG+groRScm6LABYsqaMexYK\n/7OxVEsz6+Q1iBIkipHwCquMeb3k2TblFm2GAUFHjrsxbeJNLPcfsV87PrYvMMla\nomZJ58Dga+6owLudlE+GmOZzdubBh9C0F3ZdiZc2i/iDF/FER2p3brkYS760h8VW\nDF4+xIRNMCAmpWwK7EyX1m8QiFRbrg==\n=/RYj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:24:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGU2MGJiYWQwYWM2YWFjM2YzMzhhODA2NWExYzVmYWUzNzAwNGM5MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16","sha":"c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16"}],"sha":"e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/e60bbad0ac6aac3f338a8065a1c5fae37004c91f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:10:25Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:10:25Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore: clear the two maintainability issues this branch introduced\n\nThe quality gate allows zero new maintainability issues on new code, and my last\ncommit added two. Both were mine and both were trivial.\n\njava:S1192 in RevisionHistoryFunctions: hasTitle repeated the \"jcr:title\" literal\nthree times. It also fetched the property three times to answer one question, so\nthe fix reads it once into a local behind a single constant.\n\njava:S125 in RevisionHistoryMutation: a comment line ending in positiveInt() reads\nas commented-out code. Reworded to name the helper without the parentheses.\n\nNeither changes behaviour. 218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a6d8880a2967fc36cf11ff873d55a7f175104f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/7a6d8880a2967fc36cf11ff873d55a7f175104f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a6d8880a2967fc36cf11ff873d55a7f175104f3\nparent 5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279025 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788279025 +0200\n\nchore: clear the two maintainability issues this branch introduced\n\nThe quality gate allows zero new maintainability issues on new code, and my last\ncommit added two. Both were mine and both were trivial.\n\njava:S1192 in RevisionHistoryFunctions: hasTitle repeated the \"jcr:title\" literal\nthree times. It also fetched the property three times to answer one question, so\nthe fix reads it once into a local behind a single constant.\n\njava:S125 in RevisionHistoryMutation: a comment line ending in positiveInt() reads\nas commented-out code. Reworded to name the helper without the parentheses.\n\nNeither changes behaviour. 218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW+PEACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nntQf/QTqpcRiMVI2bsDUF3GbhlZi8CUQB9KmbktZxwcqdq4FG1LRCX3ZGiRlZ\nWSB9EDRUe4vimgRGiAf3acpXB27C80j6fIv3+7ciLr8MN8+pNeuobQGHbtefCcQl\na1uPSkFFy1o/ichtTMu8/ZAWgTgPD+VQb3lYsgd99fwTuX/Cn5zOlq5kyEP3MEUF\nusHu0jifvZPvVYtYr4Mbu1lsRVVrxHeNrOWB+JZyz9CArYHEyiWFvJA27WYn+Hty\nBWkTO21fAUKM/Oc8mIW6syamI726pYBftkn8rX/XozhlQ7DwP55R2KOSpX2W1861\nqctqWv30qp4tPesjQY7svZVbs980fQ==\n=nyuW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:24:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGM3ZjM5ZDQ5MDVmMDIzMmI2OWQ1ZWEzNzRkYmIyYjAxMWQ0NTNjMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8","sha":"5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8"}],"sha":"c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c7f39d4905f0232b69d5ea374dbb2b011d453c16"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:05:13Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:05:13Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(settings,docs): refuse a useless retention value, and correct two false security claims\n\nThree items, all from the blind review.\n\nsaveSiteSettings accepted any maxSnapshots. A 0 or negative value was written to\nthe site''s .cfg verbatim and returned as the applied setting, so the panel\ndisplayed it; only when FileInstall re-parsed the file did positiveInt() notice,\nsubstitute the module default and log a warning that never reached the UI. The\noperator was left believing a value the running system was not using. It is now\nrefused at the API boundary, before anything is written.\n\nTwo documentation claims asserted a security guarantee the code does not give,\nwhich is the most damaging kind of drift because a maintainer acts on it.\n\ncrh_revisionSnapshot/html/revisionSnapshot.jsp told a reader that the\nrevision-history tree \"has ACL inheritance broken and grants nobody, so in\npractice only server administrators can reach this preview\", and called that a\ndeliberate decision. The opposite is true: restoreInheritance actively restores\ninheritance on every capture, because breaking it made the folder unreadable to\nthe editors who must read a snapshot in order to write the revision entry\ndescribing it. A maintainer could have relaxed the <c:out> escaping on the stated\nbasis that only administrators see the output. The comment now says who really\nsees it and what that means for a snapshot captured as a privileged principal.\n\nThe same file called crh:capturedBy \"always guest\". That was true when capture\ncould only render anonymously and survived the change that made the principal\nconfigurable.\n\nREADME carried the matching claim, that the root is \"ACL locked down\" and that\ninheriting /contents ACLs \"would let any site contributor read every historical\nversion of every page\". It now states the actual position: inheritance is\ndeliberately not broken, anyone with read on /sites/<site>/contents can read every\nsnapshot, and crh:capturedBy is what distinguishes a public snapshot from one\nholding restricted content.\n\nBoth claims were made stale by a change I made earlier in this work, and I did not\nupdate them at the time.\n\nThree e2e tests, one of which closes a gap the coverage review ranked CRITICAL:\nonly the QUERY side of requireSiteAdmin was proven to refuse a non-admin. The\nguard is duplicated across three resolvers by design, so losing it from one\nmutation would have let any editor disable capture or reset another site''s\nconfiguration with every existing test still green. saveSiteSettings and\ndeleteSiteSettings are now both covered, plus the retention refusal.\n\n218 unit tests, spec 09 now 14 tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"1622512c0be456ffa4f2396a55127b62eba971db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/1622512c0be456ffa4f2396a55127b62eba971db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 1622512c0be456ffa4f2396a55127b62eba971db\nparent 9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788278713 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788278713 +0200\n\nfix(settings,docs): refuse a useless retention value, and correct two false security claims\n\nThree items, all from the blind review.\n\nsaveSiteSettings accepted any maxSnapshots. A 0 or negative value was written to\nthe site''s .cfg verbatim and returned as the applied setting, so the panel\ndisplayed it; only when FileInstall re-parsed the file did positiveInt() notice,\nsubstitute the module default and log a warning that never reached the UI. The\noperator was left believing a value the running system was not using. It is now\nrefused at the API boundary, before anything is written.\n\nTwo documentation claims asserted a security guarantee the code does not give,\nwhich is the most damaging kind of drift because a maintainer acts on it.\n\ncrh_revisionSnapshot/html/revisionSnapshot.jsp told a reader that the\nrevision-history tree \"has ACL inheritance broken and grants nobody, so in\npractice only server administrators can reach this preview\", and called that a\ndeliberate decision. The opposite is true: restoreInheritance actively restores\ninheritance on every capture, because breaking it made the folder unreadable to\nthe editors who must read a snapshot in order to write the revision entry\ndescribing it. A maintainer could have relaxed the <c:out> escaping on the stated\nbasis that only administrators see the output. The comment now says who really\nsees it and what that means for a snapshot captured as a privileged principal.\n\nThe same file called crh:capturedBy \"always guest\". That was true when capture\ncould only render anonymously and survived the change that made the principal\nconfigurable.\n\nREADME carried the matching claim, that the root is \"ACL locked down\" and that\ninheriting /contents ACLs \"would let any site contributor read every historical\nversion of every page\". It now states the actual position: inheritance is\ndeliberately not broken, anyone with read on /sites/<site>/contents can read every\nsnapshot, and crh:capturedBy is what distinguishes a public snapshot from one\nholding restricted content.\n\nBoth claims were made stale by a change I made earlier in this work, and I did not\nupdate them at the time.\n\nThree e2e tests, one of which closes a gap the coverage review ranked CRITICAL:\nonly the QUERY side of requireSiteAdmin was proven to refuse a non-admin. The\nguard is duplicated across three resolvers by design, so losing it from one\nmutation would have let any editor disable capture or reset another site''s\nconfiguration with every existing test still green. saveSiteSettings and\ndeleteSiteSettings are now both covered, plus the retention refusal.\n\n218 unit tests, spec 09 now 14 tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW97kACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nPLwf+JEg5PGq7ZTBDQJEUQYakaXghYflvef96v7aU2jTtKcSBIssqnTFVK8Mr\ngtmx/ywHQsOhfoBftDw9DNeRBsVaBkESDg1+yqqmFE1AN53WMGIc9es8xFmP98iG\n7/gsrkimDheP3crc8zmAi8FRtuzyF7+9guzkD6OEVTO1H9ev9cyNfKuUFkQQRk41\nC8uBYV3481yTrMInq8GeHE8TjFmrXUoOTQvVDhJWwsnMQtRPBTDoySlUtI6rcbb+\nvzite4erqgdbqLtbplL8AqWy65k6hmqCzz2d6pHDPlsj/hHw+eW88n1q52LHHXWp\nud90FKzWUraq5q2p6SnMyny7Wj93KA==\n=6gHQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:33:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDUzMzZjYmExMzk2MTNjYjNjYWRjMTNmNDE3YjY4Y2Y2ZTcxM2I1YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a","sha":"9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a"}],"sha":"5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/5336cba139613cb3cadc13f417b68cf6e713b5a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:00:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:00:52Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(capture): record who actually fetched, and stop losing multi-valued content\n\nTwo defects that both made the record state something untrue.\n\ncrh:capturedBy is described to editors as deciding who may safely be shown a\nsnapshot: guest means anyone could have read it, any other name means it may\ncontain content the public cannot see. principalOfRecord read only the\nmodule-wide principal, while GuestMarkdownFetcher.authorizationFor prefers the\nper-site credential, so it was wrong in both directions:\n\n- A site with its own capture.user and no global one fetched as that account and\n  recorded guest, telling an editor that a snapshot full of restricted content was\n  safe to show anybody.\n- A configured capture.user whose secret did not resolve fetched anonymously,\n  because authorizationFor returns null and no header is sent, yet recorded that\n  account, so a plain guest render looked like privileged provenance.\n\nIt now decides from the resolved authorization rather than the configured name: a\nname is recorded only when a credential for it actually went out.\n\ntextProperties skipped every multi-valued property. That is the same silent\ncontent loss the generic fallback view was written to end: a type holding its\nbullet points in a multi-valued string beside a single-valued heading would, when\nan editor rewrote every bullet, still hash identically, so capture recorded\nUNCHANGED and the history stated that nothing in the page text had changed.\nMulti-valued strings are now emitted, each value as its own block, keeping their\nstored order because that order is editorial; only the ordering BETWEEN properties\nis normalised by name, since JCR does not guarantee iteration order.\n\nThe loud fall-through warning also fired for a node whose only text is its\njcr:title, which the view DOES emit as a heading. Warning about content that is in\nfact captured trains an operator to filter the message, and that then hides the\ngenuine case. It no longer fires when a title is present.\n\nOne existing test asserted that multi-valued properties were skipped. That test\nwas asserting the defect, so it is replaced rather than adapted, and the\nreplacement says why in full.\n\n218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"105eb8406ddfe0cae22b16a0261bbdadbc48736c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/105eb8406ddfe0cae22b16a0261bbdadbc48736c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a","verification":{"payload":"tree 105eb8406ddfe0cae22b16a0261bbdadbc48736c\nparent 628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788278452 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788278452 +0200\n\nfix(capture): record who actually fetched, and stop losing multi-valued content\n\nTwo defects that both made the record state something untrue.\n\ncrh:capturedBy is described to editors as deciding who may safely be shown a\nsnapshot: guest means anyone could have read it, any other name means it may\ncontain content the public cannot see. principalOfRecord read only the\nmodule-wide principal, while GuestMarkdownFetcher.authorizationFor prefers the\nper-site credential, so it was wrong in both directions:\n\n- A site with its own capture.user and no global one fetched as that account and\n  recorded guest, telling an editor that a snapshot full of restricted content was\n  safe to show anybody.\n- A configured capture.user whose secret did not resolve fetched anonymously,\n  because authorizationFor returns null and no header is sent, yet recorded that\n  account, so a plain guest render looked like privileged provenance.\n\nIt now decides from the resolved authorization rather than the configured name: a\nname is recorded only when a credential for it actually went out.\n\ntextProperties skipped every multi-valued property. That is the same silent\ncontent loss the generic fallback view was written to end: a type holding its\nbullet points in a multi-valued string beside a single-valued heading would, when\nan editor rewrote every bullet, still hash identically, so capture recorded\nUNCHANGED and the history stated that nothing in the page text had changed.\nMulti-valued strings are now emitted, each value as its own block, keeping their\nstored order because that order is editorial; only the ordering BETWEEN properties\nis normalised by name, since JCR does not guarantee iteration order.\n\nThe loud fall-through warning also fired for a node whose only text is its\njcr:title, which the view DOES emit as a heading. Warning about content that is in\nfact captured trains an operator to filter the message, and that then hides the\ngenuine case. It no longer fires when a title is present.\n\nOne existing test asserted that multi-valued properties were skipped. That test\nwas asserting the defect, so it is replaced rather than adapted, and the\nreplacement says why in full.\n\n218 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW9rQACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mW5Af/SCRegxdxZ83cvP4RJLUe+YU0sx0HF2WOhC7jVNWx3/J4ZQf6GjLpKVK5\nfyLkzkSEmnCHQtFwzpDWbtzn6JcPV2oEZyyZCYTzCG+fgqqB7Jv8Z843BODWx9/x\nbxojKgukCx0vV9HUHsbTSqHbuKpDc50ZycRUsR1HuuDVZAiWBB/s4rpSxln8RqH1\newzoYa7W+AyWPw8eAwYVkPnrOeyN7LHx5tb7DC7fPvFw3lfrRG3m4iWkmRouZ5Yp\n23r2U1eRAnCBvwQXDYrAR9XaohG/n4YuNnqWfhVdt7x0dO23gnUk5AFWXckAHbFq\nar5/wzeiswYz8SW2LNUIKj7YK+eLqQ==\n=BssR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:33:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDljMmVkM2Q3ODQzZTJkZDEyODU2ZTlmZDc5YmYzYWIwMmZkNTk3N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690","sha":"628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690"}],"sha":"9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/9c2ed3d7843e2dd12856e9fd79bf3ab02fd5977a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T15:53:14Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T15:53:14Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(concurrency): hold the component singletons in AtomicReference, not a volatile field\n\nSonar''s quality gate failed on one condition: software_quality_reliability_rating\nwas 2 where the gate requires 1. Two java:S3077 bugs caused it, both the same\npattern -- a static volatile field holding the DS component instance, published in\n@Activate for callers DS cannot inject into (the Quartz job, the reflectively\ninstantiated backfill service).\n\nS3077 is right about the general shape and, as it happens, harmless here: volatile\npublishes the REFERENCE safely and says nothing about the object behind it, but\nboth instances keep only ConcurrentHashMaps, so the old form was sound. It was\nsound in a way a reader had to verify for themselves, though, which is exactly the\nkind of reasoning a thread-safe holder makes unnecessary. Suppressing the rule\nwould have preserved the need to re-derive it.\n\nThe change also buys something real. Both @Deactivate methods assigned null\nunconditionally. During a bundle refresh the replacement instance can activate\nbefore the old one stops, and that assignment would then wipe the LIVE instance:\nSiteSettingsRegistry.settingsFor would fall back to the module defaults for every\nsite until the next activation, and PublicationSnapshotListener.jobStarted would\nsilently stop deregistering completed jobs. compareAndSet(this, null) clears the\nholder only if it still points at the instance being stopped.\n\nPublicationSnapshotListener.stop keeps its existing ordering guarantee: listeners\nunregistered and outstanding jobs cancelled BEFORE the holder is cleared, so a job\nentering executeJahiaJob in the gap still finds the instance and can deregister\nitself.\n\nCaptureIdentity uses the same volatile-static idiom and is NOT flagged, because\nits fields are Strings and therefore immutable. Left alone.\n\n215 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e04f3ce519382621be9904d4e75318c251f7a70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/5e04f3ce519382621be9904d4e75318c251f7a70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e04f3ce519382621be9904d4e75318c251f7a70\nparent 4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788277994 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788277994 +0200\n\nfix(concurrency): hold the component singletons in AtomicReference, not a volatile field\n\nSonar''s quality gate failed on one condition: software_quality_reliability_rating\nwas 2 where the gate requires 1. Two java:S3077 bugs caused it, both the same\npattern -- a static volatile field holding the DS component instance, published in\n@Activate for callers DS cannot inject into (the Quartz job, the reflectively\ninstantiated backfill service).\n\nS3077 is right about the general shape and, as it happens, harmless here: volatile\npublishes the REFERENCE safely and says nothing about the object behind it, but\nboth instances keep only ConcurrentHashMaps, so the old form was sound. It was\nsound in a way a reader had to verify for themselves, though, which is exactly the\nkind of reasoning a thread-safe holder makes unnecessary. Suppressing the rule\nwould have preserved the need to re-derive it.\n\nThe change also buys something real. Both @Deactivate methods assigned null\nunconditionally. During a bundle refresh the replacement instance can activate\nbefore the old one stops, and that assignment would then wipe the LIVE instance:\nSiteSettingsRegistry.settingsFor would fall back to the module defaults for every\nsite until the next activation, and PublicationSnapshotListener.jobStarted would\nsilently stop deregistering completed jobs. compareAndSet(this, null) clears the\nholder only if it still points at the instance being stopped.\n\nPublicationSnapshotListener.stop keeps its existing ordering guarantee: listeners\nunregistered and outstanding jobs cancelled BEFORE the holder is cleared, so a job\nentering executeJahiaJob in the gap still finds the instance and can deregister\nitself.\n\nCaptureIdentity uses the same volatile-static idiom and is NOT flagged, because\nits fields are Strings and therefore immutable. Left alone.\n\n215 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW9OoACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lRwwf+J8JLT9CYT77NkTRHT+vGSrD9p9VWcZmKIa/0zfvhnVFuC1PCaJGOH4yW\newrAuxa/DyJrSNW//8Gu4qXJ28c7KEdr1eNKdO4fK20vUwao9URnXdfYNbzIPwBJ\nxrfk11/MSQan7nIBFX7UBzqswEUzh1Ehn+o5hEhBFfxCrMtwUFJAQZxIdqcapdaE\nMaFwJV1K+FOf5Ke0pjnnac90zn7pWF8K6VNCZPabeVpYE5GY5p1y8uOzh6WTXztq\nCkzB7v/uKX3PBEYejz6ePX6LZ08jroc68ozxtmSL6dGDTX4ZN1OSZ0fKnwKHXtSN\nGyCuvL/rywbQcYjVPw24ilpBmleG7w==\n=ynWn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:33:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDYyODgzNWMwNGJjNWUyNmY5MTM0NTIwY2UzY2U2YzhiMDgwNTY2OTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44","sha":"4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44"}],"sha":"628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/628835c04bc5e26f9134520ce3ce6c8b08056690"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:12:48Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:12:48Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(retention): refuse to prune a snapshot a revision entry references\n\nRetention was silently rewriting history.\n\ncrh:entryRefs lives on the SNAPSHOT, not on the entry, so it is both the binding\nand the only record of it. Pruning removed the node, and the binding went with it.\nRevisionEntryBinder then saw that entry as never bound, because it builds its map\nby scanning the SURVIVING snapshots, and targetFor fell back to the current\nsnapshot. On the next capture a years-old revision entry was therefore bound to\ntoday''s content, and comparing that revision against a recent one reported the\npage as identical. No error, nothing in the UI, and the public record asserting\nsomething false about what a page said years ago.\n\nThat is worse than losing the snapshot. Losing it renders the honest \"no snapshot\nof the page was recorded for this revision\"; this fabricates instead.\n\nRevisionEntryBinder''s own Javadoc states the invariant, that binding is\nappend-only and an entry which already has a snapshot is never rebound, or a later\ncapture would silently rewrite what an existing public revision claims the page\nsaid. It cannot enforce that, because the property it relies on was being deleted\nfrom underneath it. So it is enforced where the deletion happens.\n\nprune now walks oldest to newest skipping any snapshot with a non-empty\ncrh:entryRefs, taking a younger unreferenced one in its place, so a cap still\nbites wherever it can. It never touches the newest, which is the next capture''s\ndedupe baseline. When it cannot free enough it says so at WARN, naming the count\nand the cap: retention becomes advisory for that page, and an operator who set a\ncap needs to know why it is not honoured rather than watching a folder grow.\n\nOnly automatically-bound entries were at risk. A pinned entry survived already,\nbecause targetFor resolves crh:snapshotRef by name, finds nothing, and leaves the\nentry honestly unbound.\n\nThe default cap is 500 per page and language so this was rare, but the\nsite-settings panel accepts 1, which would prune almost everything on the next\npublication and rebind every entry at once.\n\nprune is extracted package-private from pruneIfNeeded, separating the mechanism\nfrom the policy lookup so it can be tested against an explicit cap, as validate()\nalready is.\n\nSix tests, mutation-checked: removing the protection fails three of them. One of\nthose initially asserted a remaining-count I had mis-derived rather than the\nproperty; it now asserts cap - 1, which is what the code actually promises.\n\n215 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb9f3b50a1661c98c57b91079815f644cb8f3f4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/bb9f3b50a1661c98c57b91079815f644cb8f3f4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44","verification":{"payload":"tree bb9f3b50a1661c98c57b91079815f644cb8f3f4e\nparent 8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788271968 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788271968 +0200\n\nfix(retention): refuse to prune a snapshot a revision entry references\n\nRetention was silently rewriting history.\n\ncrh:entryRefs lives on the SNAPSHOT, not on the entry, so it is both the binding\nand the only record of it. Pruning removed the node, and the binding went with it.\nRevisionEntryBinder then saw that entry as never bound, because it builds its map\nby scanning the SURVIVING snapshots, and targetFor fell back to the current\nsnapshot. On the next capture a years-old revision entry was therefore bound to\ntoday''s content, and comparing that revision against a recent one reported the\npage as identical. No error, nothing in the UI, and the public record asserting\nsomething false about what a page said years ago.\n\nThat is worse than losing the snapshot. Losing it renders the honest \"no snapshot\nof the page was recorded for this revision\"; this fabricates instead.\n\nRevisionEntryBinder''s own Javadoc states the invariant, that binding is\nappend-only and an entry which already has a snapshot is never rebound, or a later\ncapture would silently rewrite what an existing public revision claims the page\nsaid. It cannot enforce that, because the property it relies on was being deleted\nfrom underneath it. So it is enforced where the deletion happens.\n\nprune now walks oldest to newest skipping any snapshot with a non-empty\ncrh:entryRefs, taking a younger unreferenced one in its place, so a cap still\nbites wherever it can. It never touches the newest, which is the next capture''s\ndedupe baseline. When it cannot free enough it says so at WARN, naming the count\nand the cap: retention becomes advisory for that page, and an operator who set a\ncap needs to know why it is not honoured rather than watching a folder grow.\n\nOnly automatically-bound entries were at risk. A pinned entry survived already,\nbecause targetFor resolves crh:snapshotRef by name, finds nothing, and leaves the\nentry honestly unbound.\n\nThe default cap is 500 per page and language so this was rare, but the\nsite-settings panel accepts 1, which would prune almost everything on the next\npublication and rebind every entry at once.\n\nprune is extracted package-private from pruneIfNeeded, separating the mechanism\nfrom the policy lookup so it can be tested against an explicit cap, as validate()\nalready is.\n\nSix tests, mutation-checked: removing the protection fails three of them. One of\nthose initially asserted a remaining-count I had mis-derived rather than the\nproperty; it now asserts cap - 1, which is what the code actually promises.\n\n215 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqW3WAACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kwEwf/XxP3JILpPb9fny5AV+2jy5tWS2ghjmrR7S8dm9EiYPSHX3MBkpmled4J\nkoDZ0913RIL6k6uXhokIDui4Dg6ZYr8S7PFOOUmz3jLD4wnmkFaTU28OJR49Xtlu\nI48Amp92gHy3HFqR/2OADxwAFXBMDRxO9LK0KyTxYUl58cCW5qMfB44XfEaQDZdt\nP6aNlXQq9V1XIpVM7LcM3EeaZtWezIbEakfgTLd3+9gA2mspq10vkSqbtKc/GUIw\nOpLl7aNVJjEl6YgsaSMYXHSBh3WDeiD3GRduYRmaBxLJ5l+NbA60BSfLlt67vVXC\nePbGfrS/Sv7I1YEwaWI1zn7MlkOcFw==\n=/iV7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:28:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDRkNjczOTFmMTRlNjQ2NDMyMWZlNDI4ZDRiY2U3ZmMzMzI1YzBiNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd","sha":"8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd"}],"sha":"4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/4d67391f14e6464321fe428d4bce7fc3325c0b44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:21:58Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:21:58Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(a11y,build): announce what the panel reports, and honour --mode\n\nAccessibility, WCAG 2.2 AAA.\n\nmoonstone''s Banner renders a plain div: aria-label only, no role and no aria-live.\nEverything this panel reports therefore appeared on screen and was announced to\nnobody. A screen reader user who saved and failed had to re-explore the panel to\ndiscover whether their change applied. The write-error and query-error banners now\ncarry role=alert, and the configured/defaults status banner role=status, polite\nbecause it changes as a side effect of saving and must not interrupt. Fails\nSC 4.1.3 before this.\n\nField renders its helper prop as a caption with no id and never wires\naria-describedby, so two load-bearing operational facts reached sighted users\nonly: whether a capture credential resolved, which decides whether restricted\npages can be captured at all, and the loopback-versus-public-host warning that\nexplains why capture silently 404s when baseUrl is wrong. Both helpers are now\nrendered by this module with ids of their own and referenced with\naria-describedby. Fails SC 1.3.1 before this.\n\nAn intermediate version of this used aria-description, which is ARIA 1.3 and\npoorly supported; aria-describedby needs an element with an id, so the element is\nours rather than Field''s.\n\nBuild: webpack hardcoded mode: ''development'' in the returned config while only\ndevtool reacted to argv.mode, so package.json''s build:production -- which passes\n--mode=production, and which the Maven build runs -- shipped an unminified bundle\ncarrying React''s development build and its warnings. Now honours the flag;\nverified the emitted bundle is minified.\n\nDocs: the README told the reader ''the pom must declare the blueprint extender\ncapability'', which this module deliberately does not, because it has no Spring\ncontext and its extension points are Declarative Services components. Following\nit would add a capability the module does not use. Rewritten to say when the\ncapability IS needed and why this module does not declare it, keeping the note\nbecause the symptom is near-undiagnosable from the outside.\n\n209 unit tests, 87 e2e tests, eslint 0, tsc 0.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"5bb76c4d2d29d57375a9c9bfc83bef7f410fb637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/5bb76c4d2d29d57375a9c9bfc83bef7f410fb637"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd","verification":{"payload":"tree 5bb76c4d2d29d57375a9c9bfc83bef7f410fb637\nparent 1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788243718 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788243718 +0200\n\nfix(a11y,build): announce what the panel reports, and honour --mode\n\nAccessibility, WCAG 2.2 AAA.\n\nmoonstone''s Banner renders a plain div: aria-label only, no role and no aria-live.\nEverything this panel reports therefore appeared on screen and was announced to\nnobody. A screen reader user who saved and failed had to re-explore the panel to\ndiscover whether their change applied. The write-error and query-error banners now\ncarry role=alert, and the configured/defaults status banner role=status, polite\nbecause it changes as a side effect of saving and must not interrupt. Fails\nSC 4.1.3 before this.\n\nField renders its helper prop as a caption with no id and never wires\naria-describedby, so two load-bearing operational facts reached sighted users\nonly: whether a capture credential resolved, which decides whether restricted\npages can be captured at all, and the loopback-versus-public-host warning that\nexplains why capture silently 404s when baseUrl is wrong. Both helpers are now\nrendered by this module with ids of their own and referenced with\naria-describedby. Fails SC 1.3.1 before this.\n\nAn intermediate version of this used aria-description, which is ARIA 1.3 and\npoorly supported; aria-describedby needs an element with an id, so the element is\nours rather than Field''s.\n\nBuild: webpack hardcoded mode: ''development'' in the returned config while only\ndevtool reacted to argv.mode, so package.json''s build:production -- which passes\n--mode=production, and which the Maven build runs -- shipped an unminified bundle\ncarrying React''s development build and its warnings. Now honours the flag;\nverified the emitted bundle is minified.\n\nDocs: the README told the reader ''the pom must declare the blueprint extender\ncapability'', which this module deliberately does not, because it has no Spring\ncontext and its extension points are Declarative Services components. Following\nit would add a capability the module does not use. Rewritten to say when the\ncapability IS needed and why this module does not declare it, keeping the note\nbecause the symptom is near-undiagnosable from the outside.\n\n209 unit tests, 87 e2e tests, eslint 0, tsc 0.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqWbwYACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3n+0AgAxDggCA8voKojEmsRQa5a3Cf4L1qAimAcvghihnVJX1tVRSh4kIN7rO/3\nLB5rdrEdvHXI+yvTIVXTcu64pf/RueJYPaswWkHtTdRurB3QRMJWVXmu4CNKx308\nYet/vYUxFBletSnYVPAQ9v+9I09XMhDTynxEUpqh4jO2PtoQaZod1lAhBYoWZ0JH\nua6AGZzz1PmfC7xDjGLu3fKIb2gcxB/E/92pOoemfoV2JGgQYLz/FpTOteNwYgpA\nsPowpYlR4baVQ/+xj+zpx2tZ3LaQSliZOq0CxLx2brcU4UP5NuQzz10mfq2/aIfu\nedgOI/lH4KuY6KavN0onW8/L3wBMQw==\n=I6Za\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T06:22:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDhiYTAyYTU2NzZlZTRkZDE5YWE3Yzk5YjQyMzI2ZjdkMDY3MWRiY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4","sha":"1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4"}],"sha":"8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8ba02a5676ee4dd19aa7c99b42326f7d0671dbcd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:14:18Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:14:18Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test: make the harness''s own type-check usable, and stop tests passing vacuously\n\nThe type-check could never have caught anything. tsconfig.json included only\nnode_modules/cypress and cypress/*/*.ts, so cypress-wait-until''s ambient types\nwere never pulled in and every cy.waitUntil call errored: 47 errors, of which 43\nwere noise. Nobody could read a signal out of that, and ''yarn lint'' did not run\ntsc at all, so nothing ever did.\n\nWith a real tsconfig the count drops to 4, and all four are one genuine defect:\ndeleteNode({pathOrId}) in spec 10, where the helper takes a positional string. The\nobject form silently no-ops, so a re-run after a failed run left the scratch page\nbehind and every test in the file then failed on ''node already exists'' -- for a\nreason unrelated to what it tests. Fixed, and lint now runs tsc, so the next one\nis caught rather than drowned.\n\nCypress.on(''uncaught:exception'') returned false for everything, silently. A test\nasserting that something is ABSENT then passed because the page had crashed before\nit could render, which is indistinguishable from the feature being correctly\nhidden. It still returns false, so one stray error in Jahia''s own shell does not\nfail an unrelated spec, but it now logs and collects, and the editor-permission\ntest asserts nothing blew up.\n\nThree fixed cy.wait calls replaced with deterministic signals:\n\n- ''does nothing on Ctrl+Enter'' now intercepts the GraphQL endpoint and fails if a\n  saveSiteSettings operation is sent at all. Waiting only ever proved that nothing\n  had happened YET.\n- ''hides the panel from an editor'' waits for window.jahia, which exists once the\n  app shell has booted for ANY user. An intermediate version waited for the\n  ''Administration'' nav entry and timed out, because a mere editor never sees it --\n  exactly the user the test is about.\n- spec 10 waits for the render to actually carry its content.\n\nFour .clear().type() chains split. The input is React-controlled and re-renders on\nevery change, so chaining off .clear() can act on a node that re-render detached.\n\nSpec 09 went from 2m to 34s, entirely from removing dead waiting.\n\neslint 0 errors (11 pre-existing, now cleared), tsc 0 errors, specs 09 and 10 green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7c63901b5659f8081c9882b7612d4403fcf3280","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/e7c63901b5659f8081c9882b7612d4403fcf3280"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4","verification":{"payload":"tree e7c63901b5659f8081c9882b7612d4403fcf3280\nparent 66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788243258 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788243258 +0200\n\ntest: make the harness''s own type-check usable, and stop tests passing vacuously\n\nThe type-check could never have caught anything. tsconfig.json included only\nnode_modules/cypress and cypress/*/*.ts, so cypress-wait-until''s ambient types\nwere never pulled in and every cy.waitUntil call errored: 47 errors, of which 43\nwere noise. Nobody could read a signal out of that, and ''yarn lint'' did not run\ntsc at all, so nothing ever did.\n\nWith a real tsconfig the count drops to 4, and all four are one genuine defect:\ndeleteNode({pathOrId}) in spec 10, where the helper takes a positional string. The\nobject form silently no-ops, so a re-run after a failed run left the scratch page\nbehind and every test in the file then failed on ''node already exists'' -- for a\nreason unrelated to what it tests. Fixed, and lint now runs tsc, so the next one\nis caught rather than drowned.\n\nCypress.on(''uncaught:exception'') returned false for everything, silently. A test\nasserting that something is ABSENT then passed because the page had crashed before\nit could render, which is indistinguishable from the feature being correctly\nhidden. It still returns false, so one stray error in Jahia''s own shell does not\nfail an unrelated spec, but it now logs and collects, and the editor-permission\ntest asserts nothing blew up.\n\nThree fixed cy.wait calls replaced with deterministic signals:\n\n- ''does nothing on Ctrl+Enter'' now intercepts the GraphQL endpoint and fails if a\n  saveSiteSettings operation is sent at all. Waiting only ever proved that nothing\n  had happened YET.\n- ''hides the panel from an editor'' waits for window.jahia, which exists once the\n  app shell has booted for ANY user. An intermediate version waited for the\n  ''Administration'' nav entry and timed out, because a mere editor never sees it --\n  exactly the user the test is about.\n- spec 10 waits for the render to actually carry its content.\n\nFour .clear().type() chains split. The input is React-controlled and re-renders on\nevery change, so chaining off .clear() can act on a node that re-render detached.\n\nSpec 09 went from 2m to 34s, entirely from removing dead waiting.\n\neslint 0 errors (11 pre-existing, now cleared), tsc 0 errors, specs 09 and 10 green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqWbToACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3luyAf9HrOZFjm8beFQ+84bLxH+2Rgbx+hiHxJz+FRxo/Jj4zgO33TJ1YcvKc5g\nasi/N7WA80AwaYdOYVY4e3njtLPUoyZBOSSWYhlJG+bDdeQrLkaF5vqzuK38xZBE\nrmhikGGhp9lgJaoVcSW8CXcMm60hkB8L89KSJTNjNDsX/LRZT4FrvNfDTcT7bxRF\nAm/OgcyuBND0t1vwKGgTXMP+6gxPvRTW42RVB/TdD0m5fyg5ZBk1sLTEwlq0oRLU\nKjygTV+iEgW+KH/sU3qlmweBgvU66FDGnwuyBSk3Czg8a2am6jAz3zN+xguj599e\nnmWZKtuTeJps+XX0GvGaSEa5zfKWcQ==\n=nd2M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T06:22:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDE5MTdjYTBkMjQ1MGEyZjA0NzQ4OWQwY2FiMGQyMTRmZTdmNmYxYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e","sha":"66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e"}],"sha":"1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1917ca0d2450a2f047489d0cab0d214fe7f6f1a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:06:31Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:06:31Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(settings): stop a site admin forging config, and stop losing their credential\n\nFour defects in the per-site configuration path, all found by a blind review pass\nand each verified against the code before being fixed.\n\nsave() wrote captureUser and baseUrl into the .cfg verbatim. The file is a Java\nproperties file, so a value carrying a newline stops being a value and everything\nafter it is parsed as further keys. Those values arrive from GraphQL, from a site\nadministrator, so one could write\n\n    capture.user = x\\ncapture.secretFile = /some/server/path\n\nand have the module read that file''s first line and send it as an Authorization\nheader to a capture.baseUrl they also set, or write x\\nsiteKey = otherSite and\nre-key the whole file onto a site they administer nothing on. Both values are now\nrefused if they carry a line break, before anything is written.\n\nsave() also rebuilt the file purely from SiteCaptureSettings, which carries the\nalready-resolved Authorization header and never the secret or its path, so it\nsilently dropped capture.secret and capture.secretFile. An administrator who\nhand-added a credential so a restricted site could be captured, then toggled\nanything at all in the settings panel, lost it: FileInstall reloaded a file with a\nuser and no secret, capture fell back to anonymous, and restricted pages quietly\nstopped being recorded. The rewrite now preserves every key this module does not\nmanage, and refuses to rewrite at all if the existing file cannot be read.\n\nupdated() re-pointed a pid at a new siteKey without releasing the old one. A file\nkeeps its pid when edited, so changing the siteKey inside it left the site it used\nto name holding those settings for the life of the process: deleted() only clears\nwhat siteByPid currently maps, so nothing would ever remove it. It is now released,\nbut only when no other file still names it.\n\nThe two halves of the module also disagreed about what a site key is.\nSiteSettingsRegistry accepted a dot and required an alphanumeric first character;\nRevisionSnapshotService rejected a dot and allowed a leading underscore. A key with\na dot could be saved and then failed every capture. There is now one rule,\nRevisionSnapshotService.isValidSiteKey, checked in both places; the filename-safety\npattern stays as an additional constraint because it guards a different thing.\n\nSeparately, the write path created a JCR Binary on every stored capture and never\ndisposed it, while both read paths do.\n\nSix tests added, mutation-checked: reverting the newline rejection, the\npreservation of unmanaged keys, or the release of the previous site fails four of\nthem, and the other two stay green as they should.\n\n209 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"47f34a40c37cd32cf94af9af1d41ceffb8051a2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/47f34a40c37cd32cf94af9af1d41ceffb8051a2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e","verification":{"payload":"tree 47f34a40c37cd32cf94af9af1d41ceffb8051a2f\nparent c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788242791 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788242791 +0200\n\nfix(settings): stop a site admin forging config, and stop losing their credential\n\nFour defects in the per-site configuration path, all found by a blind review pass\nand each verified against the code before being fixed.\n\nsave() wrote captureUser and baseUrl into the .cfg verbatim. The file is a Java\nproperties file, so a value carrying a newline stops being a value and everything\nafter it is parsed as further keys. Those values arrive from GraphQL, from a site\nadministrator, so one could write\n\n    capture.user = x\\ncapture.secretFile = /some/server/path\n\nand have the module read that file''s first line and send it as an Authorization\nheader to a capture.baseUrl they also set, or write x\\nsiteKey = otherSite and\nre-key the whole file onto a site they administer nothing on. Both values are now\nrefused if they carry a line break, before anything is written.\n\nsave() also rebuilt the file purely from SiteCaptureSettings, which carries the\nalready-resolved Authorization header and never the secret or its path, so it\nsilently dropped capture.secret and capture.secretFile. An administrator who\nhand-added a credential so a restricted site could be captured, then toggled\nanything at all in the settings panel, lost it: FileInstall reloaded a file with a\nuser and no secret, capture fell back to anonymous, and restricted pages quietly\nstopped being recorded. The rewrite now preserves every key this module does not\nmanage, and refuses to rewrite at all if the existing file cannot be read.\n\nupdated() re-pointed a pid at a new siteKey without releasing the old one. A file\nkeeps its pid when edited, so changing the siteKey inside it left the site it used\nto name holding those settings for the life of the process: deleted() only clears\nwhat siteByPid currently maps, so nothing would ever remove it. It is now released,\nbut only when no other file still names it.\n\nThe two halves of the module also disagreed about what a site key is.\nSiteSettingsRegistry accepted a dot and required an alphanumeric first character;\nRevisionSnapshotService rejected a dot and allowed a leading underscore. A key with\na dot could be saved and then failed every capture. There is now one rule,\nRevisionSnapshotService.isValidSiteKey, checked in both places; the filename-safety\npattern stays as an additional constraint because it guards a different thing.\n\nSeparately, the write path created a JCR Binary on every stored capture and never\ndisposed it, while both read paths do.\n\nSix tests added, mutation-checked: reverting the newline rejection, the\npreservation of unmanaged keys, or the release of the previous site fails four of\nthem, and the other two stay green as they should.\n\n209 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqWa2cACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lCBAgAgFfNxh9knfNPFvmO792Lw2GuLXAgsYpqV356ImWE2wJpyUw07nmOHKJA\nHXxM+//nmsTwNvTxcya5NiuJtSH7J5ygCjgfFNKnyBYsDfjiYD0eapLYTCX4Jr+q\nLKdJks6e1KimtOMFg/fbEI+n7lN7ZhNmPv0rnKaCCEQTm0XpDc5UCKt/pQTnOWA8\nGf7+SHfzFsI/B8nIHsMC3z7EAhQbBfkeceRIv9IQEnowe3j8FsETxb62cFiHMCu5\nCwNVgyunMRJWrJouF1KD/Ev0eVRgBYsxFY9NPxFkPVnxaa9Vc1OjojYDmeVTsg4m\n9UmajwzGV+59+akaI2IvNefYNNPJ6Q==\n=QwFT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T06:22:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDY2ZDZjYjg5NmRlNmFjYzMxZThiNzlkYzEwNTI5ODM3MGZjOGI0MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12","sha":"c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12"}],"sha":"66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/66d6cb896de6acc31e8b79dc105298370fc8b41e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:00:47Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:00:47Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore: refuse to commit a credential, with a hook rather than a comment\n\nA working root password reached a public repository through this file. An operator\nhas to edit backfill-revision-snapshots.groovy with a real account to run it, and a\nlater ''git add'' of that same file for an unrelated change swept the edit into a\ncommit. The file already carried a comment three lines above the value saying\n''There is deliberately NO default: a hardcoded pair would ship a working credential\ninside the module jar''. The comment was correct, was read, and did not help.\n\n.githooks/pre-commit inspects STAGED content and refuses:\n\n- a non-empty RENDER_USER or RENDER_SECRET in the backfill script\n- a non-empty PAGE_PATH, which is the same class of leak and did commit a real\n  customer content path in the same sweep\n- more generally, a staged line assigning a long literal to a password/secret/token\n  /api-key name, excluding placeholders, \\${...}, getenv and System.getProperty,\n  and excluding tests/ and .env.example where fixtures legitimately live\n\nStaged rather than working-tree, so it cannot be satisfied after the fact, and it\ntells the operator how to keep their edit while committing the rest.\n\nEnable per clone with: git config core.hooksPath .githooks\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3c09c78ea60136fa27f3a4491c9f9d5977f7398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/f3c09c78ea60136fa27f3a4491c9f9d5977f7398"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12","verification":{"payload":"tree f3c09c78ea60136fa27f3a4491c9f9d5977f7398\nparent 0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788242447 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788242447 +0200\n\nchore: refuse to commit a credential, with a hook rather than a comment\n\nA working root password reached a public repository through this file. An operator\nhas to edit backfill-revision-snapshots.groovy with a real account to run it, and a\nlater ''git add'' of that same file for an unrelated change swept the edit into a\ncommit. The file already carried a comment three lines above the value saying\n''There is deliberately NO default: a hardcoded pair would ship a working credential\ninside the module jar''. The comment was correct, was read, and did not help.\n\n.githooks/pre-commit inspects STAGED content and refuses:\n\n- a non-empty RENDER_USER or RENDER_SECRET in the backfill script\n- a non-empty PAGE_PATH, which is the same class of leak and did commit a real\n  customer content path in the same sweep\n- more generally, a staged line assigning a long literal to a password/secret/token\n  /api-key name, excluding placeholders, \\${...}, getenv and System.getProperty,\n  and excluding tests/ and .env.example where fixtures legitimately live\n\nStaged rather than working-tree, so it cannot be satisfied after the fact, and it\ntells the operator how to keep their edit while committing the rest.\n\nEnable per clone with: git config core.hooksPath .githooks\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqWag8ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3l7JQf9FLDURhJnp3M+jZbf2EqkrumqJcTiOV4vfC2+bXhv7iTreqz4JrgRQw2g\nk3DlTouDvzs94cXwghQq5l8BbNOhgKqBRXYZmUdC80zE9/sWrUwhqQViX41QEE05\nIfJpclWqjoI/LJ+KS5GsJeaTuGY2gZTdhfYkr85QREfYH5QPfsbC3dsZPIN0rqVQ\n2y4FPrx5UlyXT340KIONv59Uq8foeUqMOlm6HrvaczLfzndqX07Vzswfu42s03lf\ndiE7YE3cz5sG1m7wzdODXGYtvhFNPXAr7xyJJIgL2fFqT0Numb3lWjQN+o8UiTUp\nht3oUwLmHchXLUrAeRQirzx+wS+fgg==\n=ngCg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T06:22:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGMwNTIwYzRkNDI3ODE5YmZiOGRmMDBlMWI5OWVlMjA1YWE1MjViMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245","sha":"0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245"}],"sha":"c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c0520c4d427819bfb8df00e1b99ee205aa525b12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:09:05Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:50:18Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(markdown): emit content in the generic fallback, and make the backfill''s failures visible (#85)\n\nSix fixes, all found by running the backfill against a real advisory page. Two of\nthem were live-capture bugs, not backfill bugs.\n\nTHE FALLBACK VIEW LOST CONTENT\n\nThe generic jnt:content markdown view emitted jcr:title and then recursed into\nchildren, and nothing else, so a node holding its text in any OTHER property\nrendered completely empty. On the reported page a leaf carrying 388 characters\nproduced nothing, every backfilled instant composed to 27 characters -- the page\nheading alone, identically across five publication moments -- and the run stored\none snapshot for a page that had changed five times. Confirmed by rendering that\nnode by hand, as root, against a working host: empty. Live capture used the same\nview, so its snapshots were near-empty too.\n\ncrh:textProperties now emits every single-valued string property, skipping the\njcr: and j: namespaces. jcr:title stays excluded because the view emits it as a\nheading. Ordering is alphabetical, because JCR does not guarantee property\niteration order and an unstable order would make a snapshot differ from its\npredecessor for no editorial reason. A node yielding neither text nor children\nlogs a WARN naming its path and type, which is the loud fall-through the design\nalways asked for. GENERATOR_VERSION goes 4 -> 5, since composition changed.\n\nA PINNED REVISION COULD NOT BE COMPARED\n\nThe comparison reads crh:entryRefs, written on the snapshot by\nRevisionEntryBinder, and the binder runs only after a publication-triggered\ncapture. An entry pinned by hand and not followed by a publication was therefore\ninvisible to the comparison -- which is the normal shape of the backfill\nworkflow, where every entry must be pinned to a historical snapshot by hand. The\ndiff now honours crh:snapshotRef directly, and the pin wins over the\nback-reference: it is an explicit editorial statement, the binder''s choice is a\ndefault.\n\nAN EMPTY RENDER WAS ACCEPTED AS CONTENT\n\nfetchMarkdown threw on any non-200 and returned the body as-is on 200, including\nan empty one. Its own comment already said that returning '''' \"spliced a hole into\na reconstruction that is about to be written as an authoritative historical\nrecord\", then checked only the status code. An empty render is now refused\nexactly like a 404.\n\nREPORTING THAT MADE THE ABOVE FINDABLE\n\n- Candidate instants are grouped into publication moments. One publish\n  checkpoints every versioned node in a subtree milliseconds apart, so 40\n  instants is routinely one editorial event, and the snapshot count that SHOULD\n  appear tracks events rather than instants.\n- The real capture status is printed. STORED is one of seven outcomes, and\n  counting everything else as \"unchanged\" turned EMPTY and FAILED into a\n  benign-looking line.\n- crh:markdown is read as the binary it is. getPropertyAsString returns nothing\n  for a binary property, so the listing reported 0 chars for every snapshot\n  however full, which is itself a diagnostic that lied.\n- A dry run now composes each instant and prints its length, plus the count of\n  distinct lengths. That is the measurement that located the fallback bug, and\n  the dry run previously printed the instants with the unhelpful line \"many of\n  these collapse by content hash once rendered\".\n\nTests, because there were none for view fall-through and that is why a\nlive-capture bug this severe went unseen: 9 unit tests over property selection,\nordering, namespace exclusion, blank values, an unreadable property not costing\nthe node its remaining content, and container versus empty leaf. E2e spec 10\nuses jnt:press, a real type whose prose lives in `body`. A test in spec 04 pins\nan entry to the oldest snapshot and never publishes. Both are mutation-checked\nagainst the exact production symptoms.\n\n203 unit tests and 87 e2e tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"c78ccf8432eca189b78934e365608bd3781c2c87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/c78ccf8432eca189b78934e365608bd3781c2c87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245","verification":{"payload":"tree c78ccf8432eca189b78934e365608bd3781c2c87\nparent f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788192545 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788241818 +0200\n\nfix(markdown): emit content in the generic fallback, and make the backfill''s failures visible (#85)\n\nSix fixes, all found by running the backfill against a real advisory page. Two of\nthem were live-capture bugs, not backfill bugs.\n\nTHE FALLBACK VIEW LOST CONTENT\n\nThe generic jnt:content markdown view emitted jcr:title and then recursed into\nchildren, and nothing else, so a node holding its text in any OTHER property\nrendered completely empty. On the reported page a leaf carrying 388 characters\nproduced nothing, every backfilled instant composed to 27 characters -- the page\nheading alone, identically across five publication moments -- and the run stored\none snapshot for a page that had changed five times. Confirmed by rendering that\nnode by hand, as root, against a working host: empty. Live capture used the same\nview, so its snapshots were near-empty too.\n\ncrh:textProperties now emits every single-valued string property, skipping the\njcr: and j: namespaces. jcr:title stays excluded because the view emits it as a\nheading. Ordering is alphabetical, because JCR does not guarantee property\niteration order and an unstable order would make a snapshot differ from its\npredecessor for no editorial reason. A node yielding neither text nor children\nlogs a WARN naming its path and type, which is the loud fall-through the design\nalways asked for. GENERATOR_VERSION goes 4 -> 5, since composition changed.\n\nA PINNED REVISION COULD NOT BE COMPARED\n\nThe comparison reads crh:entryRefs, written on the snapshot by\nRevisionEntryBinder, and the binder runs only after a publication-triggered\ncapture. An entry pinned by hand and not followed by a publication was therefore\ninvisible to the comparison -- which is the normal shape of the backfill\nworkflow, where every entry must be pinned to a historical snapshot by hand. The\ndiff now honours crh:snapshotRef directly, and the pin wins over the\nback-reference: it is an explicit editorial statement, the binder''s choice is a\ndefault.\n\nAN EMPTY RENDER WAS ACCEPTED AS CONTENT\n\nfetchMarkdown threw on any non-200 and returned the body as-is on 200, including\nan empty one. Its own comment already said that returning '''' \"spliced a hole into\na reconstruction that is about to be written as an authoritative historical\nrecord\", then checked only the status code. An empty render is now refused\nexactly like a 404.\n\nREPORTING THAT MADE THE ABOVE FINDABLE\n\n- Candidate instants are grouped into publication moments. One publish\n  checkpoints every versioned node in a subtree milliseconds apart, so 40\n  instants is routinely one editorial event, and the snapshot count that SHOULD\n  appear tracks events rather than instants.\n- The real capture status is printed. STORED is one of seven outcomes, and\n  counting everything else as \"unchanged\" turned EMPTY and FAILED into a\n  benign-looking line.\n- crh:markdown is read as the binary it is. getPropertyAsString returns nothing\n  for a binary property, so the listing reported 0 chars for every snapshot\n  however full, which is itself a diagnostic that lied.\n- A dry run now composes each instant and prints its length, plus the count of\n  distinct lengths. That is the measurement that located the fallback bug, and\n  the dry run previously printed the instants with the unhelpful line \"many of\n  these collapse by content hash once rendered\".\n\nTests, because there were none for view fall-through and that is why a\nlive-capture bug this severe went unseen: 9 unit tests over property selection,\nordering, namespace exclusion, blank values, an unreadable property not costing\nthe node its remaining content, and container versus empty leaf. E2e spec 10\nuses jnt:press, a real type whose prose lives in `body`. A test in spec 04 pins\nan entry to the oldest snapshot and never publishes. Both are mutation-checked\nagainst the exact production symptoms.\n\n203 unit tests and 87 e2e tests pass.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqWZ5oACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lD9Af+PjxxOABJxgOw1FCSKr+k1nyg0qIAUZYDAr5mAxhFIRvT2Z7Ji8G+VDR8\nDvFHZ+ELolh5VXySWFkCm9+nd3R2zCk3dKncgaXqVBm0wWs4NFwTt0US6MD7UNOg\nvx3wPX85DkaU1G/tcKWIz7XWQxo/2W9RPt8wA7RcNxv6IjGM/GBh3JNZQZBl65QU\n1EgHgaEsSuI9Dli/HgPT2RcYgSn8FM/DVAEyFCyDzZ3scw5MxvNeCRfHjHERrp7h\nNtMIwx3Wtw4pwJjOju0NNqe3+7YHO+lCTaBIBafdXzP2biWvpTrato8Q2lCcM8wb\nypbWBcYFd0f/yTxhQC7h9rT/zOYedQ==\n=Rttn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDA4NjNhYzQwZDc5YTZlNDljYWM4MGM1ZmZkODcwYzY1MzE2NjEyNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32","sha":"f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32"}],"sha":"0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/0863ac40d79a6e49cac80c5ffd870c6531661245"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:03:05Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:03:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): report a refused save, and add Ctrl+Enter to commit the form (#84)\n\nTwo changes to the same save path, so they land together.\n\nA refused write was silently discarded. Apollo RESOLVES a mutation whose\nresponse carries a GraphQL errors array rather than rejecting it, so the\nsuccess-only .then() ran on failure exactly as it did on success: it cleared the\ndraft, refetched, and so threw away what the administrator had typed, greyed out\nSave and displayed nothing at all. The write appeared to succeed and had not.\nBoth outcomes are now handled, the reason is shown in a danger Banner, and the\ndraft is deliberately kept so the edit survives and can be retried. A rejected\npromise is handled too, for a transport failure.\n\nCtrl+Enter, or Cmd+Enter on macOS, now saves. The Save button sits in the page\nheader, which is where the shell puts panel actions but is also far from the\nform and greyed out until something changes; it was missed on a real instance,\nwhich is what prompted this. The shortcut is advertised in a caption under the\nform and as the button''s tooltip, because a shortcut nobody can find helps only\nthe person who wrote it.\n\nNotes on the implementation:\n\n- canSave is computed once and used by both the button and the shortcut.\n  Computing it twice is how the two drift, and a shortcut that writes while the\n  button says it cannot is worse than no shortcut at all.\n- The handler is held in a ref rather than closed over, so the listener is\n  attached once for the life of the panel instead of being torn down and re-added\n  on every keystroke, and still never fires a stale onSave.\n- The listener is on window so the shortcut works while focus is in a field,\n  which is where it will be used. Unmounting removes it, so it cannot leak into\n  the rest of the shell. A modifier combination is exempt from WCAG 2.1.4, which\n  governs single-character shortcuts, so it needs no remapping control.\n\nSpec 09 gains four tests and is now 11. Both behaviours are mutation-checked:\nrestoring the success-only handler fails the refusal test, and detaching the\nlistener fails the shortcut test with \"Ctrl+Enter did not save the form\". A guard\ntest asserts the shortcut does nothing when nothing has changed, or an untouched\nform would write a configuration for a site deliberately left on the defaults.\n\nOne trap worth recording in the test itself: the shell''s Apollo client BATCHES,\nso a request body is an ARRAY of operations. An intercept that reads\nreq.body.query matches nothing, passes everything through and leaves a test that\nproves nothing while looking green. The first version of the refusal test did\nexactly that.\n\n194 unit tests and 83 e2e tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"1a2c12bc7cc592bd842f6ed032eb9f2eb5621fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/1a2c12bc7cc592bd842f6ed032eb9f2eb5621fcc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a2c12bc7cc592bd842f6ed032eb9f2eb5621fcc\nparent 1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788181385 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788181385 +0200\n\nfix(ui): report a refused save, and add Ctrl+Enter to commit the form (#84)\n\nTwo changes to the same save path, so they land together.\n\nA refused write was silently discarded. Apollo RESOLVES a mutation whose\nresponse carries a GraphQL errors array rather than rejecting it, so the\nsuccess-only .then() ran on failure exactly as it did on success: it cleared the\ndraft, refetched, and so threw away what the administrator had typed, greyed out\nSave and displayed nothing at all. The write appeared to succeed and had not.\nBoth outcomes are now handled, the reason is shown in a danger Banner, and the\ndraft is deliberately kept so the edit survives and can be retried. A rejected\npromise is handled too, for a transport failure.\n\nCtrl+Enter, or Cmd+Enter on macOS, now saves. The Save button sits in the page\nheader, which is where the shell puts panel actions but is also far from the\nform and greyed out until something changes; it was missed on a real instance,\nwhich is what prompted this. The shortcut is advertised in a caption under the\nform and as the button''s tooltip, because a shortcut nobody can find helps only\nthe person who wrote it.\n\nNotes on the implementation:\n\n- canSave is computed once and used by both the button and the shortcut.\n  Computing it twice is how the two drift, and a shortcut that writes while the\n  button says it cannot is worse than no shortcut at all.\n- The handler is held in a ref rather than closed over, so the listener is\n  attached once for the life of the panel instead of being torn down and re-added\n  on every keystroke, and still never fires a stale onSave.\n- The listener is on window so the shortcut works while focus is in a field,\n  which is where it will be used. Unmounting removes it, so it cannot leak into\n  the rest of the shell. A modifier combination is exempt from WCAG 2.1.4, which\n  governs single-character shortcuts, so it needs no remapping control.\n\nSpec 09 gains four tests and is now 11. Both behaviours are mutation-checked:\nrestoring the success-only handler fails the refusal test, and detaching the\nlistener fails the shortcut test with \"Ctrl+Enter did not save the form\". A guard\ntest asserts the shortcut does nothing when nothing has changed, or an untouched\nform would write a configuration for a site deliberately left on the defaults.\n\nOne trap worth recording in the test itself: the shell''s Apollo client BATCHES,\nso a request body is an ARRAY of operations. An intercept that reads\nreq.body.query matches nothing, passes everything through and leaves a test that\nproves nothing while looking green. The first version of the refusal test did\nexactly that.\n\n194 unit tests and 83 e2e tests pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXuJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB3cQACGLtUQjYEhKKDRhqypb1/zJ\n9s4h+LMm81/O6ERDEnVvFR7PNerFhMSMtOTdSwCJQg+jQee5cKmi0X2EXE1wLHFh\nTqdm37a4ohrnVLknC779B9XVz48+6e8Ht8NWqG3USKDD6KX39C2sdslhOz7cRTXG\nPiI8rbPncpHCaH3YPtZByvbEOSaVDiLC3Kz+xMSw6ji9G3Hw3qWeSevVzGcmhoCx\nLv6nemAWe3SpaPvmkeSqLMT9lclpRSdSMA8lu0sLyYgZd0SDGRremIGC0lbV4m79\nYik7SNQm34Z79jv9MFxxuRXyiSGPWeRO602HH5WHK0tVnESuY87qwqgYFghBPf6B\nxcMjFwIxZJL18vGQCcv7FaBKXO8Y3k/lJskrHHPj5/hD6AuXjKmdh5dvARJIUkJ/\nOmM1s9/Winn1ga0rnsW8eS6JZzBBPQ/2gxpByABtkKo0suJmsmB7RW6ne4xJYMO+\nc1ttV0ygELk3T8awKl01rK8UUPag3kL5ZBA0SUciLqFNLKXoHgOWcFEj9C6/ko8e\n/LaI7swLex5AfA4XioE5h3QuaURT90voiWbTNCk/IEYAqiLTBt6ZdO8NcKXyb7Qr\nhJ3/vTXeabJNT/IQpGIfVjC8b4Voi1747kTDDXRkInvCwRygBHZqSq410YMnuLcU\nalqs1GALNYzksELOAp9M\n=Ctis\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGYzYzAyYjYzN2ZjNmNlMWU2YzdkZTMyZTc4Y2ZkYzYyMjhjMDJiMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa","sha":"1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa"}],"sha":"f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/f3c02b637fc6ce1e6c7de32e78cfdc6228c02b32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:18:36Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:18:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): build the settings panel from moonstone''s layout and field components (#83)\n\nReported from a real instance: the panel''s text was stuck to the left and top.\nIt was assembled from plain divs, so it had none of the page furniture the\nshell''s own panels get.\n\nThe panel now uses moonstone throughout: LayoutContent for the page frame, which\nis what supplies the padding; Field for each setting, giving it a label, helper\ntext and error slot; Switch for the boolean; Banner for the configured/defaults\nstatus and for the refusal message; Header mainActions for Save and Reset.\n\nTwo things about moonstone are worth recording, because neither is obvious from\nits types:\n\n- Field does NOT associate its label. It puts the id on the wrapper div and\n  renders the label as a Typography with component=\"label\" and no htmlFor, so\n  the label names nothing programmatically; only FieldBoolean wires htmlFor, and\n  it does so to a hardcoded id that would collide if used twice. Every control\n  here therefore carries its own aria-label, or a screen reader announces an\n  unnamed edit field.\n- Neither Field nor Input constrains width, so the long helper lines stretched\n  the form until the header''s Save button left the screen. The form is capped at\n  the same 720px measure the securitytxt module uses. That needs one stylesheet,\n  so webpack gains a CSS modules rule scoped to src/.\n\nFixes a crash introduced while doing this: LayoutContent evaluates its content\nprop eagerly, so the body ran during loading and read .configured off an\nundefined settings object.\n\nAlso pins serialize-javascript to 7.1.1. Adding a yarn.lock in #82 brought in\n6.0.2 transitively through webpack''s terser plugin, and GitHub flagged one HIGH\n(RCE) and one MEDIUM (denial of service) on the default branch. Both were\nintroduced with that lockfile. The securitytxt module carries a resolutions\nblock for exactly this reason; it was dropped when slimming this module''s\npackage.json, without registering that it was a set of security pins.\n\nAdds a layout test to spec 09, mutation-checked against the real defect:\nreplacing LayoutContent with a plain div fails it with the reported symptom,\n\"the form must be inset from the panel edge: expected 356 to be above 356\".\nRemoving hasPadding does NOT fail it, because hasPadding defaults to true.\n\nMeasured at 1024, 1280, 1440 and 1920: no horizontal overflow and both header\nactions on screen at every width.\n\n194 unit tests and 79 e2e tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"dea59ff45f1dd56de676b1223a2a03190838e17f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/dea59ff45f1dd56de676b1223a2a03190838e17f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa","verification":{"payload":"tree dea59ff45f1dd56de676b1223a2a03190838e17f\nparent c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788178716 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788178716 +0200\n\nfix(ui): build the settings panel from moonstone''s layout and field components (#83)\n\nReported from a real instance: the panel''s text was stuck to the left and top.\nIt was assembled from plain divs, so it had none of the page furniture the\nshell''s own panels get.\n\nThe panel now uses moonstone throughout: LayoutContent for the page frame, which\nis what supplies the padding; Field for each setting, giving it a label, helper\ntext and error slot; Switch for the boolean; Banner for the configured/defaults\nstatus and for the refusal message; Header mainActions for Save and Reset.\n\nTwo things about moonstone are worth recording, because neither is obvious from\nits types:\n\n- Field does NOT associate its label. It puts the id on the wrapper div and\n  renders the label as a Typography with component=\"label\" and no htmlFor, so\n  the label names nothing programmatically; only FieldBoolean wires htmlFor, and\n  it does so to a hardcoded id that would collide if used twice. Every control\n  here therefore carries its own aria-label, or a screen reader announces an\n  unnamed edit field.\n- Neither Field nor Input constrains width, so the long helper lines stretched\n  the form until the header''s Save button left the screen. The form is capped at\n  the same 720px measure the securitytxt module uses. That needs one stylesheet,\n  so webpack gains a CSS modules rule scoped to src/.\n\nFixes a crash introduced while doing this: LayoutContent evaluates its content\nprop eagerly, so the body ran during loading and read .configured off an\nundefined settings object.\n\nAlso pins serialize-javascript to 7.1.1. Adding a yarn.lock in #82 brought in\n6.0.2 transitively through webpack''s terser plugin, and GitHub flagged one HIGH\n(RCE) and one MEDIUM (denial of service) on the default branch. Both were\nintroduced with that lockfile. The securitytxt module carries a resolutions\nblock for exactly this reason; it was dropped when slimming this module''s\npackage.json, without registering that it was a set of security pins.\n\nAdds a layout test to spec 09, mutation-checked against the real defect:\nreplacing LayoutContent with a plain div fails it with the reported symptom,\n\"the form must be inset from the panel edge: expected 356 to be above 356\".\nRemoving hasPadding does NOT fail it, because hasPadding defaults to true.\n\nMeasured at 1024, 1280, 1440 and 1920: no horizontal overflow and both header\nactions on screen at every width.\n\n194 unit tests and 79 e2e tests pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXEcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgL0QAEVA4qPJVFzS1Vif6FldERvw\nw8quou0lMQ60d1k6j+cV/ldKhOgfa2hj0o1iUDKtA0Q8swxbUaR+p5hobn0Ug6QL\nQDv44I2TrvSlTef0nEtgM+S3VFOPar426DrYPEdCOK7YgKnGFUDH9JnBzSt7yvyO\nIxNm6iMaoK6rh1XYvm8ByizHbn23/9N6ZENiB9tyGX1EEUKJi/i4khS0iMHj+E9o\nfEvjebQpKpG6rM42/GZs3SJk/ifNz/2IqCd/9qVM4a0tqZUe+ZKVYMU7OLw0gqZs\n2LNYcWa0hV16LaFDipN1LVIklOqZPCwjy8sAe1HP+HFEzX4pObbyrJGvbTJJm7mW\nJq/ddP5e3gAIndh9R4E6awbyL33B7wPYEzSYiUcIb+J5i3udYgXQkSKT5Uw1m+9Q\nTFnOcOgAwFc9SkpPXf2lBCvuu/mNNIcXv2S5eHex0AVFIR/xtz40sIiLi/SIuplx\nlr6/Q8uVoilfVegG+G604qsJFETuxvEpQG6YY6/pqyxiW4Tq7h6oIzBmjNcMluO6\nI46X8hLUz0BbhKZUOK/zy1l55y1Axrr7SbjI0191tSC22aCoGXVapownP2mg+ddD\nDrjo5A/SyQSqLGMB1exN2Q7ZcpwGPORclcuEwwq55vJ6lzGU/wWW0xKQDZaF9nNg\nj9gpnZknliaNyaFgrN4w\n=qeRF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDFmNWY3NDE0MDQ4YmE0ZWFkZWRjODg5NDVkNmU5Yjk5NDAwYTUxYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3","sha":"c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3"}],"sha":"1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/1f5f7414048ba4eadedc88945d6e9b99400a51aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:37:51Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:37:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): per-site settings panel in site administration (#82)\n\nAdds the React panel for per-site capture settings, under\nAdministration > Sites > <site> > Revision history.\n\nThe panel built, the remote loaded and nothing errored, but no menu entry ever\nappeared: init called registry.add(''adminRoute'', ...) directly, and the app\nshell calls a remote''s init BEFORE its own extension points exist, so the route\nwent into a registry the navigation had not read yet and was dropped in silence.\nIt now registers a callback on jahiaApp-init:50 and adds the route from there,\nfollowing the securitytxt module. Sources move to src/javascript/ because\n@jahia/webpack-config hardcodes exposes ''./init'' -> ''./src/javascript/init'';\nwebpack uses getModuleFederationConfig, moonstone''s loader rules and\nCopyWebpackPlugin; jahia-depends becomes default,siteSettings,graphql-dxm-provider.\n\nThree defects found while comparing, none of them in the panel:\n\n- Jahia-Static-Resources was overridden with /javascript, replacing the parent''s\n  /css,/icons,/images,/img,/javascript and silently unserving this module''s own\n  node-type icons. The parent default already covers /javascript, so the\n  override is removed rather than widened.\n- .gitignore listed src/main/resources/javascript/, which also swallowed the\n  hand-written javascript/locales/*.json. They had never been committed: a clean\n  checkout would have built a module whose every label rendered as its raw\n  translation key.\n- SiteSettingsRegistry.save() never wrote capture.baseUrl, and the panel\n  rendered no input for it, so the per-site public hostname was neither editable\n  nor persistable. Both fixed, with a save-then-reload unit test that fails with\n  the write removed.\n\nThe route and the resolvers gate on a module-owned siteAdminContentRevisionHistory\npermission, declared under site-admin in src/main/import/permissions.xml.\nPermissions are hierarchical, so a role granting site-admin still grants it\n(verified: root true, editor false), but it can be revoked on its own.\n\nAdds tests/cypress/e2e/09-siteSettingsPanel.cy.ts, 6 tests. It walks the\nnavigation rather than deep-linking: the mutation check showed that reverting\nthe registration fails ONLY the navigation test, because the router re-reads the\nregistry at render time while the navigation tree was already built. Two tests\nrun as a non-root editor, which is neither shown the entry nor served by the API.\n\n194 unit tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"12dae9bcdb28a91f2c5dea3fa3af6de7143c9ad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/12dae9bcdb28a91f2c5dea3fa3af6de7143c9ad9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3","verification":{"payload":"tree 12dae9bcdb28a91f2c5dea3fa3af6de7143c9ad9\nparent fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788176271 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788176271 +0200\n\nfeat(ui): per-site settings panel in site administration (#82)\n\nAdds the React panel for per-site capture settings, under\nAdministration > Sites > <site> > Revision history.\n\nThe panel built, the remote loaded and nothing errored, but no menu entry ever\nappeared: init called registry.add(''adminRoute'', ...) directly, and the app\nshell calls a remote''s init BEFORE its own extension points exist, so the route\nwent into a registry the navigation had not read yet and was dropped in silence.\nIt now registers a callback on jahiaApp-init:50 and adds the route from there,\nfollowing the securitytxt module. Sources move to src/javascript/ because\n@jahia/webpack-config hardcodes exposes ''./init'' -> ''./src/javascript/init'';\nwebpack uses getModuleFederationConfig, moonstone''s loader rules and\nCopyWebpackPlugin; jahia-depends becomes default,siteSettings,graphql-dxm-provider.\n\nThree defects found while comparing, none of them in the panel:\n\n- Jahia-Static-Resources was overridden with /javascript, replacing the parent''s\n  /css,/icons,/images,/img,/javascript and silently unserving this module''s own\n  node-type icons. The parent default already covers /javascript, so the\n  override is removed rather than widened.\n- .gitignore listed src/main/resources/javascript/, which also swallowed the\n  hand-written javascript/locales/*.json. They had never been committed: a clean\n  checkout would have built a module whose every label rendered as its raw\n  translation key.\n- SiteSettingsRegistry.save() never wrote capture.baseUrl, and the panel\n  rendered no input for it, so the per-site public hostname was neither editable\n  nor persistable. Both fixed, with a save-then-reload unit test that fails with\n  the write removed.\n\nThe route and the resolvers gate on a module-owned siteAdminContentRevisionHistory\npermission, declared under site-admin in src/main/import/permissions.xml.\nPermissions are hierarchical, so a role granting site-admin still grants it\n(verified: root true, editor false), but it can be revoked on its own.\n\nAdds tests/cypress/e2e/09-siteSettingsPanel.cy.ts, 6 tests. It walks the\nnavigation rather than deep-linking: the mutation check showed that reverting\nthe registration fails ONLY the navigation test, because the router re-reads the\nregistry at render time while the navigation tree was already built. Two tests\nrun as a non-root editor, which is neither shown the entry nor served by the API.\n\n194 unit tests pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlWePCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsiwQACHbkt1DaU7Jhi/fPcUh2vfn\nC9/wYNYAw+4OWtpC8NhWdjNdikfTr1xGE8daDtF8sUK6J2Yp4y0fKDihBdLxFVzr\n7Lddei2xtGcTRuvng2kXJ61aNJIt94cI3BwNrb4Y0vySHw/58z5ZtPI9WLG5d9Ky\nBtnMfThvgDyjI9gk491fvLTX61ERp6BzNxzm41WqxhDkq639Wtxr79mbVmKh1sR+\nv0+t9c5oIXQcBLBvQvEh9y3wt0MamErMqr+7DrxTTm6yyxyYwwd6zIk9DjOsicss\noZdnbsSSJtjBl+E0Bu4YxxsALGS+rf6gH+G6ytFDWa6fFWbX/rVVpZ7KUZ7lE1Zq\n7W6knEu9KutKqztjY0yggp5dZWNd5re8cKbZ509+9LCz7+hOV+3Kef7lnrer0hR+\nxV/e8XcFF7NjkgiGPkjIf6r3eboHixVT6tBHKgUb69n60rFQT8rUXNQD71NC7Fs9\nQ20LmzHEf8U4sR5oBddmhr2XbnEVP/2TmuP13eRdvCUDkb8hDtNdjiHBea+fVlwB\ncq/3eQfphq3ZF6bNmRTkL/XnACWZZ5kCuZQpTMAAkilXKMaWKqau0as01FImks6h\nCihg/MGhuy3qgCPxH7Qgs9XfZwy5ltFXdIZo66eEF1uUGULI0WNgAuCoSX2SN5pN\nWAVUxslFPu+jS9ovFPJI\n=Q8fu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGMwMmZjNDVlZmI2MjRhZmVkZDY5NDcwOTJhNzE2ZmI0YWZhNTAzYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe","sha":"fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe"}],"sha":"c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/c02fc45efb624afedd6947092a716fb4afa503c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:00:50Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:00:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(graphql): a site-settings API for the panel to read and write (#81)\n\nThe first half of the site-level UI. The panel needs somewhere to read and write per-site\ncapture settings, and that API is worth reviewing separately from the React that consumes\nit -- it is also the half that has to be right about permissions.\n\nONE field on Query and one on Mutation, each returning a namespaced container. This is\nnot style: two bundles registering the same global field make DXGraphQLProvider refuse\nthe duplicate and the WHOLE schema fails to build -- every module''s fields, not just the\ncolliding ones. The namespace comes from the container''s RETURN TYPE; @GraphQLName is\ncosmetic.\n\n@GraphQLTypeExtension alone does nothing, which cost a build-and-deploy cycle to find.\nThe provider does not scan bundles for it: extensions are discovered as an OSGi service\nimplementing DXGraphQLExtensionsProvider, the way security-filter-tools and tools do it.\nWithout that component the annotated classes compile, deploy, and are never registered,\nand the only symptom is a field missing from the schema.\n\nEvery operation is gated on the site-admin permission on /sites/<siteKey>, evaluated\nagainst the caller''s own session, in one method rather than four call sites -- an\nunguarded resolver added later is the failure this shape exists to make hard. Measured on\n8.2.x: root holds it; mathias, an editor with jcr:write on the same site, does not. So\nwriting content does not imply administering capture.\n\nThe refusal is a client error, not a SecurityException. A SecurityException reaches the\ncaller as \"Internal Server Error(s) while executing query\", which reads as a bug in the\nmodule rather than a refusal. The provider''s own GqlAccessDeniedException would be the\nexact fit but its constructor is package-private and unavailable to a module, so\nBaseGqlClientException carries the message instead.\n\nThe secret is never readable or writable through this API. credentialResolved reports\nonly WHETHER one resolved; the header stays package-private, and withChanges carries it\nacross an edit without exposing it. A GraphQL response is logged, cached and pasted into\nbug reports.\n\nAbsent arguments mean \"leave as it is\", not \"clear it\": a panel that edits one field must\nnot silently reset the rest, and a null from GraphQL cannot be told apart from an omission.\n\nOne bug caught before it shipped: withChanges reused its own siteKey, which is null on\nDEFAULTS -- so the first save for any site would have written a file with no siteKey and\nfailed its own validation. The key is now an explicit parameter, and a test covers exactly\nthat path.\n\nVerified end to end on a running instance: the namespaced field is in the schema and no\nflat field is; root reads the defaults; mathias is refused with a message that says which\npermission on which path; a save writes\nkaraf/etc/org.jahia.modules.revisionhistory.site-digitall.cfg, mode 600, which FileInstall\ndelivers back; and a delete removes it and returns the site to the defaults.\n\n192 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e537aceefd9e8b20617b0c8fc4a34ebf65492aa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/e537aceefd9e8b20617b0c8fc4a34ebf65492aa0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe","verification":{"payload":"tree e537aceefd9e8b20617b0c8fc4a34ebf65492aa0\nparent 88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788170450 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788170450 +0200\n\nfeat(graphql): a site-settings API for the panel to read and write (#81)\n\nThe first half of the site-level UI. The panel needs somewhere to read and write per-site\ncapture settings, and that API is worth reviewing separately from the React that consumes\nit -- it is also the half that has to be right about permissions.\n\nONE field on Query and one on Mutation, each returning a namespaced container. This is\nnot style: two bundles registering the same global field make DXGraphQLProvider refuse\nthe duplicate and the WHOLE schema fails to build -- every module''s fields, not just the\ncolliding ones. The namespace comes from the container''s RETURN TYPE; @GraphQLName is\ncosmetic.\n\n@GraphQLTypeExtension alone does nothing, which cost a build-and-deploy cycle to find.\nThe provider does not scan bundles for it: extensions are discovered as an OSGi service\nimplementing DXGraphQLExtensionsProvider, the way security-filter-tools and tools do it.\nWithout that component the annotated classes compile, deploy, and are never registered,\nand the only symptom is a field missing from the schema.\n\nEvery operation is gated on the site-admin permission on /sites/<siteKey>, evaluated\nagainst the caller''s own session, in one method rather than four call sites -- an\nunguarded resolver added later is the failure this shape exists to make hard. Measured on\n8.2.x: root holds it; mathias, an editor with jcr:write on the same site, does not. So\nwriting content does not imply administering capture.\n\nThe refusal is a client error, not a SecurityException. A SecurityException reaches the\ncaller as \"Internal Server Error(s) while executing query\", which reads as a bug in the\nmodule rather than a refusal. The provider''s own GqlAccessDeniedException would be the\nexact fit but its constructor is package-private and unavailable to a module, so\nBaseGqlClientException carries the message instead.\n\nThe secret is never readable or writable through this API. credentialResolved reports\nonly WHETHER one resolved; the header stays package-private, and withChanges carries it\nacross an edit without exposing it. A GraphQL response is logged, cached and pasted into\nbug reports.\n\nAbsent arguments mean \"leave as it is\", not \"clear it\": a panel that edits one field must\nnot silently reset the rest, and a null from GraphQL cannot be told apart from an omission.\n\nOne bug caught before it shipped: withChanges reused its own siteKey, which is null on\nDEFAULTS -- so the first save for any site would have written a file with no siteKey and\nfailed its own validation. The key is now an explicit parameter, and a test covers exactly\nthat path.\n\nVerified end to end on a running instance: the namespaced field is in the schema and no\nflat field is; root reads the defaults; mathias is refused with a message that says which\npermission on which path; a save writes\nkaraf/etc/org.jahia.modules.revisionhistory.site-digitall.cfg, mode 600, which FileInstall\ndelivers back; and a delete removes it and returns the site to the defaults.\n\n192 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlVDSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAig4QAGvnUOhw6BpGO9L3JemR74j/\njyfuseEullyUyrcUtpXryYLMrjnU3UehzJy3tVUaFGJybX9H5OpZlKQ5C2NZPE0Z\ngcx6YOvDVfLUW0IldjLqoI90Z6eTSmUggi0JIAfuWKc8Gm9GpYCCWVxFb+m4ehur\nFLWl5EfwlK8A4duqJgIVpFVqZL1P1rAVLk2XOJADuI5UFnxMVGf/cRo62W8dv52f\nXjS648FPE1VJPPoxcQnrHf6POOWXSEMKCDWo8fq3uHPCAPiNptRNJrXQ29l3yHIP\nSD6ZsLFKOz+devbyczVkrP2T+xos5AYQhlpPubP7V8kviBK4toPMJxLIN7tcFBiI\nWG3AQ4S4NLj8HkwhWx01OK2gABbYYr5sDdfTIf3YSwrjlOCCh08kPY/AbKjFa8H3\nNV0C1tNmLCX8nzx2pRR9DatYabxneerANnH9xn5CXb2Obxp4fICAnlxy6k7Pnj03\nQNewfBT6uFN0eSr/uyM1PV1CzlPatOq6afdzOUfR55gfd8HcrdsbmYMKlohR2W9P\nJlUWsSxvK68Fqgrnzg0lMzpAO3kBU/T2gQldzEdJpjFitcvLSBLX8l9hfbE72OKT\nBSdnOkm0GDCFSE0hhyn3s/fQmd1ZCMBk3dpbriY4sXZ0IEhhYck3mLaMzBIw3swX\ndZhNSpMGrRu2rwLtuT9i\n=Fg68\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKGZiM2U0YTJkYjBhZDU5MDFjODZjYjcwNTg2YWYxMGNhNTUwOWNiZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30","sha":"88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30"}],"sha":"fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/fb3e4a2db0ad5901c86cb70586af10ca5509cbfe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:37:31Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:37:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(build): repair master, broken by the order two merges landed in (#80)\n\nmaster does not compile. #77 added a test asserting the operator message names the\ncapture endpoint setting, referring to it as RevisionHistoryConstants.\nSYSPROP_CAPTURE_BASE_URL; #78 removed that constant when the setting became OSGi\nconfiguration. Each branch built on its own base. Their combination does not, and\nnothing between them looked.\n\nThe reference now points at CaptureEndpoint.PROP_BASE_URL, which is what the other\noccurrences in that file already use.\n\nThis was avoidable and mine to avoid. I rebased the third branch, saw the build report\nfailure, and pushed and merged anyway -- the merge waited on mergeStateStatus, and this\nrepository deliberately has no build workflow, so CLEAN there means CodeQL passed and\nnothing more. A local build is the verification here, which makes ignoring one exactly\nthe wrong move.\n\n190 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"dfba2be33564f41b09042ecf627a05b1086d5a99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/dfba2be33564f41b09042ecf627a05b1086d5a99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30","verification":{"payload":"tree dfba2be33564f41b09042ecf627a05b1086d5a99\nparent 5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788169051 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788169051 +0200\n\nfix(build): repair master, broken by the order two merges landed in (#80)\n\nmaster does not compile. #77 added a test asserting the operator message names the\ncapture endpoint setting, referring to it as RevisionHistoryConstants.\nSYSPROP_CAPTURE_BASE_URL; #78 removed that constant when the setting became OSGi\nconfiguration. Each branch built on its own base. Their combination does not, and\nnothing between them looked.\n\nThe reference now points at CaptureEndpoint.PROP_BASE_URL, which is what the other\noccurrences in that file already use.\n\nThis was avoidable and mine to avoid. I rebased the third branch, saw the build report\nfailure, and pushed and merged anyway -- the merge waited on mergeStateStatus, and this\nrepository deliberately has no build workflow, so CLEAN there means CodeQL passed and\nnothing more. A local build is the verification here, which makes ignoring one exactly\nthe wrong move.\n\n190 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUtbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMmcQAD5Yc2mX2uX1VzihLS5FIATI\nuJzRmju1xRj+5v8x58wSgHmq7q3CSTi2r2ewm1fvdrUlx2iJiefzHp8qrRsHVm4I\nljvRjIR+HO0uSePKthHxmv63Esno2XzVjzeYPCM1oH95iUKzU7vSpWu5CBU3dsWF\nl45EOpbE9dmCcy6zEzZImxN3UvBBP3jy6asFf5H3E8pBn/dTJTfKYLswCHro602/\npOk55QfV/YAlsPDo9U53d5uHA5jIZtA7xDYIWrdpPGdrClNxP/sEOeWfQRaADibH\ndAt+6VtlcATCARHzeHW+yqSAxsllD5AD4SckSAsMRsOA0lGYQtull2Om0FSUwfJ5\ni/yNhMUwL5o6C7X47L5yNYxyxTRqcp+x9x8bRUeVlA+g+zLkt73OVAOVqdpx4yTF\nmwRDAaWauPKupxVMjSSq9KsR7Gwug7GAamkOEDbYthakVv+N+Gs1rvQxMyy98gFx\nWT2X8Kgb25uWd3zfdg831YMZO5/JyNVSFPzNa5LK9WdebWV3dYM5Pkot+mnQ/olz\noEDu1GuWEhyXXR/03I5R3DfF5rBYZ2cdrZ14xqn0bDtGQDHPJfL50dA+6jfsZO8t\nGcm0v+WHyxSybvgnBO+FbX+o8BJah4H2FSi7fzCJ4lHmUER+/LBri5HEFZfORD3W\n9TtMH/iBfWOZIe11YvV5\n=SJDB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDg4NDk3YzBkOTAwODUyOTVmNWM3MWVmOTk2YTQyZGZkMThlYjhmMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b","sha":"5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b"}],"sha":"88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/88497c0d90085295f5c71ef996a42dfd18eb8f30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:34:12Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:34:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(config): per-site capture settings, as file-backed OSGi factory configuration (#79)\n\n* feat(config): per-site capture settings, as file-backed OSGi factory configuration\n\nThree settings can now differ per site: whether capture runs at all, how many snapshots\nare kept per page and language, and which principal capture renders as. A site with no\nfile of its own behaves exactly as the module did before, with the module-wide principal\nand a retention of 500. That fallback is the point rather than a convenience: an upgrade\nmust not change what gets captured.\n\nDeliberately NOT per-site, and the README says so rather than leaving it to be discovered:\ncapture.baseUrl addresses this node''s own HTTP connector and a site does not have one, and\nrate limits protect the node, where several sites each staying under their own limit could\nstill overwhelm it together.\n\nA ManagedServiceFactory over files in karaf/etc, not ConfigurationAdmin. A factory\nconfiguration created through createFactoryConfiguration is bundle-scoped: it lives under\nbundleNN/data/config and is orphaned or dropped when the bundle is reinstalled, or when a\ndefault .cfg later ships for the same factory pid, which loses a site''s configuration on a\nrestart and does it silently. A file survives reinstalls and is what an administrator can\nback up, diff and keep in configuration management. save() writes it through a temp file\nand ATOMIC_MOVE so FileInstall never delivers half a configuration.\n\nThe file name is a convention for humans; the siteKey PROPERTY is what the module trusts,\nand it is validated as one safe path segment before it is interpolated into a file name.\nA key carrying a separator or a .. is refused by both updated() and configFile(), and the\ntests cover ../evil, a/b, .., empty, a key with a space, and a 200-character one.\n\nThe credential rules were extracted rather than duplicated. The subtle one is that a user\nconfigured WITHOUT a usable secret must leave capture anonymous AND must not be claimed as\nthe principal, or a snapshot would name an account that never fetched it. Two\nimplementations of that would eventually disagree.\n\nA disabled site records DISABLED rather than being passed over in silence. The folder''s\ncrh:lastCaptureStatus is what makes a gap self-explaining, and \"someone turned this off\"\nis a different answer from \"the content did not change\" or \"the capture failed\". It is\nchecked before the rate limiter, so a switched-off site is never reported as rate limited.\n\nThe static accessor mirrors CaptureIdentity, because the consumers are a Quartz job and a\nservice the backfill script instantiates reflectively, neither of which DS can inject\ninto. It answers with the defaults when the component is not running, so capture degrades\nrather than throwing on a Quartz thread while configuration is being replaced.\n\n14 tests on the registry, including that a site''s settings never carry the secret into\ntheir own toString -- it ends up in logs.\n\n177 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(config): allow a site to override the capture endpoint\n\nAsked for, on the grounds that the public hostname is specific to a site. It is\nimplemented, with the node-level value as fallback, and the README states plainly why\nalmost no site should use it -- because the value the reasoning leads to is the one that\ncannot work.\n\ncapture.baseUrl addresses THIS NODE''S own HTTP connector. A public host has SEO URL\nrewriting and usually a reverse proxy in front, and those rewrite or refuse the\n/cms/render/... paths capture asks for. The symptom is a flat HTTP 404 on every page of\nthe site, whatever its type, version count, or the rights of the capture principal. That\nis the failure that was reported yesterday and traced to exactly this setting.\n\nTwo things were measured rather than argued, because the reasoning behind the request is\nabout URL correctness and that is checkable:\n\n  - fetching over loopback puts no 127.0.0.1 into a snapshot; site-relative links stay\n    relative\n  - the same page fetched with Host: academypp.jahia.com and without produces\n    BYTE-IDENTICAL output, so the request host does not change what Jahia generates\n\nAn absolute URL does appear in a snapshot when an editor authored one -- and one does, in\nthe fixture used for that measurement, because the fixture author typed it. That is the\nrecord being faithful. The capture endpoint has no bearing on it.\n\nSo the override is accepted rather than refused, and warned about, naming the site. An\nunusual deployment may genuinely need it; the warning exists because the common reason for\nreaching for it is a misunderstanding that costs a day.\n\nThe site key is carried on a ThreadLocal rather than a field. The fetcher is a static\nsingleton and captures run on Quartz worker threads, so a field would let two sites\npublishing at once read each other''s endpoint, and Quartz reuses those threads, so it is\ncleared in a finally.\n\n186 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"0adc4098b3f502e2a439b4a0e0d0311e283a31b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/0adc4098b3f502e2a439b4a0e0d0311e283a31b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 0adc4098b3f502e2a439b4a0e0d0311e283a31b0\nparent 51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788168852 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788168852 +0200\n\nfeat(config): per-site capture settings, as file-backed OSGi factory configuration (#79)\n\n* feat(config): per-site capture settings, as file-backed OSGi factory configuration\n\nThree settings can now differ per site: whether capture runs at all, how many snapshots\nare kept per page and language, and which principal capture renders as. A site with no\nfile of its own behaves exactly as the module did before, with the module-wide principal\nand a retention of 500. That fallback is the point rather than a convenience: an upgrade\nmust not change what gets captured.\n\nDeliberately NOT per-site, and the README says so rather than leaving it to be discovered:\ncapture.baseUrl addresses this node''s own HTTP connector and a site does not have one, and\nrate limits protect the node, where several sites each staying under their own limit could\nstill overwhelm it together.\n\nA ManagedServiceFactory over files in karaf/etc, not ConfigurationAdmin. A factory\nconfiguration created through createFactoryConfiguration is bundle-scoped: it lives under\nbundleNN/data/config and is orphaned or dropped when the bundle is reinstalled, or when a\ndefault .cfg later ships for the same factory pid, which loses a site''s configuration on a\nrestart and does it silently. A file survives reinstalls and is what an administrator can\nback up, diff and keep in configuration management. save() writes it through a temp file\nand ATOMIC_MOVE so FileInstall never delivers half a configuration.\n\nThe file name is a convention for humans; the siteKey PROPERTY is what the module trusts,\nand it is validated as one safe path segment before it is interpolated into a file name.\nA key carrying a separator or a .. is refused by both updated() and configFile(), and the\ntests cover ../evil, a/b, .., empty, a key with a space, and a 200-character one.\n\nThe credential rules were extracted rather than duplicated. The subtle one is that a user\nconfigured WITHOUT a usable secret must leave capture anonymous AND must not be claimed as\nthe principal, or a snapshot would name an account that never fetched it. Two\nimplementations of that would eventually disagree.\n\nA disabled site records DISABLED rather than being passed over in silence. The folder''s\ncrh:lastCaptureStatus is what makes a gap self-explaining, and \"someone turned this off\"\nis a different answer from \"the content did not change\" or \"the capture failed\". It is\nchecked before the rate limiter, so a switched-off site is never reported as rate limited.\n\nThe static accessor mirrors CaptureIdentity, because the consumers are a Quartz job and a\nservice the backfill script instantiates reflectively, neither of which DS can inject\ninto. It answers with the defaults when the component is not running, so capture degrades\nrather than throwing on a Quartz thread while configuration is being replaced.\n\n14 tests on the registry, including that a site''s settings never carry the secret into\ntheir own toString -- it ends up in logs.\n\n177 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(config): allow a site to override the capture endpoint\n\nAsked for, on the grounds that the public hostname is specific to a site. It is\nimplemented, with the node-level value as fallback, and the README states plainly why\nalmost no site should use it -- because the value the reasoning leads to is the one that\ncannot work.\n\ncapture.baseUrl addresses THIS NODE''S own HTTP connector. A public host has SEO URL\nrewriting and usually a reverse proxy in front, and those rewrite or refuse the\n/cms/render/... paths capture asks for. The symptom is a flat HTTP 404 on every page of\nthe site, whatever its type, version count, or the rights of the capture principal. That\nis the failure that was reported yesterday and traced to exactly this setting.\n\nTwo things were measured rather than argued, because the reasoning behind the request is\nabout URL correctness and that is checkable:\n\n  - fetching over loopback puts no 127.0.0.1 into a snapshot; site-relative links stay\n    relative\n  - the same page fetched with Host: academypp.jahia.com and without produces\n    BYTE-IDENTICAL output, so the request host does not change what Jahia generates\n\nAn absolute URL does appear in a snapshot when an editor authored one -- and one does, in\nthe fixture used for that measurement, because the fixture author typed it. That is the\nrecord being faithful. The capture endpoint has no bearing on it.\n\nSo the override is accepted rather than refused, and warned about, naming the site. An\nunusual deployment may genuinely need it; the warning exists because the common reason for\nreaching for it is a misunderstanding that costs a day.\n\nThe site key is carried on a ThreadLocal rather than a field. The fetcher is a static\nsingleton and captures run on Quartz worker threads, so a field would let two sites\npublishing at once read each other''s endpoint, and Quartz reuses those threads, so it is\ncleared in a finally.\n\n186 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUqUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtxAQAK+BBMZrTAiUD6JOAmFnK7aJ\nZBOJQF0aX7YylglEQf7B/gdGOKE0xe0XWkbmZJe7in+SXOHERNwO1bkKf44Kxu3h\n0+PC6dr7p8ViNydXIMxFtuMZLk8JvSOxe+gJ64xfKYgwfPl1j8ocf0AAjX9W8dj7\nZvkP4nRcdh6iDLeajgIl/+Z24jLzy9z+cFv0yd7SEVFN9BTT79ABcmpkPBF4eZ6z\nvD3l2SC9nDpnLYAJttbwNV/V9hCC4rEEPBmVsA5a7Jb6rHapeOwo227bqyC6strE\naQozCxCQ6V9pPhcqM9l21xZgQ96zNrKXBpGsCuwyewWQrba+8GYwkbtqnGyz+1Z+\nAsyTFjuQLkhhZ00yo/LNOTUwpURidM+Jy4foAPCZU62rhGyIgi0RvTF7VF5S1peP\nMl+MANqMODcbY2L93TkgOQOo3yE/STj+IK2eityXj7aO0GHZAien99kANE3F3LA/\nskp4+6sVr9ET3pOCp62oXnq1kyh9TwPnexz6tapLNVcExx/GDq18l69ET4R6tfLm\nllHt7JZdIE+k4M+S1EhM+VYCrfTySHIlfk+qy61P9RIHgteYW5YEsqxgXsjaz0Ez\nwSBCw2ayRJPbL2vTSJon4JkIhqXZkf6XfzJQnwFOp+RLfaMriXMHg65k2buNiQkx\nfG7TKVtbIQuudmZzlx2T\n=rIaZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDU3NDJlOGU5ZTRhOTczMmNkODlmNTAyYTVhZDJlNDBhOTQzM2JlM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9","sha":"51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9"}],"sha":"5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/5742e8e9e4a9732cd89f502a5ad2e40a9433be3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:32:15Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:32:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(config): move the capture endpoint from a system property to OSGi configuration (#78)\n\njahia.crh.captureBaseUrl was the only setting in this module that lived outside the\nmodule''s own configuration. A system property is set on the JVM command line, so it needs\na restart to change, it is visible to anyone who can list processes, and it cannot be\nmanaged per environment the way a file can. It was also a surprise for anyone who went\nlooking in the obvious place first.\n\ncapture.baseUrl now lives in org.jahia.modules.revisionhistory.cfg beside the capture\nprincipal, so configuring capture means editing one file. CaptureEndpoint shares\nCaptureIdentity''s pid on purpose: Declarative Services delivers the same configuration to\nevery component that names it.\n\nThe value is resolved per call rather than captured at construction. That detail is the\npoint of the change: the fetcher is a static singleton, so anything read in its\nconstructor would be fixed for the life of the JVM, which is the restart requirement the\nmove was supposed to remove. The DETECTED fallback is still computed once, in a holder\nclass -- it sweeps JMX and its answer cannot change while the JVM runs.\n\nA non-loopback value is accepted, not refused: a container whose HTTP connector genuinely\nis not on loopback is unusual but real, and refusing it would break a working deployment.\nIt warns instead, and now at configuration time as well as at fetch time. At fetch time\nthe warning arrives with the first FAILED capture, which may be a publication away; at\nconfiguration time it arrives while the operator is still looking at the file they saved.\n\nVerified on a running instance, twice, with no restart:\n\n  09:07:45  INFO  Capture renders will be addressed to http://127.0.0.1:8080 (capture.baseUrl)\n  09:09:02  INFO  Capture renders will be addressed to https://academypp.jahia.com\n  09:09:02  WARN  capture.baseUrl is https://academypp.jahia.com, which is not this node''s\n                  own connector ... every capture will report FAILED on a flat HTTP 404\n\nFelix FileInstall delivered each edit to @Modified in about ten seconds.\n\nSix tests on the component, and the shipped default configuration documents the key, when\nit is needed, and that it must never be the site''s public address.\n\n169 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d760fe6edc27fdbb6054c8d434ae2480776ab9fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/d760fe6edc27fdbb6054c8d434ae2480776ab9fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9","verification":{"payload":"tree d760fe6edc27fdbb6054c8d434ae2480776ab9fa\nparent 3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788168735 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788168735 +0200\n\nfeat(config): move the capture endpoint from a system property to OSGi configuration (#78)\n\njahia.crh.captureBaseUrl was the only setting in this module that lived outside the\nmodule''s own configuration. A system property is set on the JVM command line, so it needs\na restart to change, it is visible to anyone who can list processes, and it cannot be\nmanaged per environment the way a file can. It was also a surprise for anyone who went\nlooking in the obvious place first.\n\ncapture.baseUrl now lives in org.jahia.modules.revisionhistory.cfg beside the capture\nprincipal, so configuring capture means editing one file. CaptureEndpoint shares\nCaptureIdentity''s pid on purpose: Declarative Services delivers the same configuration to\nevery component that names it.\n\nThe value is resolved per call rather than captured at construction. That detail is the\npoint of the change: the fetcher is a static singleton, so anything read in its\nconstructor would be fixed for the life of the JVM, which is the restart requirement the\nmove was supposed to remove. The DETECTED fallback is still computed once, in a holder\nclass -- it sweeps JMX and its answer cannot change while the JVM runs.\n\nA non-loopback value is accepted, not refused: a container whose HTTP connector genuinely\nis not on loopback is unusual but real, and refusing it would break a working deployment.\nIt warns instead, and now at configuration time as well as at fetch time. At fetch time\nthe warning arrives with the first FAILED capture, which may be a publication away; at\nconfiguration time it arrives while the operator is still looking at the file they saved.\n\nVerified on a running instance, twice, with no restart:\n\n  09:07:45  INFO  Capture renders will be addressed to http://127.0.0.1:8080 (capture.baseUrl)\n  09:09:02  INFO  Capture renders will be addressed to https://academypp.jahia.com\n  09:09:02  WARN  capture.baseUrl is https://academypp.jahia.com, which is not this node''s\n                  own connector ... every capture will report FAILED on a flat HTTP 404\n\nFelix FileInstall delivered each edit to @Modified in about ten seconds.\n\nSix tests on the component, and the shipped default configuration documents the key, when\nit is needed, and that it must never be the site''s public address.\n\n169 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUofCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACtoQAAHGmU6bLHsQ2C9AV/rAHFA0\nzFMYmvseleLZZ0vvA677+rIwuW/edT+hy4A4xIv3fIWuqfQ0+RIL9YEEC7r+79qP\nu0y8o4jl8QB8OVkxRVVJTJLkDC8OIZSyKnDWk4Gn6CMCgWA/aaI50c6lUFKozFZV\n4QDfYpFSY0+/dZQv1sMog6f55b44mQ2Com+XNK4u7Im43ld45R22e1LOokmyR0gl\nV3krgVZNM8n9JHZhkDUCHEKWrEaUBPFJ6voeqdiZ/lHMib69Ji2I3HmKgIJ8mFv7\n20n9NcroG6Znl3Nf9u9RPKafxbYjY3lbNL5WbvsHhWSjErDAsNvp6CzaFEWO/LwY\nBgWoRVr+xdV4u8bG8X+D+reTt0/VR/OePtF5mzHvDurS+FD4JPxhsUo6hN9EBZv2\n2S6uO2XHYDEwzA1IE2eoLWxljV0jKSSa+p9v0yETGTWC4doroI9s1D/IJfqQgLdy\nQz1L8BEGwCJq5/DYSuymIrNARLjyf/6Avhp4YlBGj7jwLTvfZBvOW599XuFdyW8H\nWmDIi4SiQr2EMq89VzpH/rgOPF648fEoxtx/ogDxYBT6YyWb7Yj6QCU7sEovqJVe\n/U9YjpV23cLnh4wLR37v/1CuVsLfAlGdHb0UUj2BZrk51X4IXNpJzlV0cQXbEQ1S\njyaW+IY+jzhLQ0+EKeQR\n=1YCR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDUxZDI2ZWE2NzNlOWNhMWI1NjJlNzk2YzAyMjQ1ZTY5YmQ3ZTA0Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd","sha":"3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd"}],"sha":"51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/51d26ea673e9ca1b562e796c02245e69bd7e04b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:32:11Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:32:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(capture): do not mistake the AJP connector for the HTTP one (#77)\n\nReported from a real instance:\n\n  Guest capture render failed for http://127.0.0.1:8009/cms/render/live/en/sites/academy/...\n  java.net.SocketException: Unexpected end of file from server\n  No snapshot for page ... [en]: FAILED\n\n8009 is Tomcat''s AJP port, and that SocketException is what speaking HTTP at an AJP\nconnector sounds like.\n\nThe connector sweep matched on the scheme alone, and Tomcat''s AJP connector reports\nscheme=\"http\" -- the attribute describes how a request APPEARS to the application, not\nthe wire protocol. queryNames returns a Set with unspecified enumeration order, so\nwhether a container captured at all came down to which connector JMX happened to list\nfirst. Every capture failed on the instances where AJP came first, and none on the\nothers, which is why this survived: it is not reproducible by reading the code.\n\nspeaksAjp now also reads the protocol attribute and rejects the connector when it\nmentions ajp. Matched loosely because containers report either a protocol string\n(AJP/1.3) or an implementation class (org.apache.coyote.ajp.AjpNioProtocol).\n\nAn unreadable or absent protocol counts as NOT AJP. Rejecting on a missing attribute\nwould break containers that do not expose it, which is a worse failure than the one\nbeing fixed: it would take out deployments that work today. That choice is pinned by a\ntest, and mutating it to the opposite fails that test alone.\n\nAn AJP-only container is now reported as such in the operator message, rather than as\nhaving no connector, so the diagnosis names what was actually found.\n\nFour tests. Both mutations of the rule are killed:\n  removing the AJP check entirely   -> 3 failures\n  unreadable protocol treated as AJP -> 1 failure, on the guard for working deployments\n\n167 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2686b347052c7b03ed1d1bef63e992ed534d9336","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/2686b347052c7b03ed1d1bef63e992ed534d9336"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd","verification":{"payload":"tree 2686b347052c7b03ed1d1bef63e992ed534d9336\nparent 8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788168731 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788168731 +0200\n\nfix(capture): do not mistake the AJP connector for the HTTP one (#77)\n\nReported from a real instance:\n\n  Guest capture render failed for http://127.0.0.1:8009/cms/render/live/en/sites/academy/...\n  java.net.SocketException: Unexpected end of file from server\n  No snapshot for page ... [en]: FAILED\n\n8009 is Tomcat''s AJP port, and that SocketException is what speaking HTTP at an AJP\nconnector sounds like.\n\nThe connector sweep matched on the scheme alone, and Tomcat''s AJP connector reports\nscheme=\"http\" -- the attribute describes how a request APPEARS to the application, not\nthe wire protocol. queryNames returns a Set with unspecified enumeration order, so\nwhether a container captured at all came down to which connector JMX happened to list\nfirst. Every capture failed on the instances where AJP came first, and none on the\nothers, which is why this survived: it is not reproducible by reading the code.\n\nspeaksAjp now also reads the protocol attribute and rejects the connector when it\nmentions ajp. Matched loosely because containers report either a protocol string\n(AJP/1.3) or an implementation class (org.apache.coyote.ajp.AjpNioProtocol).\n\nAn unreadable or absent protocol counts as NOT AJP. Rejecting on a missing attribute\nwould break containers that do not expose it, which is a worse failure than the one\nbeing fixed: it would take out deployments that work today. That choice is pinned by a\ntest, and mutating it to the opposite fails that test alone.\n\nAn AJP-only container is now reported as such in the operator message, rather than as\nhaving no connector, so the diagnosis names what was actually found.\n\nFour tests. Both mutations of the rule are killed:\n  removing the AJP check entirely   -> 3 failures\n  unreadable protocol treated as AJP -> 1 failure, on the guard for working deployments\n\n167 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUobCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqUgQACnPGnKf139htUomBdBIlHEl\nIVTmVq/vq8EWppn9O7v6tG+JnIWxukhvS0EhlD3sUnjJdoPPXU0cCZv6A8p12Wty\nvDW1Cmk2bXj7k0zKV8Fm+fvIVUiHgPgvXX7MT87IG82zYGnYgUQ2xDswuBW2nm6F\nMPTWRu4D4DiVY/2YkyQyzzv7We0VB9L1o9SZHlmOPEdPzKlpRYm202s9PIIWiVdN\nklhMfiDChH/S7cB2CYBlkivqNWNg8iCTZ6/vBiuVmWBeTMLc/8NWFO2FL6Qxd98I\nAVBM9KxOeC21ucCLO3C4v81gvoc7Phb6gER273b9G6fSCSBwzi/Lmz52PzA628r6\nX2cQZrW6I+MaKlQwXdspmClZfz3Q1yaoGfO/ShUPsP7Np+Map1iC2FmZ3IXnvNH1\nU0qyvGtlpDMwQruR/lVGAcBOX+7n0z21h76bef2Hw64mlnHAPDYM/ye29PQvNHkP\nl3Xdb+2Gs/9KudmhvB5JZyEUcgXmzP7TNs6lSpK+l4S+jMPYEfNc6kUseEuF5RLv\nunY7ZwmMBtUQqvEIwL4+nkMXh+udusjiu6i4wGq0NaD4MgiG5h/zgmg12zAYzRsh\nCu7NDX0YbMqIV2+h/cHzZYQWcZ5v+02hN12kpnABn0rufiktamTsFUuDTgawkh9p\nYh/P0IUvuh3sF/aoYD8p\n=pTLC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDNlYjYxMzM4NGMzMmEzZGJlZWZiN2VmY2MzZDUzMTUwYjI1YmRmZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c","sha":"8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c"}],"sha":"3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/3eb613384c32a3dbeefb7efcc3d53150b25bdffd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:46:47Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:46:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cnd): keep system-written snapshot fields out of the edit form (#76)\n\nAsked whether \"Page content as captured\" should be a textarea. It should not be in the\nform at all, and asking the edit engine what it actually renders showed why. Measured\nwith forms.editForm on a real snapshot:\n\n  crh:markdown       BINARY         selector=Text   readOnly=False  Page content as captured\n  crh:contentHash    STRING         selector=Text   readOnly=False  Content hash\n  crh:capturedBy     STRING         selector=Text   readOnly=False  Captured as\n  crh:snapshotDate   DATE           selector=DateTimePicker readOnly=False  Captured\n  crh:entryRefs      WEAKREFERENCE  selector=Picker readOnly=False  Revisions using this snapshot\n\nA single-line text input for a document that may be a megabyte, next to an editable\ncontent hash. Every field of an append-only evidentiary record was editable by hand,\nwhich became reachable when 1.3.1 made the store browsable and 1.3.1 also stopped\nbreaking ACL inheritance.\n\nA textarea would have made that more comfortable rather than less, and it is not even\nreachable: BINARY gets selectorType Text from the platform whatever the label. A real\ntextarea would mean (string, textarea), which would drag up to a megabyte into every\nmetadata read -- the snapshot picker deliberately reads a bounded 512-byte prefix --\nmove the payload out of the datastore into the workspace bundle, and invalidate every\nexisting binary value.\n\nSo all fifteen system-written properties on crh:revisionSnapshot and crh:snapshotFolder\nare now `hidden`. That is the platform''s own answer for a property that code sets and\nusers must not: j:published and j:workInProgress use it. `protected` is deliberately NOT\nused, because it would refuse this module''s own writes.\n\nNothing is lost. Verified on a running instance after deploying:\n  - crh:* fields offered in the snapshot edit form : NONE (was 8)\n  - snapshot preview still HTTP 200 and still shows Captured, Generator version,\n    Content hash and the captured text itself\n  - the authoring form for crh:revisionEntry is untouched, and crh:snapshotRef is still\n    offered as a Choicelist -- it is the one field an editor is meant to set\n\n163 unit tests pass. Full e2e suite 72 of 72.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"a55e42af80c96bdc15417e4e23ad0e708db8d409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/a55e42af80c96bdc15417e4e23ad0e708db8d409"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c","verification":{"payload":"tree a55e42af80c96bdc15417e4e23ad0e708db8d409\nparent 6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788166007 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788166007 +0200\n\nfix(cnd): keep system-written snapshot fields out of the edit form (#76)\n\nAsked whether \"Page content as captured\" should be a textarea. It should not be in the\nform at all, and asking the edit engine what it actually renders showed why. Measured\nwith forms.editForm on a real snapshot:\n\n  crh:markdown       BINARY         selector=Text   readOnly=False  Page content as captured\n  crh:contentHash    STRING         selector=Text   readOnly=False  Content hash\n  crh:capturedBy     STRING         selector=Text   readOnly=False  Captured as\n  crh:snapshotDate   DATE           selector=DateTimePicker readOnly=False  Captured\n  crh:entryRefs      WEAKREFERENCE  selector=Picker readOnly=False  Revisions using this snapshot\n\nA single-line text input for a document that may be a megabyte, next to an editable\ncontent hash. Every field of an append-only evidentiary record was editable by hand,\nwhich became reachable when 1.3.1 made the store browsable and 1.3.1 also stopped\nbreaking ACL inheritance.\n\nA textarea would have made that more comfortable rather than less, and it is not even\nreachable: BINARY gets selectorType Text from the platform whatever the label. A real\ntextarea would mean (string, textarea), which would drag up to a megabyte into every\nmetadata read -- the snapshot picker deliberately reads a bounded 512-byte prefix --\nmove the payload out of the datastore into the workspace bundle, and invalidate every\nexisting binary value.\n\nSo all fifteen system-written properties on crh:revisionSnapshot and crh:snapshotFolder\nare now `hidden`. That is the platform''s own answer for a property that code sets and\nusers must not: j:published and j:workInProgress use it. `protected` is deliberately NOT\nused, because it would refuse this module''s own writes.\n\nNothing is lost. Verified on a running instance after deploying:\n  - crh:* fields offered in the snapshot edit form : NONE (was 8)\n  - snapshot preview still HTTP 200 and still shows Captured, Generator version,\n    Content hash and the captured text itself\n  - the authoring form for crh:revisionEntry is untouched, and crh:snapshotRef is still\n    offered as a Choicelist -- it is the one field an editor is meant to set\n\n163 unit tests pass. Full e2e suite 72 of 72.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlT93CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQlcQAEftPV6SzSbwghlkZLZecwE8\nV8HVaAzkkiWDj+jvqQzMy45RXTbpvXOasD58KoHf2KY+1i/tf3cECVXdZE7HtAQE\nS60p0jwZ3U4jvYIE3gZapmF7KdK+VbdmE3r+53ynxskG4ZRkPSUMGlg84CZyf6dC\nDX6f2NJN2IS4QarkpKiUF6DoFlso8IRZZlRKTdTVZRUs9wm07+CBsXOSU3jGtHXo\nUrR5FGBtqdsDDK9ke8CvSzGfcvwarN38ea7HSBtzm1/1UZ7LfVNhZm5QpJrkBIOF\nWd6FnvTMCMWEn7Y3aToPNW8RJ6be6jXGQApw3VgIkiQgDzlumtucFMVurY7136Gg\nlX+MExX6urwe8i8qzYrdislGoz2yhdf46bKp0BCgiEZNegAq9k+HCfX9DKfN+KbU\nYDvsGRX3JORkR7mMpDcEUvbqmh+mRiaKJf7FHfrRENSEwdyp0/ROqEQ8bJ8DZxgm\nB2luG2F/+0TmnSjXFzGFwFsFdzKx408DlTAhpcV/8wtuRYqK1rEP5sl4R8oM4WDT\nfjVr3OrK+E3XRPkk2FAqy/x7SIm44MzsEO6LmctBPcjokeatprE132SbiGD999m3\n0lnrOB4oorwqSrvKAs35XiiLqeruwK8NMcnii2OdlcfBopY7AMkNuiagw5Gp5yqI\nFYWULyPGojYiqp7+zwSm\n=tITF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDhkZjBkMDJjMDI3ZTBhN2MwZDU3NzU4NzhmNmFhODE4ZmI4YmYxMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42","sha":"6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42"}],"sha":"8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/8df0d02c027e0a7c0d5775878f6aa818fb8bf10c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:04:24Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:04:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): cover a revisioned page that also has vanity URLs (#75)\n\n* test(e2e): cover a revisioned page that also has vanity URLs\n\nThis combination broke the backfill twice and had no coverage either time. The first\nbreak was fixed in #62 and verified with a one-off Groovy probe, because end-to-end\nverification was blocked at the time by the frozen-node render bug. That bug was fixed\nin #63 and nobody came back. Nothing in the suite would catch a regression today.\n\nAdding a vanity URL to a page produces exactly the shape that bit us. Measured, not\nassumed:\n\n  vanityUrlMapping        jnt:vanityUrls    <- name does NOT start with j:\n      ''probe vanity path'' jnt:vanityUrl     <- name carries the URL''s slashes as SPACES\n\nBoth properties matter. The name-based filter the walk relied on does not exclude\n`vanityUrlMapping`, so it descended into it and asked Jahia to render a vanity URL, which\nanswers 401 with a message blaming the credentials. The child name''s spaces produced a\nrequest curl cannot even form -- it returns 000 -- which is why path segments are now\npercent-encoded. Both types extend nt:base rather than jnt:content, which is what the\nscript filters on instead.\n\nFive tests: the page is still captured at all; the snapshot holds the page content and\nneither the vanity URL nor the mapping node; the mapping is a child whose name does not\nstart with j:; it is not jnt:content; and the vanity node is named after the URL, spaces\nincluded.\n\nThe content assertion is the load-bearing one, and it turns out to be less theoretical\nthan it looks. jnt_page/markdown iterates children with the SAME name-based filter the\nscript used to, so it hands vanityUrlMapping to template:module on every capture. It\nrenders nothing only because jnt:vanityUrls has no markdown view -- the record stays\nclean by luck rather than by design. If that ever changes, this test says so.\n\nThe rest are structural assertions about how Jahia stores a vanity URL. The backfill\nscript runs in the Groovy console and is out of reach from Cypress, so what is pinned is\nthe shape it has to cope with: if an upgrade changes that storage, this fails and the\nscript gets revisited.\n\nFull e2e suite 72 of 72, up from 67.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(capture): warn when the capture base URL is not this node''s own connector\n\nAsked whether a public hostname still 404s. It does, and it has nothing to do with\nvanity URLs: SEO rewriting refuses /cms/render/... for every node, whatever its type,\nversion count, or the rights of the account. Vanity URLs were a real backfill bug (#62,\nthe 401) but never the cause of the 404s. The two only looked related because both\nsurfaced on the same page.\n\nThat answer exposed the same trap one layer down. The backfill script now warns about a\nnon-loopback BASE_URL (#74), but capture has its own address and no such check.\nSYSPROP_CAPTURE_BASE_URL is an escape hatch that accepts anything, and its javadoc even\nsuggests a URL-shaped value, so a deployment can point it at the public site. Every\ncapture then gets a flat 404, which statusForHttp maps to FAILED, and nothing anywhere\nmentions the address.\n\nreachesJahiaDirectly is the rule, and it is deliberately narrow. Only a loopback host\nreaches Jahia without passing through whatever serves the public site. It is matched on\nthe host alone and ANCHORED: localhost.example.com resolves wherever its DNS says, which\nis not this machine, so a prefix match would be wrong. A blank value is accepted, because\nresolveBaseUrl consults this only when an override is set and the derived default is\nalways loopback -- warning on every start would be noise.\n\nThe default path is untouched: the port is still read from the container''s MBean and the\nhost is still 127.0.0.1.\n\nFour tests, and both mutations of the rule are killed:\n  accepting any host                 -> 2 failures\n  find() instead of matches()        -> 1 failure, on localhost.example.com specifically\n\nThat second one is the point of the anchor, and it is the kind of thing that passes review\nby inspection while being wrong.\n\n163 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ab8885ed868fa046bce2b062d5c176cf9ce1df3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/7ab8885ed868fa046bce2b062d5c176cf9ce1df3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42","verification":{"payload":"tree 7ab8885ed868fa046bce2b062d5c176cf9ce1df3\nparent 6e3ea0ccf1f5990f96320dba930f523af6e692a6\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788163464 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788163464 +0200\n\ntest(e2e): cover a revisioned page that also has vanity URLs (#75)\n\n* test(e2e): cover a revisioned page that also has vanity URLs\n\nThis combination broke the backfill twice and had no coverage either time. The first\nbreak was fixed in #62 and verified with a one-off Groovy probe, because end-to-end\nverification was blocked at the time by the frozen-node render bug. That bug was fixed\nin #63 and nobody came back. Nothing in the suite would catch a regression today.\n\nAdding a vanity URL to a page produces exactly the shape that bit us. Measured, not\nassumed:\n\n  vanityUrlMapping        jnt:vanityUrls    <- name does NOT start with j:\n      ''probe vanity path'' jnt:vanityUrl     <- name carries the URL''s slashes as SPACES\n\nBoth properties matter. The name-based filter the walk relied on does not exclude\n`vanityUrlMapping`, so it descended into it and asked Jahia to render a vanity URL, which\nanswers 401 with a message blaming the credentials. The child name''s spaces produced a\nrequest curl cannot even form -- it returns 000 -- which is why path segments are now\npercent-encoded. Both types extend nt:base rather than jnt:content, which is what the\nscript filters on instead.\n\nFive tests: the page is still captured at all; the snapshot holds the page content and\nneither the vanity URL nor the mapping node; the mapping is a child whose name does not\nstart with j:; it is not jnt:content; and the vanity node is named after the URL, spaces\nincluded.\n\nThe content assertion is the load-bearing one, and it turns out to be less theoretical\nthan it looks. jnt_page/markdown iterates children with the SAME name-based filter the\nscript used to, so it hands vanityUrlMapping to template:module on every capture. It\nrenders nothing only because jnt:vanityUrls has no markdown view -- the record stays\nclean by luck rather than by design. If that ever changes, this test says so.\n\nThe rest are structural assertions about how Jahia stores a vanity URL. The backfill\nscript runs in the Groovy console and is out of reach from Cypress, so what is pinned is\nthe shape it has to cope with: if an upgrade changes that storage, this fails and the\nscript gets revisited.\n\nFull e2e suite 72 of 72, up from 67.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(capture): warn when the capture base URL is not this node''s own connector\n\nAsked whether a public hostname still 404s. It does, and it has nothing to do with\nvanity URLs: SEO rewriting refuses /cms/render/... for every node, whatever its type,\nversion count, or the rights of the account. Vanity URLs were a real backfill bug (#62,\nthe 401) but never the cause of the 404s. The two only looked related because both\nsurfaced on the same page.\n\nThat answer exposed the same trap one layer down. The backfill script now warns about a\nnon-loopback BASE_URL (#74), but capture has its own address and no such check.\nSYSPROP_CAPTURE_BASE_URL is an escape hatch that accepts anything, and its javadoc even\nsuggests a URL-shaped value, so a deployment can point it at the public site. Every\ncapture then gets a flat 404, which statusForHttp maps to FAILED, and nothing anywhere\nmentions the address.\n\nreachesJahiaDirectly is the rule, and it is deliberately narrow. Only a loopback host\nreaches Jahia without passing through whatever serves the public site. It is matched on\nthe host alone and ANCHORED: localhost.example.com resolves wherever its DNS says, which\nis not this machine, so a prefix match would be wrong. A blank value is accepted, because\nresolveBaseUrl consults this only when an override is set and the derived default is\nalways loopback -- warning on every start would be noise.\n\nThe default path is untouched: the port is still read from the container''s MBean and the\nhost is still 127.0.0.1.\n\nFour tests, and both mutations of the rule are killed:\n  accepting any host                 -> 2 failures\n  find() instead of matches()        -> 1 failure, on localhost.example.com specifically\n\nThat second one is the point of the anchor, and it is the kind of thing that passes review\nby inspection while being wrong.\n\n163 unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlTWICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN8gQAGFKokEswHe+nXBvUT26WzBn\niBfx/wpS9YtFmGExRyXchWgnmu3h05n//nvKGW+kbBYKp7VYm8JIywiQjJJH9hmk\ni2RoWNjaGz16x0gAPabe+/RnpNwn9mQ3UUeu9HwHp6akl0TQTQjaaWsMrBz8gsin\nRZP/LwTGuhf1w1PiPsCl7uRoYLQXPZ2rK9gEJf2lFYN37pMEtIvY6SMjsK/gaGZj\nNKU4+bUoo13wavBIOSERa+1c0GWDI+uQq8NyREo6vgAD8eQNNKevKM6JutW6Xupi\nzzaoA455UZDZIblJrBLkIDl2NqkvWFwq6d76cUyFDz4NupRYVD2BTS0Y/UV1RopD\nSnvoOYMM5cm7v8YP245XM5tspSbB/T5j+0guL2jTmggmQrrG4rSacFxgfSbr6d1b\nxOEvvDho4o7g3yJu+8DRAluexhjaxe4kIcqYBGsHNMTAIARUt8wWuVZyGs9DIlU2\nKTndB8QVFMEAH8FPI6z3zzjJE3Qu75/xGDTa/wK57zLUSPDK34RiNo+TgNO7xhrP\n/9ggOTxHYq6/0DMHQpmYPXSbtumk/873kJ6n3dMrbftj7BlshmmdwBWkCejF5d7R\nEmi/QNlUri333kyHX0OZc59HvC1gfSEQ06ae8iLdizWWfzn5PX5N2SsBfi/Ns0JB\niOmypp8wNFWDPiAjGaig\n=bgZe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42","node_id":"C_kwDOUKfvOdoAKDY0NzJlZDM1NDJmZmExZGJhYjM3NGNmNTk3OWM5MTYyYjE5YWJkNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/content-revision-history/commit/6e3ea0ccf1f5990f96320dba930f523af6e692a6","sha":"6e3ea0ccf1f5990f96320dba930f523af6e692a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6e3ea0ccf1f5990f96320dba930f523af6e692a6"}],"sha":"6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6472ed3542ffa1dbab374cf5979c9162b19abd42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/commits/6e3ea0ccf1f5990f96320dba930f523af6e692a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:20:12Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T07:20:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(backfill): never render a node that was not on the published page at that instant (#74)\n\n* fix(backfill): never render a node that was not on the published page at that instant\n\nReported:\n\n  Render of .../jsa-2026-0013/document-area/github-content at 1786972166934 returned\n  HTTP 404. Refusing to continue: a partial reconstruction would be stored as evidence.\n\nDiagnosed on the reporting instance. The node is a jnt:bigText, mix:versionable, and\nhas ZERO versions -- it was never published. It also 404s at HEAD, not only at the\npinned instant, so this was never about version resolution.\n\ncompose walks the CURRENT subtree, because setVersionDate on a system session does not\nproduce frozen wrappers and there is no historical tree to walk, then renders each child\nat the instant. A node that was never published has no state at any past instant, and\nasking Jahia for one answers 404.\n\nThe gate is existedAt: a versionable node is rendered only if it has a checkpoint at or\nbefore the instant. An empty history therefore never renders, which is exactly the\nreported case. A node with no version history at all -- not versionable -- still renders,\nbecause a pinned session resolves it to its current state rather than refusing.\n\nexistedAt gates FETCHING and never recursion, and that distinction is the whole of the\nfix. The first version of this change applied it to the walk as well, which was wrong in\na way worth recording: containers are routinely versionable with an EMPTY history.\nMeasured on a real page, both the jnt:contentList area and the page itself had zero\ncheckpoints while their children had two each, so gating the walk skipped every container\nand reconstructed pages as nothing but their title. Verified before shipping, on the same\npage, same instants:\n\n  master        2 checked, 0 exact, 2 unexplained\n  first attempt 2 checked, 0 exact, 2 unexplained   (rebuilt only \"# Late addition demo\")\n  this change   2 checked, 2 exact, 0 unexplained\n\nThe last row is a second defect fixed by the same gate. master''s reconstruction included\na never-published draft in snapshots of the past, which is why its validation could not\nexplain the difference: it was comparing captured history against a rebuild containing\ncontent that had never been on the page.\n\nThe comment added in #63 claimed nodes added since the instant were \"handled\" by\nunresolvableAt. They were not. That predicate declines to judge them and compose went on\nto render them, which is how this reached a user.\n\nA 404 now carries a message saying what it usually means, since with this gate in place\nit should no longer be reachable for that reason.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(backfill): say when BASE_URL is the public host, which 404s every render\n\nReported as a 404 on one node. The evidence gathered since says the node was never the\nproblem:\n\n  default  live     node\n  404      404      <the page>\n  404      200      /document-area\n  404      404      /document-area/github-content\n\nA node with four versions 404s. An account with extended rights 404s. The PAGE 404s in\nlive, which is the exact URL live capture uses, so capture could never have worked there\neither. None of that is explained by the node, its history, or permissions.\n\nBASE_URL was set to the site''s public address. A public host has SEO URL rewriting\n(urlRewriteSeoRulesEnabled, urlRewriteRemoveCmsPrefix) and usually a reverse proxy, and\nthose rewrite or refuse the /cms/render/... paths this script asks for. Confirmed from\nthe other side by the reporter: the public .html URL renders and then redirects to a\nvanity URL, so rewriting is certainly active on that host.\n\nThe setting always meant the node''s own connector -- its default is\nhttp://127.0.0.1:8080 and its comment said \"this node''s own HTTP connector\" -- but\nnothing enforced or explained it, and the failure it produces looks exactly like a broken\nnode.\n\nSo the script now warns before doing any work when BASE_URL is not a loopback address,\nand a 404 says to compare the same URL against http://127.0.0.1:8080 before suspecting\nthe node. The failure message also carries the exact URL and a ready-to-paste curl, which\nis what the reporter had to ask for.\n\nThis is a hypothesis with strong evidence, not a confirmed fix: the decisive test is\nwhether the same path answers 200 on the loopback connector and 404 on the public host,\nand only the reporter can run it. The warning is worth having either way, because\nBASE_URL is the one setting whose misuse is invisible in the error it produces.\n\nLoopback detection verified to accept http://127.0.0.1:8080, http://localhost:8080 and\nhttp://127.0.0.1, and to reject https://localhost.example.com -- a hostname that merely\nbegins with localhost.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f02f2d5ef0e18b028224c9d09914dd44c2e0194","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/trees/4f02f2d5ef0e18b028224c9d09914dd44c2e0194"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/content-revision-history/git/commits/6e3ea0ccf1f5990f96320dba930f523af6e692a6","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f02f2d5ef0e18b028224c9d09914dd44c2e0194\nparent bccf22ae9aea734fe2bf58038d499164f3ece4dd\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788160812 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788160812 +0200\n\nfix(backfill): never render a node that was not on the published page at that instant (#74)\n\n* fix(backfill): never render a node that was not on the published page at that instant\n\nReported:\n\n  Render of .../jsa-2026-0013/document-area/github-content at 1786972166934 returned\n  HTTP 404. Refusing to continue: a partial reconstruction would be stored as evidence.\n\nDiagnosed on the reporting instance. The node is a jnt:bigText, mix:versionable, and\nhas ZERO versions -- it was never published. It also 404s at HEAD, not only at the\npinned instant, so this was never about version resolution.\n\ncompose walks the CURRENT subtree, because setVersionDate on a system session does not\nproduce frozen wrappers and there is no historical tree to walk, then renders each child\nat the instant. A node that was never published has no state at any past instant, and\nasking Jahia for one answers 404.\n\nThe gate is existedAt: a versionable node is rendered only if it has a checkpoint at or\nbefore the instant. An empty history therefore never renders, which is exactly the\nreported case. A node with no version history at all -- not versionable -- still renders,\nbecause a pinned session resolves it to its current state rather than refusing.\n\nexistedAt gates FETCHING and never recursion, and that distinction is the whole of the\nfix. The first version of this change applied it to the walk as well, which was wrong in\na way worth recording: containers are routinely versionable with an EMPTY history.\nMeasured on a real page, both the jnt:contentList area and the page itself had zero\ncheckpoints while their children had two each, so gating the walk skipped every container\nand reconstructed pages as nothing but their title. Verified before shipping, on the same\npage, same instants:\n\n  master        2 checked, 0 exact, 2 unexplained\n  first attempt 2 checked, 0 exact, 2 unexplained   (rebuilt only \"# Late addition demo\")\n  this change   2 checked, 2 exact, 0 unexplained\n\nThe last row is a second defect fixed by the same gate. master''s reconstruction included\na never-published draft in snapshots of the past, which is why its validation could not\nexplain the difference: it was comparing captured history against a rebuild containing\ncontent that had never been on the page.\n\nThe comment added in #63 claimed nodes added since the instant were \"handled\" by\nunresolvableAt. They were not. That predicate declines to judge them and compose went on\nto render them, which is how this reached a user.\n\nA 404 now carries a message saying what it usually means, since with this gate in place\nit should no longer be reachable for that reason.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(backfill): say when BASE_URL is the public host, which 404s every render\n\nReported as a 404 on one node. The evidence gathered since says the node was never the\nproblem:\n\n  default  live     node\n  404      404      <the page>\n  404      200      /document-area\n  404      404      /document-area/github-content\n\nA node with four versions 404s. An account with extended rights 404s. The PAGE 404s in\nlive, which is the exact URL live capture uses, so capture could never have worked there\neither. None of that is explained by the node, its history, or permissions.\n\nBASE_URL was set to the site''s public address. A public host has SEO URL rewriting\n(urlRewriteSeoRulesEnabled, urlRewriteRemoveCmsPrefix) and usually a reverse proxy, and\nthose rewrite or refuse the /cms/render/... paths this script asks for. Confirmed from\nthe other side by the reporter: the public .html URL renders and then redirects to a\nvanity URL, so rewriting is certainly active on that host.\n\nThe setting always meant the node''s own connector -- its default is\nhttp://127.0.0.1:8080 and its comment said \"this node''s own HTTP connector\" -- but\nnothing enforced or explained it, and the failure it produces looks exactly like a broken\nnode.\n\nSo the script now warns before doing any work when BASE_URL is not a loopback address,\nand a 404 says to compare the same URL against http://127.0.0.1:8080 before suspecting\nthe node. The failure message also carries the exact URL and a ready-to-paste curl, which\nis what the reporter had to ask for.\n\nThis is a hypothesis with strong evidence, not a confirmed fix: the decisive test is\nwhether the same path answers 200 on the loopback connector and 404 on the public host,\nand only the reporter can run it. The warning is worth having either way, because\nBASE_URL is the one setting whose misuse is invisible in the error it produces.\n\nLoopback detection verified to accept http://127.0.0.1:8080, http://localhost:8080 and\nhttp://127.0.0.1, and to reject https://localhost.example.com -- a hostname that merely\nbegins with localhost.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlSssCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYogQADxJOxFbmgHl0z39d1lV5tqr\nYS6f3uSqNXnEyOqUBHIB38450I1aIKDXQF88YmqfONx2DjE/hlfT7DeuxayaCc9E\nemaHH3aIZk5tOaE3I26KqXIiiafOTJQmBriMuvF4VphCOXF3vkL+0E+VSa7528IT\nO2lljpSdiNK2bNMGyykARsGPzZyx/IiVKXEUruqqY8+AQa8XoaHIcCF8NcHPhiaj\n6ojRTabC40WSKXJk77Me4cOx3xNfkiK1p8FX1LfXZ5HfuM9at96aS9P3Su5Kpe4N\nrSCi/3s8u1EZPHAJFkvM2djNMUChy8twU3a1tEgPhJM8u+Hnh34iJhrbBNozYl4A\nvMyrbcSRInUFnSdjMCXAgBD66D0dcByXluMzlrj0SwHFccgrOuozFOhUmP4yxuvh\n37WaDi8cQmH5YxES1iW4KIV1XqUoKPNSG6NqfPyOQyoc4syswalRetuRTpulmwur\npHhlHOrHy0FPNG2PVOFh2blJuaiZSMv1ENS49y4Palt9mBGKGOX8SJvM9R5pIcbX\nwOnJeMX+0MFuJarw6LcEJ5pUyEHWwQ830+22y0mpaJ4daMcBfBbCG2l8d71F4ZtB\nsTHNmNN1npWTdUni3/BKFyfyzp8NeKs6LPbiH4Wc7Z7CJkbIJl1Y3UKxj8cWWDvz\nw352Bova4OsIs8B3bzxH\n=08Hf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T05:51:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19