m/users/anish0714","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anish0714/devpulse-mfe/commits/fcca491ce68c8195fabb748be02671114aef5a76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T02:41:37Z","email":"59595126+anish0714@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anish Dandekar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T02:41:37Z","email":"59595126+anish0714@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anish Dandekar"},"message":"Add OCR remote: extract text from images or scanned PDFs (tesseract.js)\n\nNew ocr-remote (port 3007). Runs real optical character recognition\nclient-side via tesseract.js (WebAssembly), accepting either an image\n(JPG/PNG) or a PDF - each PDF page is rendered with pdfjs-dist and OCR''d\nin turn, with a live \"page X of Y\" progress indicator reusing the same\nrender-to-canvas approach already proven in pdf-manipulation-remote and\npdf-form-filler-remote.\n\nVerified end-to-end: an image generated with known text was OCR''d with\nbyte-for-byte accuracy against the source, and a real multi-field PDF\nwas OCR''d page-by-page with the extracted text aggregated under\n\"--- Page N ---\" headers.\n\nEnglish only for now, and honest about the one exception to the\nzero-backend story: the OCR engine and language data (a few MB)\ndownload from a CDN on first use - a download, not an upload, and\ncached by the browser afterward. No image, PDF, or extracted text is\never uploaded.\n\nWires the new remote into the shell''s sidebar/Introduction and updates\nthe README. Does NOT touch .github/workflows/*.yml (same OAuth\n`workflow` scope limitation as PRs #8 and #9) - this is now the third\nremote pending that follow-up.","tree":{"sha":"520b8dd96944c94e2935654a0f18fd4748d78e9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anish0714/devpulse-mfe/git/trees/520b8dd96944c94e2935654a0f18fd4748d78e9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anish0714/devpulse-mfe/git/commits/fcca491ce68c8195fabb748be02671114aef5a76","verification":{"payload":null,"rea